{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T07:53:21.797Z","ordinal":377816,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17733-2085-7e83-adb4-b52c4424a4d5","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — exact base `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`. Reviewed `cli/src/agent.ts` (SHA-256 `9a5fab337cd42c8c68281ca4c0d6e42966ace72f9a8a64c973405a47d56ed3fa`) and `cli/test/agent_discovered_verifier_premutation.test.ts` (SHA-256 `8f3eef5f0696c4dded8d1caec69938ba7c4acc632ffad6ab76d0c608a18311ae`).\n\nThe pre-mutation capture now covers tools marked workspace-changing, unknown tools, and `spawn_subagent`, while retaining direct file-tool coverage. The regressions exercise both a first `run_command` and a first subagent edit against an initially failing discovered verifier; their final assertions check independent verification and that no unverified changes remain. I found no material behavior regression or scope issue.\n\nThis is source-only review; I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17729-d173-7ea0-aeae-81952db7e099","create_time":1793001201.7974546}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18564}}
