{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:00:24.465Z","ordinal":378130,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17734-064a-7c40-9dfa-d9e4ca640901","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9aebc3b8-c753-4fa9-beee-5963aece6e9d","process_id":"41230","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"OpenRouter|small live task|provider verification|provider.verify|nexus verify\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md | head -100; rg -n \"verify.*provider|provider.*verify|live.*task\" cli/src"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'OpenRouter|small live task|provider verification|provider.verify|nexus verify' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md","query":"OpenRouter|small live task|provider verification|provider.verify|nexus verify","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'verify.*provider|provider.*verify|live.*task' cli/src","query":"verify.*provider|provider.*verify|live.*task","path":"cli"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:23:  - **Sign in with OpenRouter** — OpenRouter's official PKCE flow for apps; it issues a user API key.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:142:(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:165:- Implemented: OpenRouter, OpenAI (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic OpenAI-compatible, ChatGPT plan and\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:291:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:294:| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:342:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\ncli/src/types.ts:93:  /** Workspace-relative deliverable paths declared by the operator before the task starts. */\ncli/src/index.ts:276:// subcommand's own (`nexus providers verify --provider openrouter` reported --provider missing).\ncli/src/provider_cli.ts:129:/** A credential-safe JSON projection for `providers verify --json`; raw provider diagnostics are deliberately omitted. */\ncli/src/provider_cli.ts:186:export async function verifyProvider(\ncli/src/provider_cli.ts:355:      const steps = await verifyProvider(config, abort.signal, { diagnosticHandler });\ncli/src/provider_connect.ts:24:async function verify(base: HarnessConfig, providerId: string, apiKey?: string): Promise<number> {\ncli/src/provider_connect.ts:36:    const count = await verify(base, providerId, value);\ncli/src/provider_connect.ts:62:        const count = await verify(base, providerId);\ncli/src/agent.ts:195:  phase: \"inference\" | \"tool\" | \"approval\" | \"provider_wait\" | \"verifying\" | \"compacting\";\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":94852806}},"started_at_ms":1793001623370,"completed_at_ms":1793001624465}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:00:25.805Z","ordinal":378131,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17739-98cd-7ec2-83a6-94eea696c67d","call_id":"call_a174b14fc8c94b91baa0ac6b759df8f5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:23:  - **Sign in with OpenRouter** — OpenRouter's official PKCE flow for apps; it issues a user API key.\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:142:(OpenRouter); otherwise it is `unknown` — never estimated. `/tokens` and `nexus run` show a cloud usage summary;\ndocs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:165:- Implemented: OpenRouter, OpenAI (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic OpenAI-compatible, ChatGPT plan and\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:291:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:294:| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:342:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\ncli/src/types.ts:93:  /** Workspace-relative deliverable paths declared by the operator before the task starts. */\ncli/src/index.ts:276:// subcommand's own (`nexus providers verify --provider openrouter` reported --provider missing).\ncli/src/provider_cli.ts:129:/** A credential-safe JSON projection for `providers verify --json`; raw provider diagnostics are deliberately omitted. */\ncli/src/provider_cli.ts:186:export async function verifyProvider(\ncli/src/provider_cli.ts:355:      const steps = await verifyProvider(config, abort.signal, { diagnosticHandler });\ncli/src/provider_connect.ts:24:async function verify(base: HarnessConfig, providerId: string, apiKey?: string): Promise<number> {\ncli/src/provider_connect.ts:36:    const count = await verify(base, providerId, value);\ncli/src/provider_connect.ts:62:        const count = await verify(base, providerId);\ncli/src/agent.ts:195:  phase: \"inference\" | \"tool\" | \"approval\" | \"provider_wait\" | \"verifying\" | \"compacting\";\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17734-064a-7c40-9dfa-d9e4ca640901","create_time":1793001625.8052063}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
