{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:00:30.606Z","ordinal":378137,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17734-064a-7c40-9dfa-d9e4ca640901","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-09aaec49-bd1d-4f7a-845a-cccc0e550abd","process_id":"60514","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '140,170p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '120,220p' cli/src/provider_cli.ts; sed -n '260,300p' cli/src/index.ts; sed -n '330,370p' cli/src/provider_cli.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '140,170p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '120,220p' cli/src/provider_cli.ts","name":"provider_cli.ts","path":"cli/src/provider_cli.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '260,300p' cli/src/index.ts","name":"index.ts","path":"cli/src/index.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '330,370p' cli/src/provider_cli.ts","name":"provider_cli.ts","path":"cli/src/provider_cli.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n]);\n\nfunction safeStepDetail(ok: boolean, detail: string): string {\n  if (!ok) return detail === \"Provider request failed\" ? detail : \"Verification failed\";\n  if (/^streamed completion received \\(\\d+ chars\\)$/.test(detail)) return detail;\n  if (/^echo_token tool call completed \\(\\d+ call\\(s\\)\\)$/.test(detail)) return detail;\n  return detail === \"tool result round trip completed\" ? detail : \"Verification succeeded\";\n}\n\n/** A credential-safe JSON projection for `providers verify --json`; raw provider diagnostics are deliberately omitted. */\nexport function verificationSummary(\n  steps: readonly VerificationStep[],\n  receipts: readonly import(\"./usage.js\").InferenceReceipt[],\n  target?: Pick<HarnessConfig, \"provider\" | \"model\">,\n) {\n  const provider = safeProviderId(target?.provider ?? receipts[0]?.providerId);\n  const model = target?.model ?? receipts[0]?.selectedModel;\n  return {\n    passed: steps.length === 3 && steps.every((step) => step.ok),\n    ...(provider ? { provider } : {}),\n    ...(model ? { model: safeModelId(model) } : {}),\n    steps: steps.map(({ step, ok, requestId, detail, failureKind, failureCondition }) => {\n      const safeKind = failureKind && SAFE_FAILURE_KINDS.has(failureKind) ? failureKind : undefined;\n      const safeCondition = failureCondition && SAFE_FAILURE_CONDITIONS.has(failureCondition) ? failureCondition : undefined;\n      return {\n        step, ok, requestId, detail: safeStepDetail(ok, detail),\n        ...(safeKind ? { failureKind: safeKind } : {}),\n        ...(safeCondition ? { condition: safeCondition } : {}),\n      };\n    }),\n    receipts: receipts.map(({ at, requestId, role, providerId, selectedModel, effectiveModel, endpointOrigin, protocol, disclosure, executions, outcome, failureKind, usage, usageConfidence, costConfidence }) => {\n      const origin = safeOriginOf(endpointOrigin);\n      return {\n        at, requestId, role, providerId: safeProviderId(providerId) ?? \"(unrecognized provider)\",\n        selectedModel: safeModelId(selectedModel),\n        ...(effectiveModel ? { effectiveModel: safeModelId(effectiveModel) } : {}),\n        ...(origin ? { endpointOrigin: origin } : {}),\n        protocol, disclosure, ...(executions !== undefined ? { executions } : {}), outcome,\n        ...(failureKind && SAFE_FAILURE_KINDS.has(failureKind) ? { failureKind } : {}), ...(usage ? { usage } : {}), usageConfidence, costConfidence,\n      };\n    }),\n  };\n}\n\nconst ECHO_TOOL: ToolDefinition = {\n  type: \"function\",\n  function: {\n    name: \"echo_token\",\n    description: \"Echo the given token back. Call this exactly once with the token the user gives you.\",\n    parameters: { type: \"object\", properties: { token: { type: \"string\", description: \"The token to echo\" } }, required: [\"token\"] },\n  },\n};\n\nexport interface VerificationStep {\n  step: string;\n  ok: boolean;\n  detail: string;\n  requestId: string;\n  failureKind?: string;\n  failureCondition?: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * Live qualification without workspace content: a streamed completion, then a tool round trip (the model must call\n * echo_token with a nonce, receive its result and answer). Each step is one receipt in the usage ledger.\n */\nexport async function verifyProvider(\n  config: HarnessConfig,\n  signal?: AbortSignal,\n  options?: { diagnosticHandler?: (level: \"error\" | \"warn\", message: string) => void },\n): Promise<VerificationStep[]> {\n  const client = new LocalLlmClient({ ...config, maxSteps: 1 }, { role: \"qualification\", diagnosticHandler: options?.diagnosticHandler });\n  const steps: VerificationStep[] = [];\n  const run = async (step: string, fn: (requestId: string) => Promise<string>) => {\n    const requestId = randomUUID();\n    try {\n      steps.push({ step, ok: true, detail: await fn(requestId), requestId });\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      steps.push({\n        step,\n        ok: false,\n        detail: err instanceof InferenceError ? \"Provider request failed\" : \"Verification failed\",\n        requestId,\n        failureKind: err instanceof InferenceError ? err.kind : \"verification_error\",\n        ...(err instanceof InferenceError ? { failureCondition: err.condition } : {}),\n      });\n    }\n  };\n  await run(\"streamed completion\", async (id) => {\n    let streamed = \"\";\n    const m = await client.chatCompletionStream([{ role: \"user\", content: \"Reply with exactly the word READY.\" }], [], (t) => (streamed += t), id, signal);\n    const text = typeof m.content === \"string\" ? m.content : \"\";\n    if (!/READY/i.test(text)) throw new Error(`unexpected reply: ${text.slice(0, 80)}`);\n    return `streamed completion received (${streamed.length} chars)`;\n  });\n  if (!steps[0].ok) return steps;\n  const nonce = `n${randomUUID().slice(0, 8)}`;\n  const history: ChatMessage[] = [\n    { role: \"system\", content: \"You are a connectivity check. Use the tool when asked.\" },\n    { role: \"user\", content: `Call echo_token with token \"${nonce}\", then tell me what it returned.` },\n  ];\n    triggerBackgroundGc();\n    spawnTui(tuiBin, sidecarScript);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (isInteractiveTty && !tuiBin) {\n    console.error(\"nexus: the live TUI is not built (run 'make build'); starting the REPL.\");\n  }\n\n  await startRepl(options);\n}\n\nconst program = new Command();\n\n// Options given before a subcommand belong to the top-level launch (`nexus --provider X` opens the TUI with it);\n// options after a subcommand belong to that subcommand. Without this, the top-level --provider/-m swallowed the\n// subcommand's own (`nexus providers verify --provider openrouter` reported --provider missing).\nprogram.enablePositionalOptions();\n\nprogram\n  .name(\"nexus\")\n  .description(\"Nexus Code - Custom Autonomous Coding Harness for Local AI (LM Studio / vLLM)\")\n  .version(getBuildIdentity().string)\n  .option(\"--repl\", \"Start interactive coding session (REPL)\")\n  .option(\"--live\", \"Start live TUI\")\n  .option(\"-r, --resume [id]\", \"Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\")\n  .option(\"--approve\", \"Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\")\n  .option(\"-y, --yes\", \"Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\")\n  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\n  .option(\"--read-only\", \"Reject all mutating tool executions and commands\")\n  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\n  .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\")\n  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory (default: current directory)\")\n  .option(\"-s, --max-steps <number>\", \"Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\")\n  .option(\"--max-total-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\")\n  .option(\"--strict-token-count\", \"Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\")\n  .option(\"--max-turn-minutes <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\")\n  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n  .option(\"--no-continuation\", \"End a turn at --max-steps instead of continuing while it makes progress\")\n  .option(\"-t, --temperature <number>\", \"Model temperature (default: 0.2)\")\n  .option(\"--shell <type>\", \"Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash)\", \"bash\")\n      const authorized = config.authorizedDisclosureOrigins ?? [];\n      console.log(pc.dim(`Authorized cloud destinations: ${authorized.length ? authorized.map((origin) => safeOriginOf(origin) ?? \"(invalid endpoint)\").join(\", \") : \"none\"}`));\n      console.log(pc.dim(\"Select with --provider <id> --model <id> (or NEXUS_PROVIDER / NEXUS_MODEL in ~/.config/nexus/config.env).\\n\"));\n    });\n\n  providers\n    .command(\"verify\")\n    .description(\"Live check: streamed completion and a tool round trip against a provider (sends no workspace content)\")\n    .requiredOption(\"--provider <id>\", \"Provider to check\")\n    .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model id (default: $NEXUS_MODEL)\")\n    .option(\"--base-url <url>\", \"Override the provider's base URL\")\n    .option(\"-j, --json\", \"Print steps and receipts as JSON\")\n    .action(async (options: any) => {\n      let config: HarnessConfig;\n      try {\n        config = buildConfig(options);\n      } catch (err: any) {\n        console.error(pc.red(safeConfigurationError(err)));\n        process.exit(2);\n      }\n      const abort = new AbortController();\n      process.once(\"SIGINT\", () => abort.abort(new Error(\"SIGINT\")));\n      const diagnosticHandler = (level: \"error\" | \"warn\", message: string) => {\n        (level === \"warn\" ? console.warn : console.error)(pc.dim(safeClientDiagnostic(message, config)));\n      };\n      const steps = await verifyProvider(config, abort.signal, { diagnosticHandler });\n      const receipts = UsageLedger.global().all();\n      const summary = verificationSummary(steps, receipts, { provider: config.provider, model: config.model });\n      if (options.json) {\n        console.log(JSON.stringify({ date: new Date().toISOString(), ...summary }, null, 2));\n      } else {\n        console.log(pc.bold(`\\nLive provider check\\n${describeTarget(config)}`));\n        for (const s of steps) {\n          const disposition = s.ok ? \"passed\" : `failed${s.failureKind ? ` (${s.failureKind}${s.failureCondition ? `/${s.failureCondition}` : \"\"})` : \"\"}`;\n          console.log(`  ${s.ok ? pc.green(\"✓\") : pc.red(\"✗\")} ${s.step}: ${disposition} — ${s.detail}`);\n        }\n        const usageSummary = UsageLedger.global().summary();\n        if (usageSummary) console.log(pc.dim(usageSummary));\n        console.log(summary.passed ? pc.green(\"\\nInference verified (completion + tool round trip).\\n\") : pc.red(\"\\nNot verified.\\n\"));\n      }\n      process.exitCode = summary.passed ? 0 : 1;\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":18374978}},"started_at_ms":1793001629587,"completed_at_ms":1793001630606}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:00:32.300Z","ordinal":378138,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17739-b22b-7053-be32-29be72e974ed","call_id":"call_706363421f134a6fae00f47bd1ab3b55","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n]);\n\nfunction safeStepDetail(ok: boolean, detail: string): string {\n  if (!ok) return detail === \"Provider request failed\" ? detail : \"Verification failed\";\n  if (/^streamed completion received \\(\\d+ chars\\)$/.test(detail)) return detail;\n  if (/^echo_token tool call completed \\(\\d+ call\\(s\\)\\)$/.test(detail)) return detail;\n  return detail === \"tool result round trip completed\" ? detail : \"Verification succeeded\";\n}\n\n/** A credential-safe JSON projection for `providers verify --json`; raw provider diagnostics are deliberately omitted. */\nexport function verificationSummary(\n  steps: readonly VerificationStep[],\n  receipts: readonly import(\"./usage.js\").InferenceReceipt[],\n  target?: Pick<HarnessConfig, \"provider\" | \"model\">,\n) {\n  const provider = safeProviderId(target?.provider ?? receipts[0]?.providerId);\n  const model = target?.model ?? receipts[0]?.selectedModel;\n  return {\n    passed: steps.length === 3 && steps.every((step) => step.ok),\n    ...(provider ? { provider } : {}),\n    ...(model ? { model: safeModelId(model) } : {}),\n    steps: steps.map(({ step, ok, requestId, detail, failureKind, failureCondition }) => {\n      const safeKind = failureKind && SAFE_FAILURE_KINDS.has(failureKind) ? failureKind : undefined;\n      const safeCondition = failureCondition && SAFE_FAILURE_CONDITIONS.has(failureCondition) ? failureCondition : undefined;\n      return {\n        step, ok, requestId, detail: safeStepDetail(ok, detail),\n        ...(safeKind ? { failureKind: safeKind } : {}),\n        ...(safeCondition ? { condition: safeCondition } : {}),\n      };\n    }),\n    receipts: receipts.map(({ at, requestId, role, providerId, selectedModel, effectiveModel, endpointOrigin, protocol, disclosure, executions, outcome, failureKind, usage, usageConfidence, costConfidence }) => {\n      const origin = safeOriginOf(endpointOrigin);\n      return {\n        at, requestId, role, providerId: safeProviderId(providerId) ?? \"(unrecognized provider)\",\n        selectedModel: safeModelId(selectedModel),\n        ...(effectiveModel ? { effectiveModel: safeModelId(effectiveModel) } : {}),\n        ...(origin ? { endpointOrigin: origin } : {}),\n        protocol, disclosure, ...(executions !== undefined ? { executions } : {}), outcome,\n        ...(failureKind && SAFE_FAILURE_KINDS.has(failureKind) ? { failureKind } : {}), ...(usage ? { usage } : {}), usageConfidence, costConfidence,\n      };\n    }),\n  };\n}\n\nconst ECHO_TOOL: ToolDefinition = {\n  type: \"function\",\n  function: {\n    name: \"echo_token\",\n    description: \"Echo the given token back. Call this exactly once with the token the user gives you.\",\n    parameters: { type: \"object\", properties: { token: { type: \"string\", description: \"The token to echo\" } }, required: [\"token\"] },\n  },\n};\n\nexport interface VerificationStep {\n  step: string;\n  ok: boolean;\n  detail: string;\n  requestId: string;\n  failureKind?: string;\n  failureCondition?: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * Live qualification without workspace content: a streamed completion, then a tool round trip (the model must call\n * echo_token with a nonce, receive its result and answer). Each step is one receipt in the usage ledger.\n */\nexport async function verifyProvider(\n  config: HarnessConfig,\n  signal?: AbortSignal,\n  options?: { diagnosticHandler?: (level: \"error\" | \"warn\", message: string) => void },\n): Promise<VerificationStep[]> {\n  const client = new LocalLlmClient({ ...config, maxSteps: 1 }, { role: \"qualification\", diagnosticHandler: options?.diagnosticHandler });\n  const steps: VerificationStep[] = [];\n  const run = async (step: string, fn: (requestId: string) => Promise<string>) => {\n    const requestId = randomUUID();\n    try {\n      steps.push({ step, ok: true, detail: await fn(requestId), requestId });\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      steps.push({\n        step,\n        ok: false,\n        detail: err instanceof InferenceError ? \"Provider request failed\" : \"Verification failed\",\n        requestId,\n        failureKind: err instanceof InferenceError ? err.kind : \"verification_error\",\n        ...(err instanceof InferenceError ? { failureCondition: err.condition } : {}),\n      });\n    }\n  };\n  await run(\"streamed completion\", async (id) => {\n    let streamed = \"\";\n    const m = await client.chatCompletionStream([{ role: \"user\", content: \"Reply with exactly the word READY.\" }], [], (t) => (streamed += t), id, signal);\n    const text = typeof m.content === \"string\" ? m.content : \"\";\n    if (!/READY/i.test(text)) throw new Error(`unexpected reply: ${text.slice(0, 80)}`);\n    return `streamed completion received (${streamed.length} chars)`;\n  });\n  if (!steps[0].ok) return steps;\n  const nonce = `n${randomUUID().slice(0, 8)}`;\n  const history: ChatMessage[] = [\n    { role: \"system\", content: \"You are a connectivity check. Use the tool when asked.\" },\n    { role: \"user\", content: `Call echo_token with token \"${nonce}\", then tell me what it returned.` },\n  ];\n    triggerBackgroundGc();\n    spawnTui(tuiBin, sidecarScript);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (isInteractiveTty && !tuiBin) {\n    console.error(\"nexus: the live TUI is not built (run 'make build'); starting the REPL.\");\n  }\n\n  await startRepl(options);\n}\n\nconst program = new Command();\n\n// Options given before a subcommand belong to the top-level launch (`nexus --provider X` opens the TUI with it);\n// options after a subcommand belong to that subcommand. Without this, the top-level --provider/-m swallowed the\n// subcommand's own (`nexus providers verify --provider openrouter` reported --provider missing).\nprogram.enablePositionalOptions();\n\nprogram\n  .name(\"nexus\")\n  .description(\"Nexus Code - Custom Autonomous Coding Harness for Local AI (LM Studio / vLLM)\")\n  .version(getBuildIdentity().string)\n  .option(\"--repl\", \"Start interactive coding session (REPL)\")\n  .option(\"--live\", \"Start live TUI\")\n  .option(\"-r, --resume [id]\", \"Resume previous session (defaults to latest if id omitted)\")\n  .option(\"--approve\", \"Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\")\n  .option(\"-y, --yes\", \"Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\")\n  .option(\"--mode <mode>\", \"Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\")\n  .option(\"--read-only\", \"Reject all mutating tool executions and commands\")\n  .option(\"-e, --endpoint <url>\", \"Local LLM endpoint (default: $LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT)\")\n  .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\")\n  .option(\"-w, --workspace <path>\", \"Workspace directory (default: current directory)\")\n  .option(\"-s, --max-steps <number>\", \"Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\")\n  .option(\"--max-total-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit total-step limit for one turn (default: none; progressing work continues)\")\n  .option(\"--strict-token-count\", \"Refuse a request the connection could not count on a worker (default: proceed on the labelled estimate)\")\n  .option(\"--max-turn-minutes <number>\", \"Continuation: an explicit wall-clock limit for one turn in minutes (default: none)\")\n  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n  .option(\"--no-continuation\", \"End a turn at --max-steps instead of continuing while it makes progress\")\n  .option(\"-t, --temperature <number>\", \"Model temperature (default: 0.2)\")\n  .option(\"--shell <type>\", \"Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh (default: bash)\", \"bash\")\n      const authorized = config.authorizedDisclosureOrigins ?? [];\n      console.log(pc.dim(`Authorized cloud destinations: ${authorized.length ? authorized.map((origin) => safeOriginOf(origin) ?? \"(invalid endpoint)\").join(\", \") : \"none\"}`));\n      console.log(pc.dim(\"Select with --provider <id> --model <id> (or NEXUS_PROVIDER / NEXUS_MODEL in ~/.config/nexus/config.env).\\n\"));\n    });\n\n  providers\n    .command(\"verify\")\n    .description(\"Live check: streamed completion and a tool round trip against a provider (sends no workspace content)\")\n    .requiredOption(\"--provider <id>\", \"Provider to check\")\n    .option(\"-m, --model <name>\", \"Model id (default: $NEXUS_MODEL)\")\n    .option(\"--base-url <url>\", \"Override the provider's base URL\")\n    .option(\"-j, --json\", \"Print steps and receipts as JSON\")\n    .action(async (options: any) => {\n      let config: HarnessConfig;\n      try {\n        config = buildConfig(options);\n      } catch (err: any) {\n        console.error(pc.red(safeConfigurationError(err)));\n        process.exit(2);\n      }\n      const abort = new AbortController();\n      process.once(\"SIGINT\", () => abort.abort(new Error(\"SIGINT\")));\n      const diagnosticHandler = (level: \"error\" | \"warn\", message: string) => {\n        (level === \"warn\" ? console.warn : console.error)(pc.dim(safeClientDiagnostic(message, config)));\n      };\n      const steps = await verifyProvider(config, abort.signal, { diagnosticHandler });\n      const receipts = UsageLedger.global().all();\n      const summary = verificationSummary(steps, receipts, { provider: config.provider, model: config.model });\n      if (options.json) {\n        console.log(JSON.stringify({ date: new Date().toISOString(), ...summary }, null, 2));\n      } else {\n        console.log(pc.bold(`\\nLive provider check\\n${describeTarget(config)}`));\n        for (const s of steps) {\n          const disposition = s.ok ? \"passed\" : `failed${s.failureKind ? ` (${s.failureKind}${s.failureCondition ? `/${s.failureCondition}` : \"\"})` : \"\"}`;\n          console.log(`  ${s.ok ? pc.green(\"✓\") : pc.red(\"✗\")} ${s.step}: ${disposition} — ${s.detail}`);\n        }\n        const usageSummary = UsageLedger.global().summary();\n        if (usageSummary) console.log(pc.dim(usageSummary));\n        console.log(summary.passed ? pc.green(\"\\nInference verified (completion + tool round trip).\\n\") : pc.red(\"\\nNot verified.\\n\"));\n      }\n      process.exitCode = summary.passed ? 0 : 1;\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17734-064a-7c40-9dfa-d9e4ca640901","create_time":1793001632.2998855}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
