{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:04:53.320Z","ordinal":378369,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1773c-9417-7e32-a0cb-d3e5e6bfeafe","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6e76cb99-a290-4e0d-9273-6d8218acf72d","process_id":"92154","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md; printf '\\nPR current content excerpt:\\n'; gh api 'repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/contents/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md?ref=v1/readiness-rc7-checkpoint' --jq .content | base64 -d | sed -n '1,220p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md; printf '\\nPR current content excerpt:\\n'; gh api 'repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/contents/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md?ref=v1/readiness-rc7-checkpoint' --jq .content | base64 -d | sed -n '1,220p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"cat: .git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md: Is a directory\n\nPR current content excerpt:\n# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 06:24 UTC at `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, incorporating PR #249 (`8e562b0f3406e94003806746cb69a5258f72a59f`) and PR #250. PR #249 merged at 05:57 UTC and PR #250 merged at 06:20 UTC. On this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirms all components are `1.0.0-rc.8`. CodeQL run [40279197561](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197561) passed. Exact-main CI [40279197785](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197785) is still running; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed Rust tests and release builds and were running the CLI test suite at 06:24 UTC. The current checkpoint does not claim full CI success.\n\n**RC and publication state:** The latest public prerelease remains `v1.0.0-rc.7`; `v1.0.0-rc.8` is not yet tagged or published. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The `rc.8` source version is not itself evidence of an accepted or installed RC. No release artifact should be published until every required acceptance gate passes.\n\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1), for held-out T2/T3 corpus custody, remains OPEN (last observed update 02:33:48 UTC); the required custodian sealing and independent private-custody acceptance are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4 qualification, installed exact-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and the human terminal matrix (0/15 at last evidence) remain incomplete. Treat the older entries below as historical snapshots; they do not supersede these current observations.\n\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 02:27 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`. CI run [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) and CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) both completed successfully on that exact commit. CI passed the Node 22/24 and Linux test matrices, requirements enforcement, security gates, package build and reproducibility, SBOM checks, and package/install smoke checks.\n\n**PR #246 / `agent.ts`:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) has been updated onto current `main`; its exact head is `2351e57ace040a48e9ff082d285a5d7edc8ed385`, based on `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`. `KimiCode-defect-scan` retains the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. The implementation patch hash remains identical to the previously independently accepted diff (`d2d17c7c36072a0c310e998d67df69821007a2085990f84ca9342556610df853`). Exact-head CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; CI run [40259036321](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40259036321) has Node 22 and Node 24 jobs still running. No merge has occurred; require those checks to finish successfully before integration.\n\n**Release state:** RC7 remains the latest public qualification prerelease and does not include PR #243 or subsequent main changes. Held-out qualification, provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4, human terminal evidence, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. Stable v1.0.0 has not been published; publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n\nThe 02:24 checkpoint below is retained as a historical snapshot and is superseded by this exact-head update.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 02:24 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; superseded by 02:27 update)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074` (PR #244 merge). CI run [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) and CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) both completed successfully on that exact commit. The CI run passed Node 22 and 24, Linux CLI and Rust tests, requirements enforcement, security gates, Linux package creation, reproducibility comparisons, SBOM validation, and package/install smoke checks.\n\n**PR #246 / `agent.ts` handoff:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) remains open at `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`. Its exact-head run [40255358554](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255358554), CodeQL run [40255358512](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255358512), and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed on that old base; these are not current-main integration evidence. `KimiCode-defect-scan` owns `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`, branch `v1/defect-agent-readonly-current`, worktree `/home/mike/nexus-wt/agent-readonly-current`. The claims log records handoff at 01:54 UTC and an actionable handoff checkpoint at 02:24 UTC: the previously active current-main CI has completed successfully, so Kimi can update the branch normally onto current `origin/main`, then rerun exact-head checks and obtain any required independent re-review. At this checkpoint the PR branch is still on its old base and has not been integrated.\n\n**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, an ancestor of current `main`. It adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock. Its required checks passed and an independent review accepted the exact diff. This is source remediation on current `main`; RC6 and RC7 artifacts predate it. The next installed RC still needs to be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming a released fix.\n\n**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the signature as unverified (`bad_email`); it is not verified-signature provenance. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; both results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n\n**Custody and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian response after the 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC metadata-only request. Public manifest metadata does not satisfy independent private custody acceptance. OpenRouter remains disconnected on the last checked Ubuntu desktop status; no E4 local gateway qualification evidence was available there. No stable `v1.0.0` release is published; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`, and existing publication authorization remains granted but gated on the required acceptance evidence.\n\nThe previous 02:19 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; this 02:24 checkpoint supersedes its integration-CI and PR #246 handoff status.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 02:19 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; superseded by 02:24 update)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074` (PR #244 merge). CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) passed on that exact commit. In CI [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634), Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; the Linux x86-64 CLI suite passed at 02:18:37 UTC and `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passed at 02:18:39 UTC. Linux package creation began at 02:18:39 UTC and is still running; the workflow has no final conclusion yet.\n\n**PR #246 / `agent.ts` handoff:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) remains open at head `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`. Exact-head run [40255358554](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255358554) completed successfully across Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64, including Linux package reproducibility. CodeQL run `40255358512` and JavaScript/TypeScript checks also passed. `KimiCode-defect-scan` retains the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. A read-only merge-tree preflight against current `main` found no conflicts, but the branch has not yet been updated or merged. The claims log records that Kimi's next step is to update normally onto current `main` and rerun exact-head checks; the old-base run is not integration evidence.\n\n**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, an ancestor of current `main`. It adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock. Its required checks passed and an independent review accepted the exact diff. This is source remediation on current `main`; RC6 and RC7 artifacts predate it. The next installed RC still needs to be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming a released fix.\n\n**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the signature as unverified (`bad_email`); it is not verified-signature provenance. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; both results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n\n**Custody and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian response after the 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC metadata-only request. Public manifest metadata does not satisfy independent private custody acceptance. OpenRouter remains disconnected on the last checked Ubuntu desktop status; no E4 local gateway qualification evidence was available there. No stable `v1.0.0` release is published; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`, and publication authorization remains granted but gated on all mandatory acceptance evidence.\n\nThe previous 02:14 and 01:55 checkpoints below are retained as historical snapshots; this 02:19 checkpoint supersedes their current CI and PR #246 status.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 02:14 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; superseded by 02:19 update)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074` (PR #244 merge). CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) passed on that exact commit. CI [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) has Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; its Linux x86-64 job is still running `npm --prefix cli test` and has no final conclusion. Requirements enforcement and Linux packaging are not yet verified for this run.\n\n**PR #246 / `agent.ts` handoff:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) remains open at `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`; `KimiCode-defect-scan` owns the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. Its Node 22/24 tests, CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. In Linux job 121360325779, the CLI suite passed at 02:12:07 UTC, the first Linux package build passed at 02:13:55 UTC, and the reproducibility package build was still running at 02:14 UTC. A read-only merge-tree preflight against current `main` produced `f9653711777c4ad9be0aff59db816ea57b3dfd83` without conflicts; no branch update or merge has been performed. After all current checks finish, the recorded path remains a normal update onto current `main` followed by exact-head checks.\n\n**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged at 00:16 UTC as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, which is an ancestor of current `main`. Its focused change adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock; its tests and required PR checks passed, with independent review ACCEPT recorded for the exact diff. This is source-level remediation on current `main`, not behavior in the older RC6 or RC7 artifacts. The installed next RC must still be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming the issue fixed in a release. The `FILE_cli_src_checkpoint.ts` claim has been released after verifying merge, checks and a clean worktree.\n\n**RC and qualification:** Signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` still resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive digest is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. RC7 cross-runner reproducibility passed (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)) and installed ChatGPT verification passed 3/3 with `gpt-6-luna`; those results apply only to RC7. The five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix remains 0/15. T2/T3/T4 and standalone/provider qualification remain incomplete; no held-out execution has started.\n\n**Custody and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian response after the 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC metadata-only request. Public manifest metadata does not satisfy independent private custody acceptance. OpenRouter remains disconnected on the last checked Ubuntu desktop status; no E4 local gateway qualification evidence was available there. No stable `v1.0.0` release is published; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`, and existing publication authorization remains granted but gated on the required acceptance evidence.\n\nThe previous checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; this 02:14 UTC checkpoint supersedes its 01:55 UTC CI and PR #246 step statuses.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 01:55 UTC at `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; superseded by 02:14 update)\n\n**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074` (PR #244 merge). Post-merge CodeQL [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) passed on that exact commit. CI [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) is still running its Node 22 and Node 24 full CLI suites; setup, build, Rust tests/build, version sync, and requirements check steps have passed, but the workflow has no final conclusion yet. Do not treat the source gate as fully green until the workflow completes.\n\n**`agent.ts` handoff / PR #246:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) is open at head `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, still based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`. The slice has independent source-review ACCEPT and targeted build/tests passed, while its exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 suites remain in progress; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. At 01:54 UTC the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim was handed from `codex-root` to `KimiCode-defect-scan` with the branch and worktree recorded. The handoff requires waiting for the current checks to finish, merging current `origin/main` normally, and rerunning exact-head checks before integration.\n\n**RC7 qualification evidence:** Signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` remains the latest published candidate, resolving to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; its Linux archive digest remains `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. Cross-runner reproducibility passed for RC7 only (run [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777)); ChatGPT provider verification passed 3/3 on the installed RC7 using `gpt-6-luna`. A fresh provider-status check on the Ubuntu desktop at 01:54 UTC found ChatGPT connected and OpenRouter disconnected. RC7 evidence does not qualify a later candidate or establish acceptance.\n\n**Remaining qualification and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public update is the coordinator request from 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no custodian response or new custody acceptance. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone qualification remains incomplete, including OpenRouter; T2/T3/T4 qualification remains incomplete; the five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is unaccepted and no stable `v1.0.0` release is published. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on all required acceptance evidence.\n\n## Superseded release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 00:58 UTC at `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`)\n\n**Release state:** GitHub published signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7`; signed tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) succeeded. The published Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `7b8a5fd1d214919ae939275e59b76406d393fae31cdf4b184c33883b02dc64a9`. RC7 is an unaccepted prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is not published.\n\n**Exact `main` source gates:** `origin/main` is `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, merging PR #243's checkpoint index-lock diagnostic fix. Exact-main CI [40248550055](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550055) and CodeQL [40248550144](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248550144) both passed on that SHA. A clean detached checkout with isolated HOME/XDG passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals. The PR #243 diff SHA-256 `fb6b7d5d81d66cb237799b4d7a41c3dfd59f931eeaa84e75117a38bf9fc97928` matched its independently accepted diff exactly. RC7 predates this merge and cannot qualify the updated source.\n\n**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\n\n**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\n\n**Disposition:** Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is not accepted and no stable release is claimed. The next release candidate must include the merged checkpoint fix, pass exact-source CI and qualification gates, and be installed and identified before product qualification. Remaining gates include independent held-out custody and T2, provider/standalone behavior, T3/T4, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted once every required gate passes.\n\n## Superseded release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-25 23:43 UTC at `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`)\n\n## Earlier release checkpoint (superseded; observed 2026-10-25 23:43 UTC at `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`)\n\n**Release state:** GitHub lists `v1.0.0-rc.6` as the latest published prerelease. Signed tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` (tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824`) now points to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) is in progress. GitHub has not published an RC7 release or assets yet. RC6 is not an accepted RC, and no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\n\n**Exact `main` source gates:** Current `origin/main` is `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40243331241](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331241) passed on this exact SHA. Post-merge CI run [40243331324](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243331324) completed successfully on this exact SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility, SBOM, smoke, and installer checks passed. At this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These source gates do not constitute installed-RC acceptance.\n\n**Candidate changes:** PR #241 merged source/version preparation at `431cb194`, and signed RC7 tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` points to that exact source. PR #243 is refreshed onto exact base `431cb194` at head `a563eee0206d1287f5375a0ae113b1ca392fffd1`. Its CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed; its exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs are running in CI run [40244800085](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40244800085). Independent source review accepted the exact candidate diff. PR #244 updates only this readiness document at head `0618fbc9d123043506f76eacf9753892cdd06963`; its CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 checks passed, while Linux packaging is running in [40243816407](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40243816407). PR #245 updates four manifests/lockfiles for the completed Cloudflare experiment at head `13a955dbe156daec996fd97cfe6946024a3f0b48`; CodeQL, JavaScript/TypeScript, Node 22, and Node 24 passed, and Linux packaging is running in [40244355480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40244355480). An independent source review accepted PR #245's exact diff. No PR has been merged on the strength of checks from another commit.\n\n**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\n\n**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n\n## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-23 13:35 UTC at `1f3c655`)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n\n**Distribution scope:** The release owner confirmed the supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive only; npm publication is inapplicable. The current release workflow is the authority for published assets.\n\n**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\n\n**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n\n**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\n\n**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n\n## Current RC3 artifact and installed-candidate status (observed 2026-10-23 09:11 UTC at `1b9791f`; point-in-time snapshot)\n\n**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\n\n**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\n\n**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\n\n**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\n\n## Historical readiness snapshot (observed 2026-10-23 08:14 UTC at `1b9791f`; superseded above)\n\n**Release source and branch reconciliation:** Release PRs #147, #153, #157, and #159 target `main`; the current release source is `origin/main@1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` from 2026-10-21 and is not the source used by the current RC3 candidate PRs. Do not combine evidence from those different heads. The shared checkout remains dirty and was not modified.\n\n**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. Post-merge CI run [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL run [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) are running on the exact merge commit; do not claim post-merge CI complete until both terminate successfully.\n\n**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\n\n**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n\n**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Next source action is to finish exact post-merge CI on `1b9791f`; after it passes, proceed through the accepted RC3 workflow and exact-artifact qualification. Held-out qualification remains dependent on the independent custodian and cannot start before custody and runner compatibility are accepted.\n\n## Historical readiness snapshot (observed 2026-10-23 04:11 UTC at `1a484c3`; superseded above)\n\n**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\n\n**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in the isolated readiness worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows remain mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only; it does not qualify an installed RC or change any acceptance threshold.\n\n**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n\n**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\n\n**Doctor evidence:** The user-reported D1/D2/D3 findings were fixed in PR #151. PR #155 addresses the residual D1b latency from serial asynchronous metadata checks over large task directories. Its focused tests passed 5/5 and TypeScript checking passed; broad local doctor tests had 8 environment-prerequisite failures because the fresh worktree lacked built `cli/dist` and `nexus-tui/core` artifacts. Those failures were not classified as product regressions or counted as a pass. Exact-main CI `39896372677` subsequently passed all three jobs, including the complete CLI suite and Linux package/install checks.\n\n**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags remain `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor and checkpoint-choice fix. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at exact main and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.2`. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. A new candidate must use the next RC identity after source CI and release prerequisites pass, then undergo installed-artifact qualification.\n\n**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n\n## Historical integration checkpoint (observed 2026-10-23 02:13 UTC at `fa16045`; superseded by the current status above)\n\n**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\n\n**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n\n**Source requirements gate:** At exact main `fa16045`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed in a clean detached Git worktree with isolated HOME/XDG. Retained stdout is in the [exact-main enforcement record](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/requirements-enforce-main-fa16045.txt). It reported 123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows are explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification. This is the pre-RC source gate only. It does not qualify an installed RC or change any requirement's acceptance threshold.\n\n**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\n\n**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\n\n**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n\n## Historical integration update (2026-10-22 21:14 UTC; superseded by the current status above)\n\nThe authoritative source is `origin/main@269d611ca0a0c8a55244bf70d89fa4a918b9d218`. The Node 22 convergence branch was refreshed without rewriting history and its current candidate head is `v1/node22-floor-converged@658ace9d4ab67901b5b2db1c090f6b01537be27a`; the Node `>=22` source implementation was validated at `fb798a1bd517ac85fd3c99f76d3fda1709540a8d`, and the candidate adds reviewed ruleset and acceptance-stage reconciliations. It is not yet integrated. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at version `1.0.0-rc.2`. The source requirements check currently fails because REQ-REL-111 remains partial pending exact-candidate checks; REQ-REL-003 remains partial for installed-RC platform qualification and is now explicitly mapped to ACC-PLAT in the exact-RC stage. No threshold or qualification evidence was changed.\n\nThe live GitHub `v1-protected-branches` ruleset (ID `25340146`) currently requires `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`; it does not require Node 20. The checked-in ruleset snapshot now matches that live required-check set. No live protection setting was modified. PR #137 still targets an older base, PR #146 remains a draft, and the refreshed candidate branch has not yet been opened as a replacement PR. Independent review of the refreshed candidate requested these documentation reconciliations; code/runtime review otherwise found no blocker.\n\nPR #149 is open at `1972adb8a6d4b9bacf9974f33974b61d751de8ab` on base `269d611`; Node 20/22/24 matrix checks and CodeQL pass, while its exact-head Linux packaging job is still running. Its independent source review accepted the T3 symlink hardening, but it is not integrated until the required job concludes.\n\nThe public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross