{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:08:31.049Z","ordinal":378587,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17741-0048-7b41-a3da-f13fdfedc740","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed commit `f2402d2ec261feafbb3dbf984924bfb5b7c02e2c` against base `5d38597e30d1eb904c9eb2417e05965397631dcc`; diff SHA-256 `dfc986cb20fd2f05c00536d9270be3c979ede47eca51bed641a09e5d01ab0e38`.\n\nThe CI and CodeQL runs passed on the stated `bbafae` source. RC8’s published tag resolves to that commit, its archive digest matches the release asset, and cross-runner run `40286712425` passed both builds and comparison. The installed-copy statement is supported by the setup-only report on Issue #3; it correctly keeps the terminal matrix at 0/15. Issue #1 remains open with no custodian response in its comments. The new checkpoint preserves the 06:24 snapshot as historical and leaves acceptance and stable release gated.\n\nNo tests were run. One traceability improvement: link the installed-copy sentence directly to the Issue #3 setup report."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1773c-9417-7e32-a0cb-d3e5e6bfeafe","create_time":1793002111.0487177}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18582}}
