{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:11:32.495Z","ordinal":378741,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1773c-9417-7e32-a0cb-d3e5e6bfeafe","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0b31945c81a0ab1c308de1a799c0","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Nexus v1.0.0 convergence remains active; acceptance is IN_PROGRESS.** RC8 is published and cross-runner reproducible, but it is not accepted and stable v1.0.0 is not published.\n\nI updated the existing readiness PR with the exact-main CI result, RC8 asset digest and reproducibility run, isolated install evidence, and current blockers. The update is at [`4bb8f9d`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/4bb8f9d1eb80bef57e98e0ca08d470adca77d90e), independently reviewed as **ACCEPT**, and `git diff --check` passed. Exact-head Node 22/24 checks are still running; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. I did not run a local suite while Kimi held the active SUITE claim.\n\nRemaining release gates include custodian acceptance and held-out qualification, provider and standalone checks, T3/T4, and the 15-cell human terminal matrix. GitHub also marks the RC7/RC8 tag signatures unverified despite local GPG verification; the stable tag must use an identity GitHub verifies.\n\nThe earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade failed because RC6 rejected GitHub’s signed asset redirect. RC8 contains the redirect fix, but the isolated RC8 install did not replace the regular RC6 installation.\n\nI requested a safe-boundary update for the old RC7 provider claim. No duplicate provider run or claim takeover has occurred."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793002289602,"completed_at_ms":1793002292495}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:11:32.499Z","ordinal":378742,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0b31945c81a0ab1c308de1a799c0","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Nexus v1.0.0 convergence remains active; acceptance is IN_PROGRESS.** RC8 is published and cross-runner reproducible, but it is not accepted and stable v1.0.0 is not published.\n\nI updated the existing readiness PR with the exact-main CI result, RC8 asset digest and reproducibility run, isolated install evidence, and current blockers. The update is at [`4bb8f9d`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/4bb8f9d1eb80bef57e98e0ca08d470adca77d90e), independently reviewed as **ACCEPT**, and `git diff --check` passed. Exact-head Node 22/24 checks are still running; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. I did not run a local suite while Kimi held the active SUITE claim.\n\nRemaining release gates include custodian acceptance and held-out qualification, provider and standalone checks, T3/T4, and the 15-cell human terminal matrix. GitHub also marks the RC7/RC8 tag signatures unverified despite local GPG verification; the stable tag must use an identity GitHub verifies.\n\nThe earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade failed because RC6 rejected GitHub’s signed asset redirect. RC8 contains the redirect fix, but the isolated RC8 install did not replace the regular RC6 installation.\n\nI requested a safe-boundary update for the old RC7 provider claim. No duplicate provider run or claim takeover has occurred.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1773c-9417-7e32-a0cb-d3e5e6bfeafe","create_time":1793002289.586875,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0b31945c81a0ab1c308de1a799c0","turn_id":"01a1773c-9417-7e32-a0cb-d3e5e6bfeafe","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a17743-c513