{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:13:51.984Z","ordinal":378841,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0bbb706881a0b49a113e941ded03","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9fd532521af14a9e8c337a85bf87d81d","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc7-checkpoint/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n@@\\n-**RC8 construction and reproducibility:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) was published at 07:26 UTC and resolves to the exact source commit above. Its Linux archive has GitHub asset digest `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. Cross-runner RC reproducibility workflow [40286712425](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40286712425) completed successfully against that exact tag, including Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds and artifact comparison. An installed RC8 copy was also provenance-verified on the Ubuntu desktop in an isolated qualification prefix ([setup record](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559)); this was not the user's normal Nexus installation and is not full installed-RC acceptance. The earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade attempt failed because RC6 rejected GitHub's signed release-asset redirect. The redirect allowlist and URL-secret redaction are present in RC8; the RC6 installation was not changed by the isolated RC8 check.\\n+**RC8 construction and reproducibility:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) was published at 07:26 UTC and resolves to the exact source commit above. Its Linux archive has GitHub asset digest `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. Cross-runner RC reproducibility workflow [40286712425](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40286712425) completed successfully against that exact tag, including Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds and artifact comparison. An installed RC8 copy was also provenance-verified on the Ubuntu desktop in an isolated qualification prefix ([setup record](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559)); this was not the user's normal Nexus installation and is not full installed-RC acceptance. The tag's local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub reports it as unverified (`bad_email`); the stable tag must use a signer identity that GitHub verifies against the signing key. The earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade attempt failed because RC6 rejected GitHub's signed release-asset redirect. The redirect allowlist and URL-secret redaction are present in RC8; the RC6 installation was not changed by the isolated RC8 check.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17744-1457-7f53-89ce-61dd3a1325e4","create_time":1793002427.4406736}}}
