{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:15:03.477Z","ordinal":378914,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17744-1457-7f53-89ce-61dd3a1325e4","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0c0311d881a0a95fa3b9993e0880","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**The campaign remains active; acceptance is IN_PROGRESS.** RC8 is still a prerelease, not an accepted release.\n\nThe real-terminal setup is ready on `ubuntu-desktop` (10.0.8.3). I verified the isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868939)`, confirmed the package manifest hash, and prepared the harness and evidence directories. The human matrix is still **0/15**; each cell requires an operator to judge the checks and save two screenshots.\n\nFrom each correctly sized terminal, run the matching cell command. Kitty must have its keyboard protocol enabled; `tmux-gnome` must be tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal.\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/rc8-qual-bbafae/bin:$PATH\"\ncd \"$HOME/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal-acceptance\"\nOUT=\"$HOME/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal/evidence\"\n./run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.8 --terminal xterm --size 80x24 --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nRepeat for all 15 terminal/size pairs: xterm, kitty, tmux-gnome, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. The harness prompts for the two screenshot paths per cell; save distinct images under `$HOME/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal/screenshots/`. The harness records each operator verdict and its process and terminal-restoration measurements.\n\nPR #251’s refreshed checkpoint was independently accepted. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed; Node 22 and 24 checks are still running. A follow-up documenting GitHub’s `bad_email` signature status is committed locally but not pushed yet; I’m waiting for its independent review and the current PR checks.\n\nThe Kimi SUITE owner’s D–F bisect is still running, so I have not started another local test run. Other unresolved gates include held-out custodian acceptance, provider/standalone qualification, T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance. RC8’s local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub marks it unverified; the eventual stable tag needs a GitHub-verified signing identity."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793002499088,"completed_at_ms":1793002503477}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:15:03.484Z","ordinal":378915,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0c0311d881a0a95fa3b9993e0880","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**The campaign remains active; acceptance is IN_PROGRESS.** RC8 is still a prerelease, not an accepted release.\n\nThe real-terminal setup is ready on `ubuntu-desktop` (10.0.8.3). I verified the isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868939)`, confirmed the package manifest hash, and prepared the harness and evidence directories. The human matrix is still **0/15**; each cell requires an operator to judge the checks and save two screenshots.\n\nFrom each correctly sized terminal, run the matching cell command. Kitty must have its keyboard protocol enabled; `tmux-gnome` must be tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal.\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/rc8-qual-bbafae/bin:$PATH\"\ncd \"$HOME/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal-acceptance\"\nOUT=\"$HOME/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal/evidence\"\n./run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.8 --terminal xterm --size 80x24 --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nRepeat for all 15 terminal/size pairs: xterm, kitty, tmux-gnome, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. The harness prompts for the two screenshot paths per cell; save distinct images under `$HOME/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal/screenshots/`. The harness records each operator verdict and its process and terminal-restoration measurements.\n\nPR #251’s refreshed checkpoint was independently accepted. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed; Node 22 and 24 checks are still running. A follow-up documenting GitHub’s `bad_email` signature status is committed locally but not pushed yet; I’m waiting for its independent review and the current PR checks.\n\nThe Kimi SUITE owner’s D–F bisect is still running, so I have not started another local test run. Other unresolved gates include held-out custodian acceptance, provider/standalone qualification, T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance. RC8’s local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub marks it unverified; the eventual stable tag needs a GitHub-verified signing identity.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17744-1457-7f53-89ce-61dd3a1325e4","create_time":1793002499.071875,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf0c0311d881a0a95fa3b9993e0880","turn_id":"01a17744-1457-7f53-89ce-61dd3a1325e4","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a17746-fd3b-7770-b567-3df9768accef","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18591}}
