{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:15:27.848Z","ordinal":378924,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17747-5c68-7bc3-9245-bf1061f9975b","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed `49eeea053dae33fe9389e000965b7d0de75e64d7` (parent `4bb8f9d1eb80bef57e98e0ca08d470adca77d90e`), one-line documentation change; diff SHA-256 `5bb41c41e68dc498249b742ab0675a763377089c470e01184b145e1a66c0730c`.\n\nThe local GPG verification succeeds with key `FAC522F6588C64266ABC7742140FD4DD53964C08`; GitHub reports `verified: false`, reason `bad_email`. Advising a matching signer identity for a GitHub-verified stable tag is technically accurate. The repository’s release process does not separately establish GitHub-verified GPG status as an acceptance gate, so the sentence should be read as a signing recommendation, not a new qualification threshold."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17747-5c00-79e0-9591-d386e30fc22a","create_time":1793002527.8480878}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18592}}
