c793ea163fa","order":18722,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17791-1188-7ab2-8608-4cd58583c62d","text":"The handed-off branch is clean, the independent review is recorded, and current main is `e9304b1`. The former owner’s suite claim is released and no local test process is running. I’ve taken the hot-file claims and am rebasing the single candidate commit onto that main revision.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf1f1270dc81a096316566b608aebf","order":18723,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17791-62bd-7861-8be7-462b8fb9f135","text":"The reset-retry candidate rebased cleanly onto `e9304b1` as `afec611`. I compared the original and rebased patch hashes; they are identical (`736d3d…e2f9cff`), so the existing independent ACCEPT still covers the same two-file change. I’m preparing its PR for fresh exact-head CI.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf1f688ad881a09538f455d16012a4","order":18724,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17792-b2c0-7a01-a8f2-50bc4671a4ed","text":"A separate 120-second `npm test` is currently running from Nexus in the shared, dirty checkout without a visible suite claim. I’m leaving that process and checkout untouched and will not start local tests. Hosted CI for PRs #252 and #253 continues independently.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf1fc0a08081a0bed71155b34c065e","order":18726,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17794-0bc5-7e62-8168-773ae00851cb","text":"PR #253 is open at the current main base with its byte-identical, independently accepted retry patch; fresh CI is running. PR #252 still has checks on the older base, so I’ll wait for those runs to finish before rebasing it. The unrelated shared-checkout test process has exited; I have no result for that run.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf20248dc481a0b5738a7777ec0e33","order":18729,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17795-9248-75e2-81a2-94f9fe8d912b","text":"The post-merge main Node 22/24 suites have passed and Linux setup has begun. PR #252’s older-base Node suites and PR #253’s rebased exact-head Node suites are running; PR #253 has also passed its earlier version/build/core-test steps. No local tests are running under our claims.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf20b7ba7481a083494ee8d66a587f","order":18733,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17797-d019-7632-aa7a-9feb335a59a2","text":"PR #252’s Node 22/24 suites have passed; its Linux job is building release binaries. PR #253’s Node suites and the post-merge main CLI suite remain active. I’ll rebase #252 after its current checks are terminal, preserving its reviewed diff.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf21d7c13081a0bd3caeb6f162cc69","order":18739,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1779c-34cd-79c2-a2a6-eaf8254f3908","text":"PR #252’s Node 22/24 suites have passed, and its Linux CLI suite is now running. PR #253’s Node matrix and the post-merge main Node suites are also active, with no reported failures so far.","turn_id":"01a1775d-5aef-7821-840a-9ebca31e58cd"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":18741,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not auth