ion sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-26-| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:27:| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:28:| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-29-| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-32-| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-34-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-35-**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-39-The longest dependency chain is:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-40-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:41:**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-42-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-43-- M1 comes first because the posture change (DEC-01) alters behaviour that every later test, eval and acceptance run depends on. Qualifying before it would have to be redone.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:44:- M3 is on the path because resume (AGT-01), work-unit durability (AGT-02a) and standalone sizing (PRV-06) are blockers, and the T4 class 9 test (SIGTERM, then resume) needs them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-45-- M5 is bounded by serial inference on the single gateway host.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-46-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-50-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-51-- M2, M4;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:52:- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-53-- the stripping proxy and the conformance fixtures.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-54-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-60-| G1 | End of M1 | All safety acceptance IDs pass in CI. Existing PTY suites stay green. No new skipped tests. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-61-| G2 | End of M2 | A package smoke run in a PTY shows the TUI. The doc-command test passes. Release dry-run assets are complete. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:62:| G3 | End of M3 | Continuity, inference and verification acceptance IDs pass. The eval harness self-tests pass, including the T4 smoke. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-63-| G4 | End of M4 | Persistence acceptance IDs pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-64-| G5 | After the RC | ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 pass. The DEC-05 thresholds are met. Independent reports are filed. |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-78-| Risk | Effect | Mitigation |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-79-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:80:| The DEC-01 default change breaks many test fixtures | M1 takes longer | PR-1a lands the classes behind a constant; PR-1b flips the default with mechanical fixture updates |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-81-| The gateway host is unavailable or thermally limited during M5 | M5 is delayed | Serial runs with resumable runner; schedule against the thermal-soak findings; T2 runs are resumable per task |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:82:| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-83-| Parser restriction (PLAN-11) lowers the tool-call rate on text-only models | Task quality falls | Recorded fixtures; one-RC escape hatch; the qualification measures it |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-84-| Independent reviewer is unavailable (X5) | G5 cannot be met honestly | The owner must supply a reviewer. The audit does not substitute self-assessment for it. |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-93-- the memory measurements.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-94-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\n--\neval/README.md-51-| Field | Meaning |\neval/README.md-52-|---|---|\neval/README.md:53:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md-54-| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\neval/README.md-55-| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\neval/README.md-56-| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\neval/README.md:57:| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\neval/README.md-58-| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\neval/README.md-59-| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n--\neval/README.md-81-  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\neval/README.md-82-\neval/README.md:83:## Fault injection (T4)\neval/README.md-84-\neval/README.md:85:A task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\neval/README.md-86-chat request (counted from 1):\neval/README.md-87-\neval/README.md:88:| kind | Fault |\neval/README.md-89-|---|---|\neval/README.md-90-| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n--\neval/README.md-95-| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\neval/README.md-96-\neval/README.md:97:What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\neval/README.md:98:`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\neval/README.md-99-\neval/README.md-100-- runs;\n--\neval/README.md-104-- hung past budget.\neval/README.md-105-\neval/README.md:106:The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test command, a full disk) and from the SIGTERM-then-resume\neval/README.md:107:runner case. A fixture task declares `t4Fixture: { kind, tool: \"run_command\", command, timeoutSecs }` for a hanging\neval/README.md:108:test, or `t4Fixture: { kind: \"full_disk\", tool: \"run_command\", command, storageLimitBytes }` for a full disk. Nexus\neval/README.md:109:T4 runs opt into sanitized evaluator receipts containing the digest of the command actually executed, the runner's\neval/README.md-110-timeout/exit result, and workspace free space before and after the invocation. The runner counts an exact command\neval/README.md-111-digest plus an actual timeout for a hang, or a failed command that takes the dedicated storage tmpfs from near-full\neval/README.md-112-capacity to exhausted. Both require successful cgroup cleanup with no survivors. Task metadata cannot provide\neval/README.md:113:evidence or a pass bit. `make test` includes a T4 smoke test with two injected faults (`cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`).\neval/README.md-114-\neval/README.md-115-## Qualification runs\n--\neval/README.md-143-  fresh `git init` that fetches only the pinned commit and its ancestors from the local cache (`--no-tags`, no\neval/README.md-144-  FETCH_HEAD), then checks out that commit detached. There is no `--shared` clone, alternates link, remote, tag or\neval/README.md:145:  descendant object, so the upstream fix that follows a held-out baseline is not reachable from the workspace. Staging\neval/README.md-146-  verifies this and refuses the run otherwise.\neval/README.md-147-\n--\neval/README.md-283-\neval/README.md-284-The frozen qualification config sets the limit values. They must be recorded before the first scored run and must not\neval/README.md:285:be tuned against held-out results.\neval/README.md-286-\neval/README.md-287-The evaluator proxy allows one in-flight inference request at a time and destroys the upstream HTTP request/response\neval/README.md-288-when the candidate-side request is cancelled or its connection closes. This bounds proxy concurrency and propagates\neval/README.md:289:transport cancellation, but it does not prove that a remote provider or model runtime stopped generation after the\neval/README.md-290-connection closed; that behavior requires runtime-specific evidence. The total request limit remains a separate cap.\neval/README.md-291-\n--\neval/README.md-300-  cannot do.) The 6-task pilot is directional only; qualification needs the full task set;\neval/README.md-301-- T3: false-absence claims = 0 and steering constraints honoured in ≥ 95 % of runs;\neval/README.md:302:- T4: truthful bounded outcome in 100 % of fault runs;\neval/README.md-303-- ≥ 5 runs per task-configuration, per-task results with 95 % intervals.\neval/README.md-304-\n--\neval/README.md-313-| T2 task set (pilot fixture tasks `t2-*`) | done |\neval/README.md-314-| T3 task set (fact-sheet scorer / steering checks) | not started |\neval/README.md:315:| T4 fault injector | in progress |\neval/README.md:316:| Qualification runs | blocked on independent corpus custody, enforced aggregate sandbox resource limits, completed T3/T4 workloads, exact-RC/provider evidence, and the required operational approvals; the earlier pilot's inference-hour, cloud-budget, and peer-install decisions also remain separate prerequisites |\neval/README.md-317-\neval/README.md-318-## Pilot 2026-10-13 (4 h appliance window)\n--\neval/README.md-325-\neval/README.md-326-Deviations from §9, recorded before the run: fixture tasks rather than external repositories at pinned commits; T2\neval/README.md:327:only (no T3/T4 — the window is too short); Codex CLI excluded (the gateway does not serve `/v1/responses`); Aider runs\neval/README.md-328-one `--message` exchange with `--yes-always` (its non-interactive mode); no cloud configuration (operator decision);\neval/README.md-329-runs per task as many as the window allows, run-major, target 5.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-25-2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-26-3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-29-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-30-The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-31-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:32:Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-33-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-35-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-36-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:37:### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-38-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:39:| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-40-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-41-| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-43-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:44:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:45:| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:52:| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-54-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:56:### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-57-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-58-| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-84-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:115:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-122-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-124-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-125-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-133-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-134-   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:135:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-136-5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-137-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:138:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-139-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-140-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-141-|---|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-143-| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-144-| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-148-ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-149-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-151-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:152:| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-153-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-155-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-156-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-158-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-160-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-161-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-189-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-191-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-193-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:194:For each terminal × size, check:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-195-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-196-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-199-4. Resize during streaming.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-200-5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:201:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-202-7. NO_COLOR.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-203-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-205-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-206-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-210-Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-211-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:212:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-213-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-214-- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-215-- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-216-- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:217:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-218-- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-219-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-231-  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-232-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-234-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-236-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-237-1. refused connection mid-turn\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-245-9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-246-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:247:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-248-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-249-- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-253-| Metric | Gate |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-254-|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-256-| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-257-| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-258-| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-259-| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-262-| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-263-| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-306-   - ACC-PKG-01;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-307-   - 5 random T2 tasks;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:308:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:309:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-310-3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-311-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-331-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-332-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:333:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:334:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-335-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-336-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-337-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-338-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-342-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-344-- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-345-\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":96122978}},"started_at_ms":1793008519987,"completed_at_ms":1793008521084}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:55:22.355Z","ordinal":381956,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a177a2-d473-70f0-9a80-74630305a1ff","call_id":"call_19902355a0ee41da8a0daf0a15de13ec","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9088)\nTotal output lines: 297\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-8-- **Inference.** Inference comes only from the homelab gateway (DEC-16): one model host, with runs serialised.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-9-- **Uncertainty.** The largest unknown is how many fix loops M5 qualification triggers. The pilot's history suggests at least one.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:10:- **Supporting labour.** Held-out tasks are written by an agent author (authorised, DEC-05). Independent acceptance is done by a reviewer the owner provides (X5).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-11-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-12-## Milestones\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-18-        │                                                                                   │\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-19-        └──► M4 Persistence hygiene (parallel with M2/M3) ──────────────────────────────────┤\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:20:  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-21-```\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-22-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-25-| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-26-| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:27:| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:28:| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-29-| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-32-| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-34-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-35-**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-39-The longest dependency chain is:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-40-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:41:**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-42-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-43-- M1 comes first because the posture change (DEC-01) alters behaviour that every later test, eval and acceptance run depends on. Qualifying before it would have to be redone.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:44:- M3 is on the path because resume (AGT-01), work-unit durability (AGT-02a) and standalone sizing (PRV-06) are blockers, and the T4 class 9 test (SIGTERM, then resume) needs them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-45-- M5 is bounded by serial inference on the single gateway host.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-46-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-50-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-51-- M2, M4;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:52:- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-53-- the stripping proxy and the conformance fixtures.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-54-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-60-| G1 | End of M1 | All safety acceptance IDs pass in CI. Existing PTY suites stay green. No new skipped tests. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-61-| G2 | End of M2 | A package smoke run in a PTY shows the TUI. The doc-command test passes. Release dry-run assets are complete. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:62:| G3 | End of M3 | Continuity, inference and verification acceptance IDs pass. The eval harness self-tests pass, including the T4 smoke. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-63-| G4 | End of M4 | Persistence acceptance IDs pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-64-| G5 | After the RC | ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 pass. The DEC-05 thresholds are met. Independent reports are filed. |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-78-| Risk | Effect | Mitigation |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-79-|---|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:80:| The DEC-01 default change breaks many test fixtures | M1 takes longer | PR-1a lands the classes behind a constant; PR-1b flips the default with mechanical fixture updates |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-81-| The gateway host is unavailable or thermally limited during M5 | M5 is delayed | Serial runs with resumable runner; schedule against the thermal-soak findings; T2 runs are resumable per task |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:82:| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-83-| Parser restriction (PLAN-11) lowers the tool-call rate on text-only models | Task quality falls | Recorded fixtures; one-RC escape hatch; the qualification measures it |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-84-| Independent reviewer is unavailable (X5) | G5 cannot be met honestly | The owner must supply a reviewer. The audit does not substitute self-assessment for it. |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-93-- the memory measurements.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md-94-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\n--\neval/README.md-51-| Field | Meaning |\neval/README.md-52-|---|---|\neval/README.md:53:| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\neval/README.md-54-| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\neval/README.md-55-| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\neval/README.md-56-| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\neval/README.md:57:| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\neval/README.md-58-| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\neval/README.md-59-| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n--\neval/README.md-81-  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\neval/README.md-82-\neval/README.md:83:## Fault injection (T4)\neval/README.md-84-\neval/README.md:85:A task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\neval/README.md-86-chat request (counted from 1):\neval/README.md-87-\neval/README.md:88:| kind | Fault |\neval/README.md-89-|---|---|\neval/README.md-90-| `refuse` | The connection drops without an answer |\n--\neval/README.md-95-| `malformed_tool_json` | The first tool call's arguments are no longer valid JSON |\neval/README.md-96-\neval/README.md:97:What was injected is recorded in `model.faultsInjected`. Such runs are never treated as infrastructure reruns.\neval/README.md:98:`score.mjs` reports, per fault kind:\neval/README.md-99-\neval/README.md-100-- runs;\n--\neval/README.md-104-- hung past budget.\neval/README.md-105-\neval/README.md:106:The remaining T4 classes come from task fixtures (a hanging test…4088 tokens truncated…ug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-155-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-156-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-158-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-160-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-161-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-189-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-191-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-193-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:194:For each terminal × size, check:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-195-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-196-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-199-4. Resize during streaming.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-200-5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:201:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-202-7. NO_COLOR.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-203-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:204:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-205-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-206-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-210-Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-211-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:212:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-213-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-214-- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-215-- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-216-- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:217:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-218-- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-219-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-231-  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-232-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-234-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-236-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-237-1. refused connection mid-turn\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-245-9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-246-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:247:### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-248-\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-249-- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-253-| Metric | Gate |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-254-|---|---|\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-256-| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-257-| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-258-| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-259-| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-262-| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-263-| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-306-   - ACC-PKG-01;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-307-   - 5 random T2 tasks;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:308:   - 2 T4 classes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:309:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-310-3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-311-\n--\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-331-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-332-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:333:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:334:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-335-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-336-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-337-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-338-- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-340-  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-342-- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-344-- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-345-\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1779e-a8db-7503-bc94-b7b09b7a2beb","create_time":1793008522.3551772}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
