{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:01:03.378Z","ordinal":382144,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-888b91e0-d43c-4713-a3a7-ccab9c7b6039","process_id":"14996","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '125,160p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; sed -n '20,60p' docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md; rg -n 'nvidia/nemotron|OpenRouter.*pinned|pinned.*OpenRouter' docs/v1.0.0 docs/releases eval | head -50"],"cwd":"file:///var/tmp/nexus-main-e9304b1c-validation","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '125,160p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '20,60p' docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md","name":"EVIDENCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'nvidia/nemotron|OpenRouter.*pinned|pinned.*OpenRouter' docs/v1.0.0 docs/releases eval","query":"nvidia/nemotron|OpenRouter.*pinned|pinned.*OpenRouter","path":"v1.0.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n| Item | Identity |\n|---|---|\n| Source | `db1ca55`. Exported with `git archive` to `<scratch>/snap` (non-git), and separately cloned to `<scratch>/clone`, checked out at `db1ca55`. |\n| Toolchain | node v24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, cargo/rustc 1.95.0 (2026-03/04), Ubuntu with kernel 6.8.0-142, glibc 2.39, Intel Xeon X5650 (12 threads), 46 GB RAM |\n| `harness-core` (release build from HEAD) | sha256 `cbea89b952c923a2f41529a7b13374a6e60b60c151b9ed9e4aaaead33101112f`. Identical in the snap and clone builds. |\n| `nexus-tui` (release build from HEAD) | sha256 `17bc19f69a154ceeab5c4bee01b1ed69462545d878e3d52f4c097086ab3641da`. Identical in the snap and clone builds. |\n| Checkout `cli/dist` | `node cli/dist/index.js --version` gives `0.1.0-alpha.2 (db1ca5580860, main)`. It is byte-identical to a fresh build, except the untracked `build-info.json` (E §4). |\n| Published package used for installer checks | `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (`a2e94f3`). Assets: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v0.1.0-alpha.2.tar.gz` and `SHA256SUMS`. Installed in scratch HOMEs, plus the operator's existing `~/.local/lib/nexus/v0.1.0-alpha.2` (read only). |\n| Live cloud client | Checkout build `db1ca55` (`/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/dist`), using the operator's existing provider connections: ChatGPT via the Codex CLI sign-in; OpenRouter via the crush credential. |\n\n## 2. Baseline build and test runs\n\n| Run | Environment | Commands | Outcome | Archive |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `<scratch>/snap` (non-git export) | `npm ci`, `cargo test --locked`, `npm run build`, `npm test`, `security_gates.sh`, `cargo build --release` (that order), 09:34–10:01 UTC | Rust 266/266 pass. CLI 893/905: **12 failures, all environmental**. The PTY suites ran before the release binary existed (failing in about 5 ms each). The git-dependent tests had no `.git`. The security gate failed on `git diff` outside a repository. | `evidence/baseline/baseline.log` |\n| B2 | `<scratch>/clone` (git, `db1ca55`), CI order: release build before CLI tests | `npm ci`; build; `cargo test --locked`; `cargo build --locked --release --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui`; `npm test`; `security_gates.sh`, 12:42–13:06 UTC | **Rust 266/266, CLI 905/905, security gates PASS**, working tree clean afterwards. CLI suite duration 1,169 s. | `evidence/baseline/baseline2.log` |\n| CI (historical, read only) | GitHub Actions run 38540767677 | — | 905/905. Real `cargo audit` ran (1,310 advisories, 152 crates). | E §4 |\n\n**What this proves:** the code at `db1ca55` passes its own suites when run in CI order.\n\n**What it does not prove:** that the suites cover the defects listed in AUDIT §5. Most of those defects pass the existing suites.\n\n## 3. Live runs (owner-authorized small spend, 2026-10-14, on `db1ca55`)\n\n| Run | Command | Result | Request ids | Archive |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 | `nexus providers verify --provider chatgpt -m gpt-6-luna -j` | PASS: streamed completion, tool call, tool-result round trip | `8e910140…`, `1e6c5946…`, `d8595745…` | `evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json` |\n| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\n| L3 | Throwaway git repo with a broken `add` and a `node:test` test. `NEXUS_PROVIDER=chatgpt NEXUS_MODEL=gpt-6-luna nexus run \"...fix it so the existing test passes. Do not modify the test.\"` | `TASK COMPLETED - VERIFIED (npm test)`. The fix is correct and the test is unmodified, so the label is truthful. It took 7 requests, 83,331 input and 376 output tokens, 18 s. The run also showed: `npm test` executed without approval (SEC-01/VER-01 confirmed live); `.nexus/` left untracked in the workspace (PER-06); `context_limit=65536 (client_default)` (PRV-06b). | see log | `evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log` |\n\nNo request was sent to the homelab gateway. All other inference behaviour in this package comes from mocks and fixtures (B §4, D, A2) or from historical records (labelled HIST).\n\n## 4. Scoped audit evidence\n\n| File | Scope | Notable runs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `evidence/A_core_agent.md` | Agent loop, continuity | `repro/agt_repro.test.ts` (R1, R2, R4) |\n| `evidence/A2_verification.md` | Parser, verifier, tokens | `a2probe/{parser,tester,tokens,stager}_probe.ts`; 8 targeted test files (53/54; the 1 failure is environmental) |\n| `evidence/B_providers.md` | Providers and inference | `prv/{probe,tls,err}.mts` against 127.0.0.1 mocks; 125/125 targeted tests |\n| `evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md` | Tools, security, persistence | harness-core path-jail calls; classifier probes (`probes/p1.mjs`); SSRF probe (`probes/p2.mjs`); orphan test; memory measurements; read-only stat of `~/.nexus` |\n| `evidence/D_terminal.md` + `evidence/D_pty/` | Terminal | Real-PTY scripts s1–s9 and r1a–r1d against `mockgw.py`; `pyte` screen dumps |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:372:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:423:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json:33:      \"effectiveModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:3:  \"model\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:32:      \"selectedModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:33:      \"effectiveModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:55:      \"selectedModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:56:      \"effectiveModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:78:      \"selectedModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json:79:      \"effectiveModel\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":87439180}},"started_at_ms":1793008862290,"completed_at_ms":1793008863378}}
