directory)\n17-  -s, --max-steps <number>                     Steps per segment; continuation checkpoints there instead of stopping (default: 30)\n--\n25-  --fallback <urls>                            Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if primary is unavailable\n26:  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n27-  --dry-run                                    Simulate file modifications without writing changes to disk\n28:  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n29-  --worktree                                   Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n30-  --authoritative-verifier <command>           Trusted command that must pass before any task completion; its success may authorize automatic worktree merge\n31:  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n32:  --record-flight                              Record execution into an append-only deterministic .flightlog\n33:  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n34:  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n35:  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical code implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n36:  --coder-endpoint <url>                       Dedicated inference endpoint for coder model\n37:  --provider <id>                              Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\n38:  --base-url <url>                             Override the provider's base URL (operator-only; required for 'compatible')\n39:  --planner-provider <id>                      Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\n40:  --coder-provider <id>                        Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\n41-  -h, --help                                   display help for command\n--\n44-  repl [options]                               Start interactive coding session (REPL / TUI)\n45:  run [options] [prompt...]                    Run an autonomous coding task\n46:  models [options]                             List loaded models from your local LM Studio or vLLM server\n47-  doctor [options]                             Diagnose configuration, endpoint, credentials, engine, shell, state and extensions without starting an agent\n--\n53-  plugins [options]                            List loaded custom plugins and lifecycle hooks\n54:  trust [options] [path]                       Trust a workspace so its own .mcp.json servers and plugins are loaded (they run code from the workspace)\n55:  checkpoints [options]                        List saved workspace snapshots and rollback checkpoints\n56-  audit [options]                              Inspect tool execution audit log and execution metrics\n--\n66-  operation                                    [experimental] Convergence-scheduled multi-unit operations (reroute, park, wait, resume)\n67:  connect [options] <provider>                 Connect a cloud provider: save an API key (verified first) or sign in\n68:  disconnect <provider>                        Remove the credential Nexus saved for a provider (environment and other clients are untouched)\n69:  providers                                    List cloud inference providers, credential status and the selected destinations\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":903261919}},"started_at_ms":1793009146465,"completed_at_ms":1793009147369}}
