{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:15:17.836Z","ordinal":382646,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a177b5-124c-7f30-9174-f60839451990","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2641)\nTotal output lines: 108\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...392 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-26 10:15am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (16,022t read) | 101,522t work | 84% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1692 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session investigating missing startup feature while monitoring active CI runs for post-PR177 main and PR #175 (Oct 23, 11:17 PM)\nS1693 User set approval mode to \"Default to review\" — session continuing RC.4 release gate monitoring (Oct 23, 11:19 PM)\nS1694 RC.4 release gate monitoring — CI status check on main and PR #175 while holding CR bypass blocker (Oct 23, 11:21 PM)\nS1701 RC.4 release gate session recovery — assess PR #175 CR bypass blocker and CI status across main and PR #175 branches (Oct 23, 11:22 PM)\nS1707 RC.4 release gate — monitoring CI for PR #175 (CR bypass fix needed) and main branch while holding merge pending blocker resolution (Oct 23, 11:25 PM)\nS1709 RC.4 release gate — PR #175 CR bypass fix blocked on safe-boundary handoff; monitoring main CI while waiting for claim transfer confirmation (Oct 23, 11:26 PM)\nS1718 Kimi agent handover for agent.ts — monitoring CI for PR #240 refreshed branch while main CI run 40227786412 completes (Oct 23, 11:30 PM)\n### Oct 25, 2026\nS1723 Kimi agent waiting for agent.ts handover — PR #240 REPL checkpoint failure recovery review and CI monitoring (Oct 25, 8:05 PM)\nS1730 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error from nexus upgrade, and relationship to checkpoint fix shipped in RC7 (Oct 25, 8:36 PM)\n22273 9:47p ○ RC7 File Claim Confirmed — docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md Claimed by codex-root on rc7-version-bump Branch\n22339 \" ○ RC7 Worktree — PR #241 Not Found on v1/rc7-version-bump Branch, cli/node_modules Missing\n22275 \" ○ RC7 Worktree Confirmed Active — HEAD at f28861a, No Other Agent Modifying Release Files\n22278 9:48p ○ PR #239 Terminal Controls Fix Confirmed — safeTerminal Applied to Token Stream and Task Prompt in agent.ts\n22340 \" ○ repl_checkpoint_choices.test.ts — 5/5 Tests Pass on RC7 Worktree HEAD\n22279 \" ✓ RC7 Release Notes Provenance Bullet Refined — Added NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION Detail and Validation Behavior\n22280 \" ✓ RC7 Release Notes Refinement Committed as Separate Commit — Branch Now 2 Ahead of Main\n22341 \" ○ v1/rc7-version-bump Branch Not Yet