Do not modify Nexus source”, “use a scratch copy”, “If something is wrong, REPORT IT”, and preserve the operator’s dirty tree -> isolate builds/tests, preserve negative results, and report rather than remediate. [Task 1]\n192:# Task Group: Nexus architecture reconnaissance and context-engineering baseline\n193:scope: Strictly read-only mapping of Nexus information/context flow, durable state, admission, and validation; use when the requested deliverable is an architecture investigation rather than remediation or design work.\n194:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code (rollout metadata cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost); reuse_rule=capture exact snapshot and concurrent-change risk; do not reuse `2860228` observations as current-state facts without rechecking.\n196:## Task 1: Capture baseline for the intended A-I Nexus architecture reconnaissance, incomplete\n204:- Nexus, read-only, architecture reconnaissance, context-engineering, CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md, 2860228, linear transcript resend, context admission, deterministic compaction, durable session state, no context router\n208:- for Nexus reconnaissance, the user required “read-only” and “do not modify source, tests, configuration, documentation, dependencies, Git state” -> preserve scope, record exact snapshot SHA plus concurrent-change risk, and do not implement optimization or prove a preferred theory. [Task 1]\n213:- At inspection, `/home/mike/nexus-code` was `main` `2860228cb84166d0295961587ad4934184165bd0` with substantial uncommitted concurrent documentation/Cloudflare changes. The existing `docs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md` was the first high-yield source. [Task 1]\n220:# Task Group: Nexus live Ratatui TUI review and redaction/observer isolation\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28935}},"started_at_ms":1793009730471,"completed_at_ms":1793009730472}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:15:42.255Z","ordinal":382654,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a177b5-71af-7951-bd6c-1c2506107f41","call_id":"call_25f6c273bd1f477aa2a7a00097bcdf3d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 13.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__observation_search\",\"description\":\"Search generated observations by keyword (Postgres full-text) and, when the server has search by meaning (pgvector, CLAUDE_MEM_SERVER_VECTOR_SEARCH), by meaning (embedding similarity), fused by reciprocal rank. A natural-language question works. Search by meaning has no relevance cutoff, so it always returns the nearest matches; keyword-only search returns only observations containing a query term. Calls /v1/search. Server runtime only. Params: query (required), projectId (optional), platformSource, limit (default 20, max 100). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__observation_search(args: {\\n  // Max results (default 20, max 100)\\n  limit?: number;\\n  // Optional platform source filter, e.g. claude, codex, cursor\\n  platformSource?: string;\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  // Search query (required)\\n  query: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__save_memory\",\"description\":\"Save an explicit durable note, decision, correction or handoff into worker-mode claude-mem. Use this for your own note taking after searching memory for duplicates. Include project when the note belongs to a specific project. Server runtime uses observation_add to write to the selected server. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__save_memory(args: {\\n  // Optional provenance or source metadata.\\n  metadata?: { [key: string]: unknown; };\\n  // Project receiving the note; defaults to the active checkout.\\n  project?: string;\\n  // Durable memory text.\\n  text: string;\\n  // Concise searchable title.\\n  title?: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read\",\"description\":\"Read this project's to-do lists and working state written with work_state_write: every open item, or one list, with done and dropped items when includeClosed is true. Params: list, includeClosed. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read(args: {\\n  // Also show done and dropped items and closed lists\\n  includeClosed?: boolean;\\n  // Read only this list\\n  list?: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write\",\"description\":\"Your canonical to-do list and working state for this project, kept across sessions: whatever is still open is shown at the start of every session. Each call appends one entry to a list. To-do item: fields {\\\"task\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"todo\\\" | \\\"doing\\\" | \\\"done\\\" | \\\"dropped\\\", ...details}. State on the list itself: any other fields (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\" closes the list). Returns what is still open in the list. Params: list (required), fields (required). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write(args: {\\n  // Keys to set. Include \\\"task\\\" to update a to-do item. Values are strings, numbers, booleans, or null to clear a key.\\n  fields: { [key: string]: string | number | boolean | null; };\\n  // The to-do list or tracked thing this entry belongs to, e.g. \\\"release\\\" or \\\"auth-refactor\\\"\\n  list: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}]"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1:# Task Group: Nexus Code client release and Cloudflare contest publ