{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:22:36.561Z","ordinal":382952,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf29e8885881a0bef08d5b5e61e404","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The signed redirect was the cause. **Correction to what I said earlier:** your screenshot shows **RC6** running the upgrade command, so RC6’s updater rejected GitHub’s signed asset URL while trying to download RC7. It was not RC7’s check.\n\nPR #248 fixes that redirect handling, and its merge is included in RC8’s source. That does **not** fix the already-running RC6 updater: it still uses RC6’s code. The first move to RC8 therefore needs the verified standalone RC8 installer; after RC8 is installed, its updater has the fix. I have not changed or verified the installation on mike-dev. Any GitHub CLI sign-in needed for the installer must be on mike-dev itself; signing in on ubuntu-desktop does not carry over.\n\nRelease work continues:\n\n- PR #253 merged as `1434a93`. Its exact-head CI, Linux reproducible packaging, CodeQL, and independent review passed. Post-merge CodeQL passed; main CI is still running.\n- PR #252 is rebased onto that merge at `561b8d1`, independently accepted, and diff-check clean. It remains local until main CI finishes; then I’ll push it and run exact-head checks.\n- Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC8 is still a prerelease; held-out custody, live-task completion, the human terminal matrix, and exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\nThe signed URL you pasted was short-lived and has expired; I have not repeated or recorded its signature.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":27,"lineEnd":29,"note":"used the established evidence-bound release reporting preference"},{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":42,"lineEnd":42,"note":"used the requirement to distinguish installer success from product acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":["01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15"]}},"started_at_ms":1793010152565,"completed_at_ms":1793010156561}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:22:36.579Z","ordinal":382953,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf29e8885881a0bef08d5b5e61e404","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The signed redirect was the cause. **Correction to what I said earlier:** your screenshot shows **RC6** running the upgrade command, so RC6’s updater rejected GitHub’s signed asset URL while trying to download RC7. It was not RC7’s check.\n\nPR #248 fixes that redirect handling, and its merge is included in RC8’s source. That does **not** fix the already-running RC6 updater: it still uses RC6’s code. The first move to RC8 therefore needs the verified standalone RC8 installer; after RC8 is installed, its updater has the fix. I have not changed or verified the installation on mike-dev. Any GitHub CLI sign-in needed for the installer must be on mike-dev itself; signing in on ubuntu-desktop does not carry over.\n\nRelease work continues:\n\n- PR #253 merged as `1434a93`. Its exact-head CI, Linux reproducible packaging, CodeQL, and independent review passed. Post-merge CodeQL passed; main CI is still running.\n- PR #252 is rebased onto that merge at `561b8d1`, independently accepted, and diff-check clean. It remains local until main CI finishes; then I’ll push it and run exact-head checks.\n- Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC8 is still a prerelease; held-out custody, live-task completion, the human terminal matrix, and exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\nThe signed URL you pasted was short-lived and has expired; I have not repeated or recorded its signature.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:27-29|note=[used the established evidence-bound release reporting preference]\nMEMORY.md:42-42|note=[used the requirement to distinguish installer success from product acceptance]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","create_time":1793010152.53428,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf29e8885881a0bef08d5b5e61e404","turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a177bb-c423-7c52-9acd-f75dfd2d87e9","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":18774}}
