{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:23:11.419Z","ordinal":382956,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","last_agent_message":"The signed redirect was the cause. **Correction to what I said earlier:** your screenshot shows **RC6** running the upgrade command, so RC6’s updater rejected GitHub’s signed asset URL while trying to download RC7. It was not RC7’s check.\n\nPR #248 fixes that redirect handling, and its merge is included in RC8’s source. That does **not** fix the already-running RC6 updater: it still uses RC6’s code. The first move to RC8 therefore needs the verified standalone RC8 installer; after RC8 is installed, its updater has the fix. I have not changed or verified the installation on mike-dev. Any GitHub CLI sign-in needed for the installer must be on mike-dev itself; signing in on ubuntu-desktop does not carry over.\n\nRelease work continues:\n\n- PR #253 merged as `1434a93`. Its exact-head CI, Linux reproducible packaging, CodeQL, and independent review passed. Post-merge CodeQL passed; main CI is still running.\n- PR #252 is rebased onto that merge at `561b8d1`, independently accepted, and diff-check clean. It remains local until main CI finishes; then I’ll push it and run exact-head checks.\n- Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC8 is still a prerelease; held-out custody, live-task completion, the human terminal matrix, and exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\nThe signed URL you pasted was short-lived and has expired; I have not repeated or recorded its signature.\n\n","started_at":1793008694,"completed_at":1793010191,"duration_ms":1496600,"time_to_first_token_ms":1744}}
