{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:26:26.445Z","ordinal":383078,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a177bc-4c48-78b2-bd13-305610903c0a","turn_id":"01a177bc-4c48-78b2-bd13-305610903c0a","last_agent_message":"**The RC6 updater rejected the signed GitHub asset redirect.** I need to correct my earlier explanation: the screenshot shows RC6 running the command to upgrade to RC7, so RC6’s code performed the rejecting check. PR #248 adds support for that redirect and is included in RC8, but the old RC6 updater can’t use code from the version it is trying to install. The RC6-to-RC7 attempt failed after backup; I have not verified or changed mike-dev’s installation.\n\n**Release progress:** PR #253 merged as `1434a93`. Its exact-head CI, Linux reproducible packaging, CodeQL, and independent review passed. Post-merge CodeQL passed; main’s Node 22 and 24 CI jobs are still running. PR #252 is rebased on `1434a93` and independently accepted at `561b8d1`; I’ll push it and start exact-head checks after main CI finishes.\n\n**Terminal matrix:** Ubuntu has RC8 installed in its isolated qualification location, all five required terminal apps, the harness, and an output directory. No evidence cells are recorded yet. SSH has no graphical display, so the 15 interactive runs and screenshots must be done from the Ubuntu desktop.\n\nFor each terminal and size, run the harness in that terminal after resizing it:\n\n```sh\n~/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh \\\n  --rc v1.0.0-rc.8 \\\n  --terminal xterm \\\n  --size 80x24 \\\n  --out ~/.local/share/nexus-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.8/terminal/evidence\n```\n\nRepeat for xterm, kitty with its keyboard protocol enabled, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code’s integrated terminal, and GNOME Terminal at `80x24`, `40x14`, and `200x60`. The harness prompts for the seven checks and screenshot paths. The full procedure is in [ACCEPTANCE.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/upgrade-tui-contaminat