{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:40:18.813Z","ordinal":383502,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177c2-7b4a-7152-ba84-5c8470f48393","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf2e11da9481a093af0abdb8f1b8fc","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"While the main suites run, I found two open medium CodeQL alerts in a test fixture: it builds child-process JavaScript by interpolating temporary file paths into `node -e` scripts. The paths are generated locally, but the fixture can avoid source construction entirely. I’m taking an isolated, file-scoped claim, changing the fixture to use script files and arguments, then I’ll hold its tests until SUITE is free."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793011217885,"completed_at_ms":1793011218812}}
