{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:08.507Z","ordinal":383648,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177c2-7b4a-7152-ba84-5c8470f48393","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-26e3565b-9aa1-44d6-a813-1066ac9387a7","process_id":"37174","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git ls-tree -r --name-only v1.0.0-rc.8 | rg 'install|release|README|UPGRADE' | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git ls-tree -r --name-only v1.0.0-rc.8 | rg 'install|release|README|UPGRADE' | head -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":".github/release.yml\n.github/workflows/release.yml\nREADME.md\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md\ndocs/releases/rulesets/protected-branches.json\ndocs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.1.md\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus-dogfooding-2026-10-03/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/parallel-defect-investigation-2026-10-04/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-AUTHORIZATION-REDACTION-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CHECKPOINT-STATE-INJECTION-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-DOCTOR-UNREADABLE-STATE-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-FILE-INFO-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-GIT-EXCLUDE-SUBSTRING-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-HTML-CONTROL-INJECTION-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-PARSER-COMMA-CORRUPTION-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-PARSER-MIXED-QUOTES-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-SYMLINK-CONFINEMENT-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RECOVER-WORKTREE-CONVERSATION-20261026/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-REPL-READONLY-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CHECKPOINT-PATH-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RUNNER-BACKGROUND-STARTUP-EXIT-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-SSRF-IPV6-CONNECT-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-TAR-AMBIENT-ENV-20261024/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-TAR-SYMLINK-TRAVERSAL-20261023/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UI-TERMINAL-INJECTION-20261025/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_AGT111_V1_CLOSURE/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_JOURNAL_COMPLEXITY_RECOVERY/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_BASELINE/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_SPLIT/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_COMPANIONS/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RMW_TRANSACTION_RECOVERY/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_COMPONENT_COHERENCE/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/public-release-identities.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/release_snapshot_2026-10-16.json\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md\neval/README.md\neval/host/README.md\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/README.md\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/install.sh\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/normalize-install.py\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/post-install-qualify.py\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/test-install-python-boundary.py\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/verify-install.py\nexperiments/routing-b1-b2-2026-10-03/README.md\nexperiments/thermal-soak-2026-10-03/README.CORRECTION.txt\nexperiments/thermal-soak-2026-10-03/README.md\nexperiments/thermal-soak-2026-10-03/policy-replay/README.md\ninstall.sh\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh\nscripts/release-tools/package-lock.json\nscripts/release-tools/package.json\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30680}},"started_at_ms":1793011388506,"completed_at_ms":1793011388507}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:08.654Z","ordinal":383649,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177c2-7b4a-7152-ba84-5c8470f48393","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dfbef5df-5326-40e2-85d6-ce2921d825ad","process_id":"88387","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show v1.0.0-rc.8:README.md | rg -n -C 2 'install|upgrade|release' | head -70; git show v1.0.0-rc.8:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md | sed -n '1,140p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show v1.0.0-rc.8:README.md | rg -n -C 2 'install|upgrade|release' | head -70; git show v1.0.0-rc.8:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md | sed -n '1,140p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"5-## Choose a path\n6-\n7:- **[Install and use Nexus Code](quickstart.md)** — supported platform, one-line installer, configuration, and first task.\n8-- **[Read the historical Cloudflare contest entry](docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md)** — the collaboration service built with Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts, its source map, and judge guide.\n9-\n10-The contest has concluded. Its submission was the agent-collaboration service; Nexus Code is the separate client and harness used to demonstrate it.\n11-\n12:## Install Nexus Code\n13-\n14:The unversioned installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, it exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag. To install a prerelease or pin a version, use the tag shown on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases) and set `NEXUS_VERSION`; see the [quickstart](quickstart.md).\n15-\n16-```sh\n17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n18-```\n19-\n20:This follows the latest stable release and installs the Linux x86-64 package under your home directory. The installer verifies its SHA-256 checksum and requires Node.js 22 or newer. To pin a specific version or install a prerelease, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to that release's tag. See [release status and platform requirements](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md).\n21-\n22-## Build and contribute\n23-\n24:See [development and release procedures](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md), [client guide](docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md), [provider setup](docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md), and the [contest entry](docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md).\n25-\n26-The client sources are in `cli/` and `core/`. The Cloudflare service and fixture are in `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/`; demo orchestration is in `demo/`.\n--\n28-## Community and project policies\n29-\n30:Read the [contribution guide](CONTRIBUTING.md), [support channels](SUPPORT.md), [security policy](SECURITY.md), [governance](GOVERNANCE.md), and [code of conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Track changes in [releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases); development plans do not establish release readiness.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\n\n## Changes since RC7\n\n- **Checkpoint safety:** checkpoint creation now detects a present or unreadable Git index lock before publishing a checkpoint reference, and reports why it stopped. It rechecks the lock after validation and stash creation so a concurrent Git operation is less likely to publish a stale checkpoint.\n- **Read-only mode consistency:** the effective permission posture is applied consistently when an agent and its workspace extensions start or change modes. A temporary checkpoint-safety fallback stays separate from the configured mode, allowing recovery without silently changing the operator's selected mode.\n- **Recovered operation continuity:** recovered operation context is retained across session restoration, while prior verifier baselines remain untrusted and require fresh verification before a recovered result can be treated as verified.\n- **Upgrade reliability:** GitHub release downloads now follow its signed release-asset redirect without forwarding GitHub credentials to the asset host. Large pre-migration backups report aggregate progress and avoid redundant directory syncs while retaining file and directory durability.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":39453}},"started_at_ms":1793011388653,"completed_at_ms":1793011388654}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:08.707Z","ordinal":383650,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177c2-7b4a-7152-ba84-5c8470f48393","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b7796420-66cd-4882-9ce0-fa19a0e25ec4","process_id":"26281","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show v1.0.0-rc.8:cli/src/upgrade.ts | sed -n '620,742p'; git show v1.0.0-rc.8:docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md | rg -n -C 3 'install|curl|bootstrap|release-assets|upgrade'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show v1.0.0-rc.8:cli/src/upgrade.ts | sed -n '620,742p'; git show v1.0.0-rc.8:docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md | rg -n -C 3 'install|curl|bootstrap|release-assets|upgrade'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"// Download, Verification, and Atomic Installation\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nexport function validateDownloadUrl(urlString: string): boolean {\n  let parsed: URL;\n  try {\n    parsed = new URL(urlString);\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  // Reject URLs with embedded credentials (user:pass@...)\n  if (parsed.username || parsed.password) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const hostname = parsed.hostname.toLowerCase();\n\n  // Test / override environments: allow custom release base URL or releases API host\n  const customBase = process.env.NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL || process.env.NEXUS_RELEASES_URL || process.env.NEXUS_RELEASES_API;\n  if (customBase) {\n    try {\n      const customParsed = new URL(customBase);\n      if (hostname === customParsed.hostname.toLowerCase()) {\n        if (parsed.protocol === \"https:\" || parsed.protocol === \"http:\") {\n          return true;\n        }\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  // Localhost allowed for local mock testing\n  if (hostname === \"127.0.0.1\" || hostname === \"localhost\") {\n    return parsed.protocol === \"http:\" || parsed.protocol === \"https:\";\n  }\n\n  // GitHub allowed domains - must be HTTPS\n  if (parsed.protocol !== \"https:\") {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  if (hostname === \"github.com\") {\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(`/${CANONICAL_REPO}/releases/download/`);\n  }\n\n  if (hostname === \"objects.githubusercontent.com\") {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  // GitHub now redirects release downloads to its signed release-assets host.\n  // Restrict the path to release objects; never allow this host as a generic CDN.\n  if (hostname === \"release-assets.githubusercontent.com\") {\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(\"/github-production-release-asset/\");\n  }\n\n  return false;\n}\n\n/** Release redirects can contain short-lived signed query parameters; diagnostics expose only the origin. */\nfunction safeDownloadOrigin(urlString: string): string {\n  try {\n    return new URL(urlString).origin;\n  } catch {\n    return \"invalid URL\";\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function downloadFile(\n  url: string,\n  destPath: string,\n  signal?: AbortSignal,\n  timeoutMs = 60000,\n  maxHops = 5\n): Promise<void> {\n  let currentUrl = url;\n  let hops = 0;\n\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n  const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(new Error(`Download timed out after ${timeoutMs}ms`)), timeoutMs);\n  if (signal) {\n    signal.addEventListener(\"abort\", () => controller.abort(signal.reason), { once: true });\n  }\n\n  try {\n    while (hops <= maxHops) {\n      if (!validateDownloadUrl(currentUrl)) {\n        throw new Error(`Disallowed download origin or invalid URL (${safeDownloadOrigin(currentUrl)})`);\n      }\n\n      const headers: Record<string, string> = { \"User-Agent\": \"nexus-upgrade\" };\n      const token = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN || process.env.GH_TOKEN;\n      if (token && (new URL(currentUrl)).hostname === \"github.com\") {\n        headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;\n      }\n\n      const res = await fetch(currentUrl, {\n        headers,\n        signal: controller.signal,\n        redirect: \"manual\",\n      });\n\n      // Handle redirect\n      if (res.status === 301 || res.status === 302 || res.status === 307 || res.status === 308) {\n        const location = res.headers.get(\"location\");\n        if (!location) {\n          throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status} redirect without Location header from ${safeDownloadOrigin(currentUrl)}`);\n        }\n        currentUrl = new URL(location, currentUrl).toString();\n        hops++;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      if (!res.ok) {\n        throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status} downloading from ${safeDownloadOrigin(currentUrl)}`);\n      }\n\n      const contentLengthHeader = res.headers.get(\"content-length\");\n      if (contentLengthHeader) {\n        const contentLength = parseInt(contentLengthHeader, 10);\n        if (contentLength > MAX_DOWNLOAD_BYTES) {\n          throw new Error(`Download size (${contentLength} bytes) exceeds maximum allowed limit (${MAX_DOWNLOAD_BYTES} bytes)`);\n        }\n      }\n1:# Nexus Code Upgrade Security & Publisher Authenticity Assessment\n2-\n3-## 1. Executive Summary\n4-\n5:This document establishes the trust boundaries, security controls, and cryptographic authenticity architecture for the `nexus upgrade` and `/upgrade` update engine introduced in Nexus Code v1.0.0 (Workstream 12, REQ-REL-115, REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-07..14).\n6-\n7-## 2. Trust Boundaries & Threat Model\n8-\n9:The self-upgrade mechanism enables operators to update their active Nexus installation to newer (or pinned) published releases directly from the CLI or TUI. Because executable updates run with the user's execution privileges and can replace core harness and TUI binaries, rigorous boundary enforcement is mandatory:\n10-\n11-### In-Scope Threats\n12-\n13-1. **Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) & Transport Tampering**:\n14-   - Attackers attempting to modify binaries in transit or redirect downloads to malicious hosts.\n15-2. **Path Traversal & Archive Extraction Vulnerabilities**:\n16:   - Malicious release archives attempting to write outside the isolated installation directory via `../` path traversal, absolute paths, escaping symlinks, devices, or hardlinks.\n17-3. **Resource Exhaustion & Tar Bombs**:\n18-   - Download streams or archive contents engineered to consume unbounded disk space or memory.\n19-4. **State & Migration Incompatibility**:\n20-   - Downgrading to older binaries that corrupt newer configuration or task persistence schemas.\n21:5. **Partial Switch / Crash Mid-Installation**:\n22-   - System failure or termination during package replacement leaving the system without an executable binary.\n23-6. **Package Manager Collision**:\n24:   - Accidental overwriting of installations managed by OS package managers (e.g. `apt`, `brew`, `npm`).\n25-7. **PATH Shadowing**:\n26-   - Updating `$PREFIX/bin/nexus` while an unmanaged or stale `nexus` binary earlier in `$PATH` continues to execute.\n27-\n--\n57-- Legacy public releases lacking `compatibility.json` are permitted under an explicit legacy policy with an advisory notice.\n58-\n59-### 3.4 Durable Provenance & Destination Verification (ACC-UPG-10)\n60:- The installer and updater write `.provenance.json` (mode 0644) inside `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION`.\n61:- Managed installations are distinguished from development checkouts (`git pull && make build`) and package-manager distributions (`apt`, `brew`).\n62:- Self-upgrade refuses to overwrite package-manager installations, directing the user to their package manager.\n63-\n64-### 3.5 Pre-Migration Backups, Atomic Symlinks & Rollback (ACC-UPG-09, ACC-UPG-11)\n65-- Before modifying files, `createPreMigrationBackup` backs up `~/.config/nexus/config.env` (mode 0600) and complete durable state/configuration snapshots (excluding backup directories) to `~/.config/nexus/backups/` and `~/.nexus/backups/`.\n66-- Replacement occurs via atomic symlink swap:\n67-  - `ln -s $PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION/bin/nexus $PREFIX/bin/.nexus-link.$PID && mv -f ... $PREFIX/bin/nexus`\n68:- `--rollback-binary` safely rolls back the launcher symlink to the previous installed version in `$PREFIX/lib/nexus`.\n69-- `--restore-backup <path>` accepts a canonical plain `config.env.bak.*` file for configuration-only restoration, or a private `~/.nexus/backups/state-backup-*` directory containing `backup.json`, `state/`, and optional `config/` for complete snapshot restoration. It rejects arbitrary files, tar archives, and redirected paths.\n70-- Run backup restoration through the stable `nexus` launcher. Close existing legacy clients before retrying a pending restore, and keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. Current managed launches route through the journal before loading configuration; the Linux process census detects already-running legacy entry points, but cannot serialize a new direct launch from a version that predates the kernel lease. That offline interval is an explicit prerequisite of the supported restore boundary.\n71-\n72-### 3.6 Transaction Journal & Crash Recovery (ACC-UPG-11)\n73:- The updater logs state progression to `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade-journal.json`:\n74-  - `preparing` -> `downloading` -> `staged` -> `switching` -> `switched` -> `verified` -> `complete`\n75-- Idempotent recovery (`--recover` and automatic startup check):\n76-  - Crashes before switching: cleans staging directory, source version remains active.\n--\n98-         subject-path: 'nexus-linux-x86_64-*.tar.gz'\n99-     ```\n100-   - This produces an immutable, cryptographic in-toto attestation signed via Sigstore's Fulcio certificate authority and recorded in the Rekor transparency log, binding the binary to the repository, workflow, and commit SHA.\n101:   - The updater can verify this provenance using `gh attestation verify` (automated hook already provided in `cli/src/upgrade.ts`) or an embedded pure-JS Sigstore bundle verifier.\n102-\n103-2. **MiniSign / PGP Detached Signatures**:\n104-   - Release workflow signs `SHA256SUMS` with a dedicated release offline key:\n--\n108-\n109-### Post-review transaction recovery\n110-\n111:Replacement package backups are recorded before renaming as `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.rollback-<transaction-id>`, outside disposable staging. Same-version repairs retain the real previous package for explicit binary rollback. Journal writes and rename boundaries are flushed before reporting completion. Recovery validates the complete source runtime and only records `rolled_back` after restoring and verifying the installation/link. Failure retains staging and package artifacts under `recovery_required` and returns a nonzero operational error; it never reports successful rollback after a failed restore. A previously verified target may be finalized only after another complete runtime check.\n112-\n113-Package health probes use an isolated temporary home, bounded output/time, and process-group cleanup. New packages must report the exact product version from launcher, core, and TUI; the core help path and TUI snapshot render must also work. Historical alpha.1/alpha.2 exceptions are restricted to exact publicly checksummed component hashes: their core reports its historical 1.2.1 identity and their TUI predates `--version`. This exception is not permission for arbitrary component mismatch.\n114-\n115:Packaged CLI/TUI startup checks pending journals before normal execution. Explicit help/version, `upgrade --check`, and supervised health probes are read-only and do not recover. Active upgrade locks prevent concurrent recovery. Qualification from a real prior public release and manual terminal acceptance remain separate release gates; synthetic fault tests do not establish them.\n116-\n117-### Concurrent stale-lock reclamation\n118-\n119:When a recovery or upgrade observes a stale lock (dead holder PID), exactly one process may unlink and replace it. Serialization uses a permanent kernel-owned guard file `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade.lock.guard` (never unlinked or replaced; accepted only as a regular file owned by the running user with no group/other permission bits): the reclaimer holds an advisory `flock` on the file's open file description for the whole reclaim section, acquired through `/usr/bin/flock` (util-linux; Linux runtime prerequisite) with exit status 75 distinguishing contention. The kernel drops the lock when the last referring descriptor closes, so a reclaimer killed by SIGKILL or power loss releases automatically instead of wedging later upgrades. If the flock utility or filesystem is unavailable, acquisition fails closed with a manual-intervention error rather than proceeding unserialized.\n120-\n121-### Durable state store coordination (schema 2)\n122-\n123:Task and session progress files refer to separate append-only message journals. Backup and rollback acquire both permanent state-store guards in a fixed order while copying or restoring these components. Guard files are omitted from snapshots and their existing inodes survive restore, including cleanup of directories absent from an older snapshot. This uses the same kernel-owned file guard as upgrade stale-lock recovery; it does not introduce a stale directory lock or unlink live guard files.\n124-\n125-Close older clients before migration or rollback. Older versions cannot participate in schema 2 store locking. A new client requires util-linux `/usr/bin/flock` for state transactions and fails closed when it is unavailable. A busy store stops a snapshot instead of producing a mixed progress/message backup.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41514}},"started_at_ms":1793011388706,"completed_at_ms":1793011388707}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:43:11.030Z","ordinal":383651,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a177ce-9a36-7e10-8bfb-19f96294b399","call_id":"call_6ee17bf97fed4704a69e133493e95da5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"b9fb94\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000041514,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3136,\"output\":\"// Download, Verification, and Atomic Installation\\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nexport function validateDownloadUrl(urlString: string): boolean {\\n  let parsed: URL;\\n  try {\\n    parsed = new URL(urlString);\\n  } catch {\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  // Reject URLs with embedded credentials (user:pass@...)\\n  if (parsed.username || parsed.password) {\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  const hostname = parsed.hostname.toLowerCase();\\n\\n  // Test / override environments: allow custom release base URL or releases API host\\n  const customBase = process.env.NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL || process.env.NEXUS_RELEASES_URL || process.env.NEXUS_RELEASES_API;\\n  if (customBase) {\\n    try {\\n      const customParsed = new URL(customBase);\\n      if (hostname === customParsed.hostname.toLowerCase()) {\\n        if (parsed.protocol === \\\"https:\\\" || parsed.protocol === \\\"http:\\\") {\\n          return true;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    } catch {}\\n  }\\n\\n  // Localhost allowed for local mock testing\\n  if (hostname === \\\"127.0.0.1\\\" || hostname === \\\"localhost\\\") {\\n    return parsed.protocol === \\\"http:\\\" || parsed.protocol === \\\"https:\\\";\\n  }\\n\\n  // GitHub allowed domains - must be HTTPS\\n  if (parsed.protocol !== \\\"https:\\\") {\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  if (hostname === \\\"github.com\\\") {\\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(`/${CANONICAL_REPO}/releases/download/`);\\n  }\\n\\n  if (hostname === \\\"objects.githubusercontent.com\\\") {\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // GitHub now redirects release downloads to its signed release-assets host.\\n  // Restrict the path to release objects; never allow this host as a generic CDN.\\n  if (hostname === \\\"release-assets.githubusercontent.com\\\") {\\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(\\\"/github-production-release-asset/\\\");\\n  }\\n\\n  return false;\\n}\\n\\n/** Release redirects can contain short-lived signed query parameters; diagnostics expose only the origin. */\\nfunction safeDownloadOrigin(urlString: string): string {\\n  try {\\n    return new URL(urlString).origin;\\n  } catch {\\n    return \\\"invalid URL\\\";\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function downloadFile(\\n  url: string,\\n  destPath: string,\\n  signal?: AbortSignal,\\n  timeoutMs = 60000,\\n  maxHops = 5\\n): Promise<void> {\\n  let currentUrl = url;\\n  let hops = 0;\\n\\n  const controller = new AbortController();\\n  const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(new Error(`Download timed out after ${timeoutMs}ms`)), timeoutMs);\\n  if (signal) {\\n    signal.addEventListener(\\\"abort\\\", () => controller.abort(signal.reason), { once: true });\\n  }\\n\\n  try {\\n    while (hops <= maxHops) {\\n      if (!validateDownloadUrl(currentUrl)) {\\n        throw new Error(`Disallowed download origin or invalid URL (${safeDownloadOrigin(currentUrl)})`);\\n      }\\n\\n      const headers: Record<string, string> = { \\\"User-Agent\\\": \\\"nexus-upgrade\\\" };\\n      const token = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN || process.env.GH_TOKEN;\\n      if (token && (new URL(currentUrl)).hostname === \\\"github.com\\\") {\\n        headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;\\n      }\\n\\n      const res = await fetch(currentUrl, {\\n        headers,\\n        signal: controller.signal,\\n        redirect: \\\"manual\\\",\\n      });\\n\\n      // Handle redirect\\n      if (res.status === 301 || res.status === 302 || res.status === 307 || res.status === 308) {\\n        const location = res.headers.get(\\\"location\\\");\\n        if (!location) {\\n          throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status} redirect without Location header from ${safeDownloadOrigin(currentUrl)}`);\\n        }\\n        currentUrl = new URL(location, currentUrl).toString();\\n        hops++;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n\\n      if (!res.ok) {\\n        throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status} downloading from ${safeDownloadOrigin(currentUrl)}`);\\n      }\\n\\n      const contentLengthHeader = res.headers.get(\\\"content-length\\\");\\n      if (contentLengthHeader) {\\n        const contentLength = parseInt(contentLengthHeader, 10);\\n        if (contentLength > MAX_DOWNLOAD_BYTES) {\\n          throw new Error(`Download size (${contentLength} bytes) exceeds maximum allowed limit (${MAX_DOWNLOAD_BYTES} bytes)`);\\n        }\\n      }\\n1:# Nexus Code Upgrade Security & Publisher Authenticity Assessment\\n2-\\n3-## 1. Executive Summary\\n4-\\n5:This document establishes the trust boundaries, security controls, and cryptographic authenticity architecture for the `nexus upgrade` and `/upgrade` update engine introduced in Nexus Code v1.0.0 (Workstream 12, REQ-REL-115, REQ-REL-116, ACC-UPG-07..14).\\n6-\\n7-## 2. Trust Boundaries & Threat Model\\n8-\\n9:The self-upgrade mechanism enables operators to update their active Nexus installation to newer (or pinned) published releases directly from the CLI or TUI. Because executable updates run with the user's execution privileges and can replace core harness and TUI binaries, rigorous boundary enforcement is mandatory:\\n10-\\n11-### In-Scope Threats\\n12-\\n13-1. **Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) & Transport Tampering**:\\n14-   - Attackers attempting to modify binaries in transit or redirect downloads to malicious hosts.\\n15-2. **Path Traversal & Archive Extraction Vulnerabilities**:\\n16:   - Malicious release archives attempting to write outside the isolated installation directory via `../` path traversal, absolute paths, escaping symlinks, devices, or hardlinks.\\n17-3. **Resource Exhaustion & Tar Bombs**:\\n18-   - Download streams or archive contents engineered to consume unbounded disk space or memory.\\n19-4. **State & Migration Incompatibility**:\\n20-   - Downgrading to older binaries that corrupt newer configuration or task persistence schemas.\\n21:5. **Partial Switch / Crash Mid-Installation**:\\n22-   - System failure or termination during package replacement leaving the system without an executable binary.\\n23-6. **Package Manager Collision**:\\n24:   - Accidental overwriting of installations managed by OS package managers (e.g. `apt`, `brew`, `npm`).\\n25-7. **PATH Shadowing**:\\n26-   - Updating `$PREFIX/bin/nexus` while an unmanaged or stale `nexus` binary earlier in `$PATH` continues to execute.\\n27-\\n--\\n57-- Legacy public releases lacking `compatibility.json` are permitted under an explicit legacy policy with an advisory notice.\\n58-\\n59-### 3.4 Durable Provenance & Destination Verification (ACC-UPG-10)\\n60:- The installer and updater write `.provenance.json` (mode 0644) inside `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION`.\\n61:- Managed installations are distinguished from development checkouts (`git pull && make build`) and package-manager distributions (`apt`, `brew`).\\n62:- Self-upgrade refuses to overwrite package-manager installations, directing the user to their package manager.\\n63-\\n64-### 3.5 Pre-Migration Backups, Atomic Symlinks & Rollback (ACC-UPG-09, ACC-UPG-11)\\n65-- Before modifying files, `createPreMigrationBackup` backs up `~/.config/nexus/config.env` (mode 0600) and complete durable state/configuration snapshots (excluding backup directories) to `~/.config/nexus/backups/` and `~/.nexus/backups/`.\\n66-- Replacement occurs via atomic symlink swap:\\n67-  - `ln -s $PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION/bin/nexus $PREFIX/bin/.nexus-link.$PID && mv -f ... $PREFIX/bin/nexus`\\n68:- `--rollback-binary` safely rolls back the launcher symlink to the previous installed version in `$PREFIX/lib/nexus`.\\n69-- `--restore-backup <path>` accepts a canonical plain `config.env.bak.*` file for configuration-only restoration, or a private `~/.nexus/backups/state-backup-*` directory containing `backup.json`, `state/`, and optional `config/` for complete snapshot restoration. It rejects arbitrary files, tar archives, and redirected paths.\\n70-- Run backup restoration through the stable `nexus` launcher. Close existing legacy clients before retrying a pending restore, and keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. Current managed launches route through the journal before loading configuration; the Linux process census detects already-running legacy entry points, but cannot serialize a new direct launch from a version that predates the kernel lease. That offline interval is an explicit prerequisite of the supported restore boundary.\\n71-\\n72-### 3.6 Transaction Journal & Crash Recovery (ACC-UPG-11)\\n73:- The updater logs state progression to `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade-journal.json`:\\n74-  - `preparing` -> `downloading` -> `staged` -> `switching` -> `switched` -> `verified` -> `complete`\\n75-- Idempotent recovery (`--recover` and automatic startup check):\\n76-  - Crashes before switching: cleans staging directory, source version remains active.\\n--\\n98-         subject-path: 'nexus-linux-x86_64-*.tar.gz'\\n99-     ```\\n100-   - This produces an immutable, cryptographic in-toto attestation signed via Sigstore's Fulcio certificate authority and recorded in the Rekor transparency log, binding the binary to the repository, workflow, and commit SHA.\\n101:   - The updater can verify this provenance using `gh attestation verify` (automated hook already provided in `cli/src/upgrade.ts`) or an embedded pure-JS Sigstore bundle verifier.\\n102-\\n103-2. **MiniSign / PGP Detached Signatures**:\\n104-   - Release workflow signs `SHA256SUMS` with a dedicated release offline key:\\n--\\n108-\\n109-### Post-review transaction recovery\\n110-\\n111:Replacement package backups are recorded before renaming as `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.rollback-<transaction-id>`, outside disposable staging. Same-version repairs retain the real previous package for explicit binary rollback. Journal writes and rename boundaries are flushed before reporting completion. Recovery validates the complete source runtime and only records `rolled_back` after restoring and verifying the installation/link. Failure retains staging and package artifacts under `recovery_required` and returns a nonzero operational error; it never reports successful rollback after a failed restore. A previously verified target may be finalized only after another complete runtime check.\\n112-\\n113-Package health probes use an isolated temporary home, bounded output/time, and process-group cleanup. New packages must report the exact product version from launcher, core, and TUI; the core help path and TUI snapshot render must also work. Historical alpha.1/alpha.2 exceptions are restricted to exact publicly checksummed component hashes: their core reports its historical 1.2.1 identity and their TUI predates `--version`. This exception is not permission for arbitrary component mismatch.\\n114-\\n115:Packaged CLI/TUI startup checks pending journals before normal execution. Explicit help/version, `upgrade --check`, and supervised health probes are read-only and do not recover. Active upgrade locks prevent concurrent recovery. Qualification from a real prior public release and manual terminal acceptance remain separate release gates; synthetic fault tests do not establish them.\\n116-\\n117-### Concurrent stale-lock reclamation\\n118-\\n119:When a recovery or upgrade observes a stale lock (dead holder PID), exactly one process may unlink and replace it. Serialization uses a permanent kernel-owned guard file `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade.lock.guard` (never unlinked or replaced; accepted only as a regular file owned by the running user with no group/other permission bits): the reclaimer holds an advisory `flock` on the file's open file description for the whole reclaim section, acquired through `/usr/bin/flock` (util-linux; Linux runtime prerequisite) with exit status 75 distinguishing contention. The kernel drops the lock when the last referring descriptor closes, so a reclaimer killed by SIGKILL or power loss releases automatically instead of wedging later upgrades. If the flock utility or filesystem is unavailable, acquisition fails closed with a manual-intervention error rather than proceeding unserialized.\\n120-\\n121-### Durable state store coordination (schema 2)\\n122-\\n123:Task and session progress files refer to separate append-only message journals. Backup and rollback acquire both permanent state-store guards in a fixed order while copying or restoring these components. Guard files are omitted from snapshots and their existing inodes survive restore, including cleanup of directories absent from an older snapshot. This uses the same kernel-owned file guard as upgrade stale-lock recovery; it does not introduce a stale directory lock or unlink live guard files.\\n124-\\n125-Close older clients before migration or rollback. Older versions cannot participate in schema 2 store locking. A new client requires util-linux `/usr/bin/flock` for state transactions and fails closed when it is unavailable. A busy store stops a snapshot instead of producing a mixed progress/message backup.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"6e7692\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00003068,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1179,\"output\":\".github/release.yml\\n.github/workflows/release.yml\\nREADME.md\\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md\\ndocs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md\\ndocs/releases/rulesets/protected-branches.json\\ndocs/releases/rulesets/release-tags.json\\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.1.md\\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.2.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.3.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.4.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.7.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.8.md\\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md\\ndocs/research/context-engineering/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus-dogfooding-2026-10-03/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus-ratatui-facelift-2026-10-03/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/parallel-defect-investigation-2026-10-04/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-AUTHORIZATION-REDACTION-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CHECKPOINT-STATE-INJECTION-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-CST-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-DOCTOR-UNREADABLE-STATE-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-EDIT-FILE-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-FILE-INFO-UNBOUNDED-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-GIT-EXCLUDE-SUBSTRING-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-HTML-CONTROL-INJECTION-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-MCP-CONFIG-PERSIST-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-NAT64-SSRF-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-PARSER-COMMA-CORRUPTION-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-PARSER-MIXED-QUOTES-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-MODE-ESCALATION-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-READONLY-SYMLINK-CONFINEMENT-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RECOVER-WORKTREE-CONVERSATION-20261026/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-REPL-READONLY-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RETENTION-CHECKPOINT-PATH-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-RUNNER-BACKGROUND-STARTUP-EXIT-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-SSRF-IPV6-CONNECT-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-TAR-AMBIENT-ENV-20261024/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-TAR-SYMLINK-TRAVERSAL-20261023/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UI-TERMINAL-INJECTION-20261025/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_AGT111_V1_CLOSURE/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_JOURNAL_COMPLEXITY_RECOVERY/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_BASELINE/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_SPLIT/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_COMPANIONS/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RMW_TRANSACTION_RECOVERY/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SCHEMA2_INTEGRATION/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_VERSION_PROBE_STORAGE/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_COMPONENT_COHERENCE/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/public-release-identities.json\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/README.md\\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/README.md\\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/README.md\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/release_snapshot_2026-10-16.json\\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md\\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md\\neval/README.md\\neval/host/README.md\\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/README.md\\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/install.sh\\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/normalize-install.py\\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/post-install-qualify.py\\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/test-install-python-boundary.py\\nexperiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/trusted-broker-bundle/verify-install.py\\nexperiments/routing-b1-b2-2026-10-03/README.md\\nexperiments/thermal-soak-2026-10-03/README.CORRECTION.txt\\nexperiments/thermal-soak-2026-10-03/README.md\\nexperiments/thermal-soak-2026-10-03/policy-replay/README.md\\ninstall.sh\\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh\\nscripts/release-tools/package-lock.json\\nscripts/release-tools/package.json\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"97ff60\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000039453,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1118,\"output\":\"5-## Choose a path\\n6-\\n7:- **[Install and use Nexus Code](quickstart.md)** — supported platform, one-line installer, configuration, and first task.\\n8-- **[Read the historical Cloudflare contest entry](docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md)** — the collaboration service built with Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts, its source map, and judge guide.\\n9-\\n10-The contest has concluded. Its submission was the agent-collaboration service; Nexus Code is the separate client and harness used to demonstrate it.\\n11-\\n12:## Install Nexus Code\\n13-\\n14:The unversioned installer follows the latest stable release. If no stable release has been published yet, it exits with a hint to select a prerelease tag. To install a prerelease or pin a version, use the tag shown on [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases) and set `NEXUS_VERSION`; see the [quickstart](quickstart.md).\\n15-\\n16-```sh\\n17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\\n18-```\\n19-\\n20:This follows the latest stable release and installs the Linux x86-64 package under your home directory. The installer verifies its SHA-256 checksum and requires Node.js 22 or newer. To pin a specific version or install a prerelease, set `NEXUS_VERSION` to that release's tag. See [release status and platform requirements](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md).\\n21-\\n22-## Build and contribute\\n23-\\n24:See [development and release procedures](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md), [client guide](docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md), [provider setup](docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md), and the [contest entry](docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md).\\n25-\\n26-The client sources are in `cli/` and `core/`. The Cloudflare service and fixture are in `experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/`; demo orchestration is in `demo/`.\\n--\\n28-## Community and project policies\\n29-\\n30:Read the [contribution guide](CONTRIBUTING.md), [support channels](SUPPORT.md), [security policy](SECURITY.md), [governance](GOVERNANCE.md), and [code of conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Track changes in [releases](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases); development plans do not establish release readiness.\\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8 release candidate\\n\\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\\n\\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest.\\n\\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`.\\n\\n## Changes since RC7\\n\\n- **Checkpoint safety:** checkpoint creation now detects a present or unreadable Git index lock before publishing a checkpoint reference, and reports why it stopped. It rechecks the lock after validation and stash creation so a concurrent Git operation is less likely to publish a stale checkpoint.\\n- **Read-only mode consistency:** the effective permission posture is applied consistently when an agent and its workspace extensions start or change modes. A temporary checkpoint-safety fallback stays separate from the configured mode, allowing recovery without silently changing the operator's selected mode.\\n- **Recovered operation continuity:** recovered operation context is retained across session restoration, while prior verifier baselines remain untrusted and require fresh verification before a recovered result can be treated as verified.\\n- **Upgrade reliability:** GitHub release downloads now follow its signed release-asset redirect without forwarding GitHub credentials to the asset host. Large pre-migration backups report aggregate progress and avoid redundant directory syncs while retaining file and directory durability.\\n\\n## Runtime requirements\\n\\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\\n\\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\\n\\n## Candidate assets\\n\\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.8` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a177c2-7b4a-7152-ba84-5c8470f48393","create_time":1793011391.030235}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
