{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:06:55.591Z","ordinal":384302,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177cf-42cc-7823-a07a-666f72e7f9a8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ae18056b-b99b-4523-82de-e8914a300150","process_id":"23567","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 3 'screenshot|scrot|import|gnome-screenshot' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-exact-main-1434-enforce","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 3 'screenshot|scrot|import|gnome-screenshot' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md","query":"screenshot|scrot|import|gnome-screenshot","path":"run-cell.sh"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-5-#   - terminal state (stty) before and after each exit;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-6-#   - processes from the cell (by HOME or workspace cwd) that survive an exit, with a planted positive control;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-7-#   - the mock's request log, which proves which scenarios ran.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:8:# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-9-#   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-10-#     --size <80x24|40x14|200x60> --out <evidence dir>\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-11-set -euo pipefail\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-143-In the TUI that opens next (the first word of each prompt selects the mock scenario):\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-144-  1  It launches and shows the TUI.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-145-  2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:146:     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-147-  3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-148-  4  Prompt \"stream\" and resize the window while it streams; restore $size afterwards.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-149-  5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:150:  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-151-Press Enter to launch.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-152-EOF\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-153-read -r _\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-160-read -r _\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-161-launch no_color NO_COLOR=1\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-162-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:163:# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-164-: > \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-165-for check in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7; do\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-166-  while true; do\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-175-cp \"$mock_log\" \"$stem.mock.log\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-176-read -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-177-while true; do\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:178:  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:179:  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-180-  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-181-     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-182-     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:183:  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-184-done\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-185-approval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-186-exit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-192-NEXUS_PATH=\"$nexus_real\" PACKAGE_DIR=\"$package\" MANIFEST_SHA=\"$manifest_sha\" TMUX_VERSION=\"$tmux_version\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-193-KITTY_PROTOCOL=\"$kitty_protocol\" OPERATOR_NAME=\"$operator\" STEM=\"$stem\" APPROVAL_SHOT=\"$approval_copy\" EXIT_SHOT=\"$exit_copy\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-194-python3 - <<'PY'\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:195:import hashlib, json, os\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-196-e = os.environ\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-197-stem = e[\"STEM\"]\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-198-sha = lambda p: hashlib.sha256(open(p, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-221-    \"tmux\": e[\"TMUX_VERSION\"] or None, \"kittyKeyboardProtocol\": e[\"KITTY_PROTOCOL\"] or None,\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-222-    \"measured\": exits, \"scenarios\": scenarios, \"checks\": checks,\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-223-    \"files\": {name: {\"path\": os.path.basename(path), \"sha256\": sha(path)} for name, path in\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:224:              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-225-               (\"answers\", f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"), (\"exits\", f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\")]},\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-226-    \"operator\": e[\"OPERATOR_NAME\"],\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-227-}\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-16-1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-17-   not resolve into a checkout.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-18-2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:19:3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-20-   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-21-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-22-## Each cell\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-35-| # | You do | You judge |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-36-|---|---|---|\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-37-| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:38:| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-39-| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-40-| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-41-| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:42:| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-43-| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-44-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-45-The script also **measures** two things:\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-48-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-49-A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-50-`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:51:results and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-52-attempt and use a new evidence directory.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-53-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-54-## Gate\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":688635184}},"started_at_ms":1793012814901,"completed_at_ms":1793012815590}}
