sh-149-  5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:150:  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-151-Press Enter to launch.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-152-EOF\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-153-read -r _\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-160-read -r _\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh-161-la…1056 tokens truncated…3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-39-| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-40-| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-41-| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:42:| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-43-| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-44-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-45-The script also **measures** two things:\n--\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-48-\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md-49-A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes