{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:35:01.204Z","ordinal":384961,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177fc-b8a0-7601-9a58-2c8637b7ce72","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf3ae4143081a0993bbfd68fc26af8","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The upgrade reached the download step, then RC7 rejected GitHub’s signed asset redirect. The backup was made, but the upgrade did not switch versions.\n\nRC8 contains the redirect-handling fix, and the earlier checkpoint recorded it installed on `mike-dev`. I can’t verify the host’s current version now: SSH reports that its host key has changed. I won’t remove or bypass that check without verifying the new key. Once the host identity is verified, I can confirm the installed version and retry from RC8 if needed."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793014500110,"completed_at_ms":1793014501204}}
