{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:39:28.225Z","ordinal":385133,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177fe-59d7-78d1-b754-fee944e5993b","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a177fe-59d7-78d1-b754-fee944e5993b","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf3bea1cb081a08ec81864addc319e","usage":{"input_tokens":117702,"cached_input_tokens":116096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":623,"reasoning_output_tokens":406,"total_tokens":118325},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2194677,"cached_input_tokens":2141184,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9318,"reasoning_output_tokens":6353,"total_tokens":2203995},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7075206170,"cached_input_tokens":6999943040,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20226180,"reasoning_output_tokens":11719068,"total_tokens":7095432350}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:39:30.351Z","ordinal":385134,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a177fe-59d7-78d1-b754-fee944e5993b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-160fb6a2-09e1-4164-81d7-38354a258a7e","process_id":"78679","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","GH_PROMPT_DISABLED=1 gh api 'repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/contents/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md?ref=1434a93ba32a5cbfa128a2007cf43bd5449a6725' --jq .content | base64 -d | sed -n '1,220p'; GH_PROMPT_DISABLED=1 gh api 'repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/contents/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md?ref=1434a93ba32a5cbfa128a2007cf43bd5449a6725' --jq .content | base64 -d | rg -n -A32 -B6 '5\\.3|terminal matrix|Terminal matrix' | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"GH_PROMPT_DISABLED=1 gh api 'repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/contents/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md?ref=1434a93ba32a5cbfa128a2007cf43bd5449a6725' --jq .content | base64 -d | sed -n '1,220p'; GH_PROMPT_DISABLED=1 gh api 'repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/contents/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md?ref=1434a93ba32a5cbfa128a2007cf43bd5449a6725' --jq .content | base64 -d | rg -n -A32 -B6 '5\\.3|terminal matrix|Terminal matrix' | head -80"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56-### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n57-\n58-| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n59-|---|---|---|\n60-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n61-\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n71-\n72-   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n73-5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n74-\n75-## 2. Environments\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n87-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n96-| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n97-| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n98-| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n99-| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n100-| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n101-| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n102-\n103-\n104-### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n105-\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n--\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":808371477}},"started_at_ms":1793014769541,"completed_at_ms":1793014770350}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:39:31.348Z","ordinal":385135,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17802-2e94-71d3-9272-84d703e169e5","call_id":"call_b0bc5c08b1444c448584fd3806a3fce6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2772)\nTotal output lines: 155\n\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partia…572 tokens truncated…24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n87-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n96-| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n97-| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n98-| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n99-| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n100-| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n101-| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n102-\n103-\n104-### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n105-\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n--\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a177fe-59d7-78d1-b754-fee944e5993b","create_time":1793014771.3482933}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
