{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:44:24.967Z","ordinal":385333,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf3d1840b081a0a57901ac8cc217a1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_60dce11a46604778b2eaee3a86601b8d","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh | rg -n -C 3 'screenshot|gnome-screenshot|scrot|IMAGE|shot' ; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,100p'\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1000});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","create_time":1793015064.255274}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:44:25.345Z","ordinal":385334,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf3d11574481a0a013c1890438689f","usage":{"input_tokens":153703,"cached_input_tokens":152832,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":794,"reasoning_output_tokens":681,"total_tokens":154497},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2902156,"cached_input_tokens":2867840,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12602,"reasoning_output_tokens":8654,"total_tokens":2914758},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7078351816,"cached_input_tokens":7003048960,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20241338,"reasoning_output_tokens":11729828,"total_tokens":7098593154}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:44:26.029Z","ordinal":385335,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-50d40342-dfeb-4350-85b5-742104ee64df","process_id":"53086","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh | rg -n -C 3 'screenshot|gnome-screenshot|scrot|IMAGE|shot' ; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,100p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh | rg -n -C 3 'screenshot|gnome-screenshot|scrot|IMAGE|shot' ; git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,100p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"5-#   - terminal state (stty) before and after each exit;\n6-#   - processes from the cell (by HOME or workspace cwd) that survive an exit, with a planted positive control;\n7-#   - the mock's request log, which proves which scenarios ran.\n8:# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\n9-#   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\n10-#     --size <80x24|40x14|200x60> --out <evidence dir>\n11-set -euo pipefail\n--\n143-In the TUI that opens next (the first word of each prompt selects the mock scenario):\n144-  1  It launches and shows the TUI.\n145-  2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\n146:     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\n147-  3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\n148-  4  Prompt \"stream\" and resize the window while it streams; restore $size afterwards.\n149-  5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\n150:  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\n151-Press Enter to launch.\n152-EOF\n153-read -r _\n--\n160-read -r _\n161-launch no_color NO_COLOR=1\n162-\n163:# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\n164-: > \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\n165-for check in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7; do\n166-  while true; do\n--\n175-cp \"$mock_log\" \"$stem.mock.log\"\n176-read -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\n177-while true; do\n178:  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n179:  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n180:  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n181:     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n182:     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n183:  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\n184-done\n185:approval_copy=\"$stem.approval.${shot_approval##*.}\"\n186:exit_copy=\"$stem.post-exit.${shot_exit##*.}\"\n187:cp \"$shot_approval\" \"$approval_copy\"\n188:cp \"$shot_exit\" \"$exit_copy\"\n189-\n190-# Values reach Python only through the environment, never through generated source.\n191-CELL=\"$cell\" ATTEMPT=\"$attempt\" TERMINAL_NAME=\"$terminal\" CELL_SIZE=\"$size\" RC=\"$rc\" NEXUS_VERSION_LINE=\"$version_line\" \\\n--\n221-    \"tmux\": e[\"TMUX_VERSION\"] or None, \"kittyKeyboardProtocol\": e[\"KITTY_PROTOCOL\"] or None,\n222-    \"measured\": exits, \"scenarios\": scenarios, \"checks\": checks,\n223-    \"files\": {name: {\"path\": os.path.basename(path), \"sha256\": sha(path)} for name, path in\n224:              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\n225-               (\"answers\", f\"{stem}.answers.tsv\"), (\"exits\", f\"{stem}.exits.tsv\")]},\n226-    \"operator\": e[\"OPERATOR_NAME\"],\n227-}\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":62919}},"started_at_ms":1793015066029,"completed_at_ms":1793015066029}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:44:27.102Z","ordinal":385336,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17806-b1dd-7f71-8255-78722fbd5c3a","call_id":"call_60dce11a46604778b2eaee3a86601b8d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1898)\nTotal output lines: 128\n\n5-#   - terminal state (stty) before and after each exit;\n6-#   - processes from the cell (by HOME or workspace cwd) that survive an exit, with a planted positive control;\n7-#   - the mock's request log, which proves which scenarios ran.\n8:# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\n9-#   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\n10-#     --size <80x24|40x14|200x60> --out <evidence dir>\n11-set -euo pipefail\n--\n143-In the TUI that opens next (the first word of each prompt selects the mock scenario):\n144-  1  It launches and shows the TUI.\n145-  2  Prompt \"approve\". While each of the two approval panels is open, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then\n146:     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\n147-  3  Enter a multiline prompt with Shift+Enter (or Alt+Enter).\n148-  4  Prompt \"stream\" and resize the window while it streams; restore $size afterwards.\n149-  5  Prompt \"sleep\" and press Esc while \"sleep 30\" runs.\n150:  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\n151-Press Enter to launch.\n152-EOF\n153-read -r _\n--\n160-read -r _\n161-launch no_color NO_COLOR=1\n162-\n163:# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\n164-: > \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\n165-for check in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7; do\n166-  while true; do\n--\n175-cp \"$mock_log\" \"$stem.mock.log\"\n176-read -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\n177-while true; do\n178:  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\n179:  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\n180:  if [[ \"$shot_approval\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && \"$shot_exit\" =~ \\.(png|jpe?g)$ && -f \"$shot_approval\" && -f \"$shot_exit\" ]] \\\n181:     && ! cmp -s \"$shot_approval\" \"$shot_exit\" \\\n182:     && (( $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_approval\") >= attempt_start && $(stat -c %Y \"$shot_exit\") >= attempt_start )); then break; fi\n183:  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.…898 tokens truncated…xit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","create_time":1793015067.101938}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
