{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:00.724Z","ordinal":385384,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf3d78051081a0b2ff99c8938d9ef2","status":"completed","call_id":"call_68b7dceb193846a5b98042ea272a5fff","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '120,160p'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification | rg 'rc\\\\.8|rc\\\\.7|providers' | head -60\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1600});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","create_time":1793015160.0235057}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:00.825Z","ordinal":385385,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf3d6a541481a08f8c104efdbaed21","usage":{"input_tokens":159162,"cached_input_tokens":158080,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1538,"reasoning_output_tokens":1424,"total_tokens":160700},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3846052,"cached_input_tokens":3805440,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17102,"reasoning_output_tokens":12550,"total_tokens":3863154},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7079295712,"cached_input_tokens":7003986560,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20245838,"reasoning_output_tokens":11733724,"total_tokens":7099541550}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:01.883Z","ordinal":385386,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8ae36ebb-c496-4a4a-8929-8910957de50b","process_id":"73541","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '120,160p'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification | rg 'rc\\.8|rc\\.7|providers' | head -60"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '120,160p'; git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification | rg 'rc\\.8|rc\\.7|providers' | head -60"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27869}},"started_at_ms":1793015161882,"completed_at_ms":1793015161883}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:02.936Z","ordinal":385387,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17808-2838-7d63-8599-7d9940f0366c","call_id":"call_68b7dceb193846a5b98042ea272a5fff","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","create_time":1793015162.9367418}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
