ication\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"costConfidence\":\"unknown\",\"outcome\":\"failed\",\"failureKind\":\"http_error\",\"usageConfidence\":\"none\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:5:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:04.677Z\",\"requestId\":\"24a6aab0-d91f-443f-a225-6abf69debe3b\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"REDACTED\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":24,\"outputTokens\":54,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":50,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:6:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:06.238Z\",\"requestId\":\"b96adfad-275b-4b96-812b-3e3152ccbfea\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"gen-1792774744-4t2kU7vz1CXEpLIH1nz4\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":321,\"outputTokens\":71,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":36,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:7:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:10.680Z\",\"requestId\":\"6b0abf39-7840-417c-a5c2-9b1585f9f835\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"gen-1792774746-6l3KwgU3yGnMxzaRncSa\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":380,\"outputTokens\":42,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":20,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:112:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:91:| L1–L3 | On the RC | With pinned models (ACCEPTANCE §4.3) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:372:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:423:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:19:- Two connection kinds: (a) legacy \"appliance/endpoint\" path (no provider id): OpenAI Chat Completions, `/v1` appended, fallback list, `X-Task-Class`, gateway token file / config.env key scoped by origin (client.ts:123-133), no receipts, no spending limits; (b) provider connections (providers.ts:46-116): openrouter, openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), compatible, chatgpt (unofficial OAuth), copilot (unofficial OAuth); pinned endpoint, own key only, `redirect:\"error\"`, receipts in `<ws>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`, spending limits (usage.ts).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:92:| G1 No live evidence of standalone LM Studio / llama.cpp / vLLM / Ollama runs. `.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl` (HISTORICAL, 2026-10-11..14) contains only provider-connection receipts: chatgpt 284 (281 completed), openrouter 12; local/appliance requests are never receipted (client.ts:561-569), so there is no machine-readable local evidence. | On a clean host with no `~/.config/nexus`, run each server with a small tool-capable model; `nexus run` a fixed 3-step edit task; capture `/status` context source, turn status, and transcript; repeat with the server's context set to 4096 to exercise PRV-06. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:93:| G2 Live cloud qualification limited to openrouter + chatgpt (docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md, HISTORICAL). openai, anthropic, copilot, compatible: mock-only. | `nexus providers verify --provider {openai,anthropic,copilot,compatible} --model <m> -j` with operator keys; archive JSON. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27491}},"started_at_ms":1793015210781,"completed_at_ms":1793015210781}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:46:52.070Z","ordinal":385425,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17808-e826-7a73-ae43-baebe20caa7a","call_id":"call_c3b882f839844957ac53d6453e32fe69","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2289)\nTotal output lines: 21\n\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json:12:    \"command\": \"nexus providers verify --provider <provider> -m <pinned-model> --json\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:18:    \"command\": \"nexus providers verify --provider <provider> --model <pinned-model> --json\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:95:  \"qualificationDisposition\": \"Provider verification passed for ChatGPT sign-in and one explicitly pinned OpenRouter model. The separate required live engineering task per ACCEPTANCE.md §4.3 remains incomplete; this record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:4:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:58:02.236Z\",\"requestId\":\"e5ad5e55-85bd-41a9-b304-459832133c3c\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"costConfidence\":\"unknown\",\"outcome\":\"failed\",\"failureKind\":\"http_error\",\"usageConfidence\":\"none\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:5:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:04.677Z\",\"requestId\":\"24a6aab0-d91f-443f-a225-6abf69debe3b\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"REDACTED\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":24,\"outputTokens\":54,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":50,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:6:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:06.238Z\",\"requestId\":\"b96adfad-275b-4b96-812b-3e3152ccbfea\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"…1089 tokens truncated…s | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:19:- Two connection kinds: (a) legacy \"appliance/endpoint\" path (no provider id): OpenAI Chat Completions, `/v1` appended, fallback list, `X-Task-Class`, gateway token file / config.env key scoped by origin (client.ts:123-133), no receipts, no spending limits; (b) provider connections (providers.ts:46-116): openrouter, openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), compatible, chatgpt (unofficial OAuth), copilot (unofficial OAuth); pinned endpoint, own key only, `redirect:\"error\"`, receipts in `<ws>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`, spending limits (usage.ts).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:92:| G1 No live evidence of standalone LM Studio / llama.cpp / vLLM / Ollama runs. `.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl` (HISTORICAL, 2026-10-11..14) contains only provider-connection receipts: chatgpt 284 (281 completed), openrouter 12; local/appliance requests are never receipted (client.ts:561-569), so there is no machine-readable local evidence. | On a clean host with no `~/.config/nexus`, run each server with a small tool-capable model; `nexus run` a fixed 3-step edit task; capture `/status` context source, turn status, and transcript; repeat with the server's context set to 4096 to exercise PRV-06. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:93:| G2 Live cloud qualification limited to openrouter + chatgpt (docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md, HISTORICAL). openai, anthropic, copilot, compatible: mock-only. | `nexus providers verify --provider {openai,anthropic,copilot,compatible} --model <m> -j` with operator keys; archive JSON. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17802-f864-7383-97fc-4fdd2f0a5d6e","create_time":1793015212.070271}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
