{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:01:38.811Z","ordinal":386020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17815-c207-77b3-8d5e-f5b6ea16defd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cc42fcdb-d1c6-4fda-b1d6-bfcab1ffc976","process_id":"47335","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -A45 -B8 '5\\.3|terminal matrix|xterm|kitty' && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, pathlib, subprocess\nroot=pathlib.Path(subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','--git-common-dir'], text=True).strip())/'nexus-claims'\nfor name in ['FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md','FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix']:\n p=root/name/'owner.json'\n print(name, json.loads(p.read_text()) if p.exists() else 'no claim')\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -A45 -B8 '5\\.3|terminal matrix|xterm|kitty' && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, pathlib, subprocess\nroot=pathlib.Path(subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','--git-common-dir'], text=True).strip())/'nexus-claims'\nfor name in ['FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md','FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix']:\n p=root/name/'owner.json'\n print(name, json.loads(p.read_text()) if p.exists() else 'no claim')\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"43-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56-### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n57-\n58-| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n59-|---|---|---|\n60-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n61-\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n71-\n72-   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n73-5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n74-\n75-## 2. Environments\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n87-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n96-| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n97-| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n98-| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n99-| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n100-| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n101-| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n102-\n103-\n104-### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n105-\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n125-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n126-\n127-1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n128-2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n129-3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n130-   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n131-   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n132-   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n133-\n134-   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n135-4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n136-5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n137-\n138-### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n139-\n140-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n141-|---|---|---|---|\n142-| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n143-| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n144-| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n145-| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n146-| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n147-\n148-ACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n149-\n150-### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n151-\n152-| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n153-|---|---|---|\n154-| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n155-| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n156-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161-### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n162-\n163-These must pass:\n164-\n165-- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n166-- `tui_diff_e2e`\n--\n182-| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n183-| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n184-| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n185-| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n186-| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n193-\n194-For each terminal × size, check:\n195-\n196-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n197-2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n198-3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n199-4. Resize during streaming.\n200-5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n201-6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n202-7. NO_COLOR.\n203-\n204-Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n205-\n206-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n207-\n208-## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n209-\n210-Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n211-\n212-### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n213-\n214-- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n215-- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n216-- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n217-- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n218-- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n219-\n220-  ```bash\n221-  set -euo pipefail\n222-  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n223-  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n224-  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n225-  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n226-  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n227-  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n228-  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n229-  ```\n230-\n231-  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n232-\n233-### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n234-\n235-9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n236-\n237-1. refused connection mid-turn\nFILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md {'agent': '/root', 'host': 'mike-dev', 'branch': 'v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet', 'worktree': '/home/mike/nexus-wt/terminal-matrix-rc3', 'base': '016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f', 'since': '2026-10-23T09:20:00Z', 'scope': 'Prepare the REQ-QUAL-108 operator worksheet for the next eligible RC; no matrix results or acceptance claim', 'reviewer': 'current_main_rc_path_audit', 'review_disposition': 'ACCEPT', 'reviewed_at': '2026-10-25T05:47:00Z', 'status': 'RC7 is now present on ubuntu-desktop at /home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.7; CLI reports 1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f), installed package tree matches published archive byte-for-byte excluding installer-created .provenance.json, and provenance archive SHA256 matches public digest 367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a. Host runs Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS with xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux 3.6, VS Code; active GNOME Wayland seat. Matrix remains 0/15; no screenshots/manual behavior claimed. Existing worksheet branch remains unintegrated; no evidence changes made.', 'head': '2b55c031498412747f5e2ef09b4ef9e288ac77ca', 'desktop_rc4_archive_sha256': '07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806', 'desktop_rc4_cli_version': '1.0.0-rc.4 (57b9285c6cea)', 'terminal_matrix_completed_cells': 0, 'updated_at': '2026-10-26T01:48:00Z'}\nFILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix {'agent': 'codex-root', 'host': 'mike-dev', 'branch': 'v1/rc7-terminal-matrix-prep', 'worktree': '/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc7-terminal-matrix-prep', 'base': '0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2', 'since': '2026-10-26T00:33:00Z', 'scope': 'Prepare a blank, RC-bound operator worksheet for ACCEPTANCE §5.3 terminal matrix; no terminal runs and no acceptance evidence; create only terminal matrix worksheet and procedure note.', 'status': 'Prepared worksheet commit 4e36019 independently accepted. The CSV has 15 pending cells bound to RC7 source and archive digest; no manual checks or screenshots exist. Await current main suite and owner integration path.', 'head': '4e36019f1a86e0e46d802537391cff3afc791fe2', 'diff_sha256': '37768a368e47dff83b1fd8b64d11c7473159bf9a26971a41c93628a202b0a678', 'independent_review': 'ACCEPT exact head by plan05_readonly_review; all 15 cells and all check columns explicitly pending; RC7 archive/source identity verified in worksheet', 'updated_at': '2026-10-26T00:35:07Z'}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27030}},"started_at_ms":1793016098810,"completed_at_ms":1793016098811}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:01:39.856Z","ordinal":386021,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17816-7410-7882-871c-88a8e52ddc21","call_id":"call_21bbd17468c842a687205b0c23c00798","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4109)\nTotal output lines: 183\n\n43-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56-### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n57-\n58-| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n59-|---|---|---|\n60-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n61-\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n71-\n72-   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n73-5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n74-\n75-## 2. Environments\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n87-Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n88-\n89-| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n90-|---|---|---|\n91-| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n92-| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n93-| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n94-| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n95-| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n96-| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n97-| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n98-| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n99-| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n100-| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n101-| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n102-\n103-\n104-### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n105-\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111-| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 o…1109 tokens truncated… integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n193-\n194-For each terminal × size, check:\n195-\n196-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n197-2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n198-3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n199-4. Resize during streaming.\n200-5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n201-6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n202-7. NO_COLOR.\n203-\n204-Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n205-\n206-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n207-\n208-## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n209-\n210-Environment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n211-\n212-### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n213-\n214-- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n215-- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n216-- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n217-- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n218-- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n219-\n220-  ```bash\n221-  set -euo pipefail\n222-  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n223-  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n224-  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n225-  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n226-  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n227-  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n228-  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n229-  ```\n230-\n231-  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n232-\n233-### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n234-\n235-9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 