{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:48:16.087Z","ordinal":387179,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a17841-1ed7-70f2-b313-6e358f0b9f3c","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2573)\nTotal output lines: 109\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...399 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-26 12:48pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (15,143t read) | 75,457t work | 80% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1693 User set approval mode to \"Default to review\" — session continuing RC.4 release gate monitoring (Oct 23, 11:19 PM)\nS1694 RC.4 release gate monitoring — CI status check on main and PR #175 while holding CR bypass blocker (Oct 23, 11:21 PM)\nS1701 RC.4 release gate session recovery — assess PR #175 CR bypass blocker and CI status across main and PR #175 branches (Oct 23, 11:22 PM)\nS1707 RC.4 release gate — monitoring CI for PR #175 (CR bypass fix needed) and main branch while holding merge pending blocker resolution (Oct 23, 11:25 PM)\nS1709 RC.4 release gate — PR #175 CR bypass fix blocked on safe-boundary handoff; monitoring main CI while waiting for claim transfer confirmation (Oct 23, 11:26 PM)\nS1718 Kimi agent handover for agent.ts — monitoring CI for PR #240 refreshed branch while main CI run 40227786412 completes (Oct 23, 11:30 PM)\n### Oct 25, 2026\nS1723 Kimi agent waiting for agent.ts handover — PR #240 REPL checkpoint failure recovery review and CI monitoring (Oct 25, 8:05 PM)\nS1730 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error from nexus upgrade, and relationship to checkpoint fix shipped in RC7 (Oct 25, 8:36 PM)\nS1733 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error and relationship to checkpoint fix shipped in RC7 (Oct 25, 9:41 PM)\nS1731 RC7 candidate PR #241 — source verification, independent review, and CI monitoring through linux-x86_64 packaging job (Oct 25, 10:20 PM)\n22392 11:01p ○ Main Branch CI Run 40240003952 — linux-x86_64 Job Now Running package-linux.sh for v1.0.0-rc.6\n22394 11:02p ○ PR #241 linux-x86_64 Job Now Running package-linux.sh for v1.0.0-rc.7\n22395 11:05p ○ Main Branch CI Run 40240003952 — linux-x86_64 Job Completed Successfully\n22396 11:07p ○ PR #241 CI linux-x86_64 Job 121314288159 Completed Successfully\n22398 \" ○ PR #241 CI Fully Green — mergeStateStatus CLEAN, Ready to Merge\n22399 \" ✓ PR #241 Merged — RC7 Version Bump Landed on Main\n22400 \" ○ PR #241 Merge Commit Confirmed — New Main CI Runs Started on 431cb19\n22401 \" ✓ RC7 Claims Updated Post-Merge — Six File Claims Released, RC7 and RELEASE_PUBLISHER Claims Updated\n22402 11:08p ○ RC7 Merge Commit 431cb19 Passes Source Gates — All Components at 1.0.0-rc.7\n22404 \" ○ Release Workflow Confirmed — Triggered by v* Tag Push, RC Tags Auto-Publish as Prerelease\n22406 \" ○ Release Workflow Stable Tag Behavior — Draft=true for Non-RC Tags, Requires Manual Publish\n22408 11:10p ○ Post-Merge Main CodeQL Run 40243331241 Completed Successfully on 431cb19\n22412 11:25p ○ Post-Merge Main CI — Both Test-Matrix Jobs Passed, linux-x86_64 Job Started on 431cb19\n22434 11:39p ○ Post-Merge Main CI Run 40243331324 — npm Test Passed, Now Running package-linux.sh for v1.0.0-rc.7\n22435 11:41p ○ Post-Merge Main CI — Second package-linux.sh Invocation for Reproducibility Check\n22436 11:43p ○ Post-Merge Main CI Run 40243331324 Completed Successfully on 431cb19\n22437 \" ○ RC7 Release Pre-Tag Gate Check Passed — All Conditions Green\n22438 \" ✓ RC7 Release Tag v1.0.0-rc.7 Pushed to GitHub\n22439 \" ○ RC7 Release Workflow Triggered — Release Not Yet Published\n22440 \" ✓ RC7 Claims Updated — Signed Tag Pushed, Release Workflow Active\n22441 11:44p ○ RC7 Release Workflow 40246054889 — Package Job Installing Rust Toolchain\n22442 \" ○ RC7 Release Workflow — Package Job Running Rust Tests for core/Cargo.tom…104 tokens truncated…sting Build Provenance\n22447 \" ✓ RC7 GitHub Release v1.0.0-rc.7 Published — Full Artifact Set Live\n22448 12:08a ○ RC7 Artifact Download — SHA256SUMS References compatibility.json Not Downloaded\n22449 \" ○ RC7 Artifact SHA256SUMS Fully Verified — All Downloads Match Published Digests\n22450 \" ○ gh attestation verify Fails When HOME Overridden — Auth Token Not Found\n22451 12:09a ○ RC7 Build Provenance Attestation Exists for Release Tarball\n22452 \" ○ GitHub Attestations API Returns bundle_url Pointer, Not Bundle Content\n22453 \" ○ RC7 Attestation Bundle Verification Blocked — Binary Format and SHA256SUMS 404\n22454 12:10a ○ RC7 Attestation Bundle is Snappy-Compressed JSON, Not Raw Protobuf\n22455 \" ○ RC7 Attestation Bundle is Sigsto