at the release gate. | Phase 2 §22 | `scripts/security_gates.sh, scripts/audit_rust_deps.py`; cli/test/security_gates.test.ts, make test | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\ndocs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:65:**Reproducibility status: blocked pending clean-account acceptance.** Resource identity is now configurable in the demo adapter and Worker rather than pinned to the recorded account. However, the included protected broker installer is still an operator-specific upgrade bundle: it requires a prior root-owned `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker` installation, a host-specific runtime/manifest, and credential files provisioned outside the repository. Its launcher clears inherited configuration, so the new per-run configuration has not yet been proven through that installed broker. The restricted validator also requires Linux `sudo`, `setpriv`, `node`, and `tsc` with the specific no-capability UID 65534 boundary. The repo does not yet provide a clean judge bootstrap for those components. The commands above can typecheck and deploy the Worker, but they do not establish a complete fresh-account run. Do not treat local synthetic broker tests or offline fixtures as Cloudflare-backed evidence.\ndocs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:27:- `scripts/installer-smoke.sh` now derives its upgrade-test version from the version under test, instead of a fixed `v0.1.0-alpha.2` that would have collided with this release.\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:589:- `SecretsVault` upgraded in place. Legacy token patterns deprecated. All outbound LLM requests immediately route through quarantine before network dispatch.\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:1344:| `cli/src/session.ts` | 104 | Transcript JSON persistence | **EXTEND** | **WP-07** | `SessionData` upgraded to complete atomic `DurableTaskState` envelope (`PERS-001` .. `PERS-004`). |\ndocs/cloudflare/CONTEST_CREDENTIAL_LIFECYCLE_PREQUALIFICATION_2026-10-02.md:104:The old installed tree is retained under `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker-previous-20261002` and `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker-preupgrade-hold` for recovery. A stale prior rollback helper rejected its old tree before mutation because its pinned manifest did not match the installed tree; no deletion occurred. The new installed rollback helper is pinned to the new manifest.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:61:| `evidence/E_distribution.md` | Distribution and doctor | 6 scratch-HOME installs; docker `ubuntu:22.04` (no node, node 12); upgrade and rollback; doctor and repair runs; CI log |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:147:- Automatic GC runs at most daily. The first run after upgrade needs acknowledgement, or `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_MATURITY_FIXES_2026-10-11_REQUEST.md:50:Investigate the npm failure accurately: the shown security script uses `npm audit --audit-level=high`, while npm reports a disallowed `--allow-scripts` option. Determine where that option originates. Separate scanner execution/configuration failure from an actual vulnerability finding. Do not call failures pre-existing without baseline evidence or bypass security checks. Make tests for simulated scanner failures deterministic so an unrelated earlier network/configuration failure does not mask the intended assertion.\ndocs/cloudflare/ARTIFACTS_FORK_ISOLATION_EVIDENCE.md:44:- **OBSERVED:** The temporary Worker `artifacts-fork-exp2` deployed at `2026-10-02T02:03:12.518585Z`, version `0fcc36f8-70a0-49c0-a9d4-5a98a3a70063`, script ID `c519eca1826b4d69bb1dd74f72e09c57`. Its two fixed fork routes discarded create-time token material; its readback route allowed only the baseline and the two fixed experiment repositories. The Worker was deleted after evidence capture; the original Experiment 1 Worker remains deployed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:97:| `egress` | fetch_web, search_web, browser_*, MCP remote tools | refused | ask | ask on the first call per origin per session, then allowed for that origin (DEC-01 option C) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKER_REMEDIATION_2026-10-08.md:300:- **Evidence.** `~/df2/postdog/accept/legacy_upgrade_probe.sh` → `legacy_s2/`: fixture on loopback, fake `HOME`, no\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKER_REMEDIATION_2026-10-08.md:313:- **Not a candidate regression.** The same scenario completes falsely on `fef7cde` as well, without an upgrade. The\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKER_REMEDIATION_2026-10-08.md:332:  - `legacy_upgrade_probe.sh` → `legacy_r1/`: the identical legacy state at the kill now ends **BLOCKED\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_BLOCKER_REMEDIATION_2026-10-08.md:402:- `legacy_upgrade_probe.sh` → `legacy_r1/`: BLOCKED UNVERIFIED.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:89:| Q7 | Ships as a supportable product | identified, reproducible, versioned builds; CI; install/upgrade/rollback; docs that match behaviour; vulnerability process |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:229:REPRODUCED · D2 no CI and no remote, P1 · D3 installation is the dev checkout (no versioned install/upgrade/rollback),\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:302:| 9 | R9, R11 product delivery, polish (§7.3), O1–O3 | 0 | install/upgrade/rollback test; independent visual acceptance re-run on the release build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:29:| CON-005 | S2 | The committed bundle fails its own checksum on `demo-transport.mjs`, and the installer is upgrade-only. | RUNTIME |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:574:| **SCAN-004** | No known applicable HIGH or CRITICAL security vulnerability may survive in a supported release or deployment artifact. Documentation of a known High/Critical vulnerability does NOT constitute remediation; remediation, upgrade, or component removal is required. | Any release artifact containing an unresolved High or Critical CVE MUST be rejected at the release gate. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:55:   - A future-schema file gives \"created by a newer Nexus (schema N); upgrade\".\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:76:- The first automatic GC after upgrade is preceded by a one-time notice with the dry-run size. It runs only after the user acknowledges it, or with `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:85:| ACC-PER-04 | A truncated session JSON gives an explicit corrupt message and a quarantined file. A `schemaVersion: 99` file gives the upgrade message. An ambiguous prefix is refused. |\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:655:- **High/Critical Zero Tolerance:** No supported release artifact may contain an unresolved applicable High or Critical vulnerability. Documentation is not remediation; remediation, upgrade, or component elimination is required.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:9:Nexus has substantial engineering foundations: typed turn outcomes, durable task and verification state, provider recovery, credential-origin controls, a purpose-built security gate, and extensive test/evidence reporting in recent reviews. The remaining maturity work is less about adding another headline feature and more about proving the complete shipped product is safe, supportable, reproducible, and operable across real upgrades and failures.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:27:**Maturity gap:** Reproducible release builds, artifact provenance/signing, SBOM completeness/schema validation, installation/upgrade/uninstall tests, and a supported platform matrix are not established by the inspected evidence. Avoid overstating package contents or security properties.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:29:**Acceptance evidence:** clean-room build from a tagged source revision; deterministic or explained build metadata; generated SBOM validated by an independent CycloneDX validator and compared with resolved lockfiles; signed checksums/provenance; install/upgrade/rollback tests on each supported platform; documentation traced to shipped behavior.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:51:**Maturity gap:** Add opt-in, privacy-preserving operational diagnostics and a support bundle that can be inspected locally and redacted. Define reliability targets and measure them without collecting source code or secrets. Provide actionable diagnosis for damaged state, missing native binaries, provider outage, and failed upgrades.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:55:### P2 — Product lifecycle: installation, upgrades, configuration, and recovery UX\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:59:**Maturity gap:** Prove the canonical installation path end to end, including fresh install, PATH resolution, native Rust binary selection, configuration precedence, upgrade with existing sessions/state, downgrade/rollback, and uninstall. Document supported environments and configuration precedence in one authoritative place.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:61:**Acceptance evidence:** install tests against produced archives/packages rather than the source checkout; clean HOME and upgrade fixtures; CLI smoke tests from every documented entry point; explicit compatibility and rollback instructions.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:204:| REQ-REL-115 | Scope addition | CLI (`nexus upgrade`) and TUI (`/upgrade`) compare installed version with releases and safely upgrade to latest stable or pinned version. | user maintenance / lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/slash/session_commands.ts` | TEST (ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06; test:cli/test/upgrade.test.ts::\"successfully performs an end-to-end upgrade with atomic symlink swap and verification\", test:cli/test/upgrade_cli.test.ts::\"returns exit code 1 when update is available in --check mode\", test:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts::\"exercises deliberate approval interaction when executing /upgrade in TUI\") | tested | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06 | **B** | REL-14 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:24:5. **Durable Candidate Identity & Milestone Recovery:** Boolean flags (`verifiedWorktreeCompletion`) are replaced with cryptographic candidate identity receipts covering tracked and relevant untracked candidate state (`CAND-001` .. `CAND-004`), and transcript-only session JSON files are upgraded to durable task recovery envelopes providing durable milestone task recovery with interrupted-state detection (`PERS-001` .. `PERS-004`) without overclaiming transparent resumption of in-flight operations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:72:| REQ-REL-11 | D3/R11 | Versioned install, upgrade, rollback; LICENSE/SECURITY/CHANGELOG | TOP_TIER D3/D4 | install.sh + GitHub prereleases v0.1.0-alpha.1/.2 with SHA256SUMS; LICENSE present; **no SECURITY.md, no CHANGELOG, no rollback procedure, no signing/provenance** | N |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/own.md:34:### D3 Installation is the development checkout; no versioned install, upgrade or rollback\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/own.md:37:- Impact: upgrade = git pull + rebuild in the tree that is also being developed; rollback = git checkout + rebuild; a half-finished build or a test run that rebuilds artefacts changes the live runtime.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:23:| **8. Product delivery** | Install script (`releases.openai.com`, GitHub fallback), npm, Homebrew cask, GitHub binaries; macOS arm64/x86_64, Linux x86_64/arm64 (musl), Windows; Apache-2.0; signed PowerShell installer (0.162.0); near-daily releases (0.162.0 Oct 8, 0.162.1 Oct 9, alphas Oct 9-10); security via Bugcrowd [CX-REPO][CX-REL][CX-SEC]. | Native installer with background auto-update; Homebrew stable (≈1 week behind) / latest casks; WinGet; apt/dnf/apk; npm deprecated; macOS/Linux/WSL/Windows; releases 2.1.294-2.1.296 within Oct 8-9; security via HackerOne; license file not read [CC-OV][CC-REPO][CC-CHG][CC-SEC]. | Install script, npm/bun/pnpm/yarn, Homebrew tap, Arch, Chocolatey, Scoop, Docker; macOS/Linux/Windows (WSL recommended); MIT; v1.19.0 (2026-10-11) moves to manual `/update` and offers `opencode upgrade --major` to OpenCode 2; SECURITY.md present [OC-INTRO][OC-REL][OC-REPO]. | Desktop (macOS/Linux/Windows), CLI install script (sh/ps1), Docker build guide; Apache-2.0; v1.54.0 (2026-10-08) [GS-REPO][GS-REL]. | PyPI `aider-chat` 0.86.2 (2026-02-12), Apache-2.0, Python 3.10-3.12; last GitHub release v0.86.0 (Aug 2025) - slow cadence [AI-PYPI][AI-REL]. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:160:- **OpenCode:** docs at opencode.ai/docs may describe 1.x while v1.19.0 offers an upgrade to \"OpenCode 2\"; 2.x behaviour\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:143:| R-PER-4 | Corrupt and future-schema sessions are reported, not shown as \"not found\". Resume id matching is unambiguous. | failure/compat | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Truncated JSON gives an explicit corrupt message. A schemaVersion 2 file gives an \"upgrade Nexus\" message. An ambiguous prefix is refused. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:79:| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20 and Node 22. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:267:## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:279:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:280:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:281:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:53:- **Distribution.** A one-line non-root installer with SHA-256 verification, version pinning, upgrade and rollback by re-running, manual uninstall that keeps user data, and Linux x86-64 / glibc ≥ 2.35 / Node ≥ 20 only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:360:  - A safe non-root installer with working upgrade and rollback.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:99:# upgrade/rollback in $S/h4: alpha.1 → alpha.2 → alpha.1 : symlink swaps correctly each time; both version dirs retained\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:129:  - Installer smoke covers install, reinstall, upgrade, bad checksum and conflict.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:82:| CON-005 | S2 (contest) | Broker install | trusted-broker-bundle/BUNDLE.sha256:11; trusted-object-manifest.json:113-121; install.sh:52-60,92 | RUNTIME: `sha256sum -c BUNDLE.sha256` gives `./broker/demo-transport.mjs: FAILED` (actual 0ad7c7da…, recorded 3238d2e9…). install.sh:92 runs `sha256sum --check` under `set -e`, so **the committed bundle cannot be installed**; it fails closed. The installer also *requires* a prior install at /opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker with a pinned prior manifest (:5-7,52-60). There is no fresh-install path. | The parameterized transport has never been reviewed or hashed into the trust root. The \"upgrade-only\" installer cannot bootstrap a clean host. | Re-hash after review. Add a fresh-install mode. |\n## main...origin/main [behind 1118]\n M AGENTS.md\n M cli/dist/agent.js\n M cli/dist/core/state.js\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\n M core/tests/adversarial_path_traversal.rs\nA  docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nA  docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nA  scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n?? cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts\n?? docs/enhancement-opportunities.md\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/README.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS\n?? docs/v1.0.0/evidence/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/plans/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/specs/\n?? jsf/\n?? nexus-continuity-validation/\n?? nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json\n?? nexus-session-session_20261023_134635_z1dnlfek.json\n/home/mike/nexus-code\nworktree /home/mike/nexus-code\nHE