{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:48:54.990Z","ordinal":387209,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17840-b5b4-7d21-b70b-23d081f0129e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b01fcee3-339d-4b0e-98c8-bc21d0ddb180","process_id":"71890","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show v1.0.0-rc.8:cli/src/upgrade.ts | sed -n '645,685p'; git show v1.0.0-rc.8:install.sh | sed -n '1,220p'; git show -s --format='RC8 tag=%H commit=%cI' v1.0.0-rc.8; git show -s --format='RC7 tag=%H commit=%cI' v1.0.0-rc.7; rg -n \"versioned|install.sh|nexus upgrade\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show v1.0.0-rc.8:cli/src/upgrade.ts | sed -n '645,685p'; git show v1.0.0-rc.8:install.sh | sed -n '1,220p'; git show -s --format='RC8 tag=%H commit=%cI' v1.0.0-rc.8; git show -s --format='RC7 tag=%H commit=%cI' v1.0.0-rc.7; rg -n \"versioned|install.sh|nexus upgrade\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md | head -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"          return true;\n        }\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  // Localhost allowed for local mock testing\n  if (hostname === \"127.0.0.1\" || hostname === \"localhost\") {\n    return parsed.protocol === \"http:\" || parsed.protocol === \"https:\";\n  }\n\n  // GitHub allowed domains - must be HTTPS\n  if (parsed.protocol !== \"https:\") {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  if (hostname === \"github.com\") {\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(`/${CANONICAL_REPO}/releases/download/`);\n  }\n\n  if (hostname === \"objects.githubusercontent.com\") {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  // GitHub now redirects release downloads to its signed release-assets host.\n  // Restrict the path to release objects; never allow this host as a generic CDN.\n  if (hostname === \"release-assets.githubusercontent.com\") {\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(\"/github-production-release-asset/\");\n  }\n\n  return false;\n}\n\n/** Release redirects can contain short-lived signed query parameters; diagnostics expose only the origin. */\nfunction safeDownloadOrigin(urlString: string): string {\n  try {\n    return new URL(urlString).origin;\n  } catch {\n    return \"invalid URL\";\n  }\n}\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nVERIFY_ATTESTATION=${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}\ncase \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" in\n  auto|0|1) ;;\n  *) fail \"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION must be auto (verify when a trusted GitHub CLI is present), 1 (require verification) or 0 (skip verification).\" ;;\nesac\nTRUSTED_GH=\nif [ -x /usr/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/bin/gh\nelif [ -x /usr/local/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/local/bin/gh\nfi\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ] && [ -z \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  fail \"provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\"\nfi\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  if \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n     \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n  elif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n  else\n    printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: %s could not verify the attestation (it may need gh auth login); the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' \"$TRUSTED_GH\" >&2\n  fi\nelif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"auto\" ]; then\n  printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: no trusted GitHub CLI at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' >&2\nfi\n\nVERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"\nBIN_DIR=\"$PREFIX/bin\"\nLINK=\"$BIN_DIR/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus\" \"$BIN_DIR\"\nif [ -e \"$LINK\" ] && [ ! -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  fail \"$LINK exists and is not a symlink; left it unchanged.\"\nfi\nif [ -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  OLD=$(readlink \"$LINK\")\n  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nfi\n\nFORCE=${NEXUS_FORCE:-0}\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\nconst record = {\n  formatVersion: 1,\n  method: \"installer\",\n  product: \"nexus-code\",\n  version,\n  ...(metadata?.revision ? { revision: metadata.revision } : {}),\n  ...(metadata?.builtAt ? { builtAt: metadata.builtAt } : {}),\n  prefix,\n  installedPath,\n  binPath,\n  managed: true,\n  archive,\n  archiveSha256,\n};\nfs.writeFileSync(output, `${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`, { mode: 0o644 });\nfs.chmodSync(output, 0o644);\nNODE\nNEXT=\"$BIN_DIR/.nexus-link.$$\"\nln -s \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" \"$NEXT\"\nmv -f \"$NEXT\" \"$LINK\"\nprintf 'Installed Nexus Code %s in %s\\n' \"$VERSION\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\ncase \":$PATH:\" in *\":$BIN_DIR:\"*) ;; *) printf 'Add this to your shell profile if needed: export PATH=\"%s:$PATH\"\\n' \"$BIN_DIR\" ;; esac\n\"$LINK\" --version\ntag v1.0.0-rc.8\nTagger: Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\n\nNexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8\n-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\nOHm1+v73HA==\n=+jid\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\nRC8 tag=bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752 commit=2026-10-26T02:19:59-04:00\ntag v1.0.0-rc.7\nTagger: Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\n\nNexus Code v1.0.0-rc.7\n-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\n5Vuneby6dQ==\n=dv9R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\nRC7 tag=431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1 commit=2026-10-25T19:07:32-04:00\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:9:| install.sh | full read + RUNTIME (6 install runs, scratch HOMEs, + docker ubuntu:22.04) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:68:| REL-10 | S3 | installer, reinstall/repair | install.sh:48-49 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. When the version dir already exists, the verified archive is discarded and the existing tree is reused after checking only 3 executables + VERSION. A corrupted or partially edited install (e.g. deleted dist files) cannot be repaired by re-running the installer. Versions accumulate forever with no prune (two versions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:88:env -i HOME=$S/h1 PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=$S bash -c 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2 sh'\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:123:- **Upgrade and rollback work** by re-running the installer with the tag (RUNTIME). Versioned dirs make rollback instant.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:132:- **Doctor is well built.** It runs with no config, no model and no session. It has a versioned JSON schema and distinct exit codes. Redaction held for env, flag, URL userinfo and query secrets. Repairs are narrow (3 kinds), confirmation-gated (non-TTY refuses without `--yes`), idempotent and backed up. They use verified chmod/mkdir helpers (safe_fs `chmodVerified` with identity expectation).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:279:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:280:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:281:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:320:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":32564}},"started_at_ms":1793018934989,"completed_at_ms":1793018934990}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:48:55.991Z","ordinal":387210,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17841-bab7-7120-8b93-e1dcf08570c7","call_id":"call_b06cd5df46244da8bc27d822302690f6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"          return true;\n        }\n      }\n    } catch {}\n  }\n\n  // Localhost allowed for local mock testing\n  if (hostname === \"127.0.0.1\" || hostname === \"localhost\") {\n    return parsed.protocol === \"http:\" || parsed.protocol === \"https:\";\n  }\n\n  // GitHub allowed domains - must be HTTPS\n  if (parsed.protocol !== \"https:\") {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  if (hostname === \"github.com\") {\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(`/${CANONICAL_REPO}/releases/download/`);\n  }\n\n  if (hostname === \"objects.githubusercontent.com\") {\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  // GitHub now redirects release downloads to its signed release-assets host.\n  // Restrict the path to release objects; never allow this host as a generic CDN.\n  if (hostname === \"release-assets.githubusercontent.com\") {\n    return parsed.pathname.startsWith(\"/github-production-release-asset/\");\n  }\n\n  return false;\n}\n\n/** Release redirects can contain short-lived signed query parameters; diagnostics expose only the origin. */\nfunction safeDownloadOrigin(urlString: string): string {\n  try {\n    return new URL(urlString).origin;\n  } catch {\n    return \"invalid URL\";\n  }\n}\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nVERIFY_ATTESTATION=${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}\ncase \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" in\n  auto|0|1) ;;\n  *) fail \"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION must be auto (verify when a trusted GitHub CLI is present), 1 (require verification) or 0 (skip verification).\" ;;\nesac\nTRUSTED_GH=\nif [ -x /usr/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/bin/gh\nelif [ -x /usr/local/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/local/bin/gh\nfi\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ] && [ -z \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  fail \"provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\"\nfi\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  if \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n     \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n  elif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n  else\n    printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: %s could not verify the attestation (it may need gh auth login); the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' \"$TRUSTED_GH\" >&2\n  fi\nelif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"auto\" ]; then\n  printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: no trusted GitHub CLI at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' >&2\nfi\n\nVERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"\nBIN_DIR=\"$PREFIX/bin\"\nLINK=\"$BIN_DIR/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus\" \"$BIN_DIR\"\nif [ -e \"$LINK\" ] && [ ! -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  fail \"$LINK exists and is not a symlink; left it unchanged.\"\nfi\nif [ -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  OLD=$(readlink \"$LINK\")\n  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nfi\n\nFORCE=${NEXUS_FORCE:-0}\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\nconst record = {\n  formatVersion: 1,\n  method: \"installer\",\n  product: \"nexus-code\",\n  version,\n  ...(metadata?.revision ? { revision: metadata.revision } : {}),\n  ...(metadata?.builtAt ? { builtAt: metadata.builtAt } : {}),\n  prefix,\n  installedPath,\n  binPath,\n  managed: true,\n  archive,\n  archiveSha256,\n};\nfs.writeFileSync(output, `${JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)}\\n`, { mode: 0o644 });\nfs.chmodSync(output, 0o644);\nNODE\nNEXT=\"$BIN_DIR/.nexus-link.$$\"\nln -s \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" \"$NEXT\"\nmv -f \"$NEXT\" \"$LINK\"\nprintf 'Installed Nexus Code %s in %s\\n' \"$VERSION\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\ncase \":$PATH:\" in *\":$BIN_DIR:\"*) ;; *) printf 'Add this to your shell profile if needed: export PATH=\"%s:$PATH\"\\n' \"$BIN_DIR\" ;; esac\n\"$LINK\" --version\ntag v1.0.0-rc.8\nTagger: Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\n\nNexus Code v1.0.0-rc.8\n-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\nOHm1+v73HA==\n=+jid\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\nRC8 tag=bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752 commit=2026-10-26T02:19:59-04:00\ntag v1.0.0-rc.7\nTagger: Mike Holownych <mike@holownych.com>\n\nNexus Code v1.0.0-rc.7\n-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\nREDACTED\n5Vuneby6dQ==\n=dv9R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\nRC7 tag=431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1 commit=2026-10-25T19:07:32-04:00\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:9:| install.sh | full read + RUNTIME (6 install runs, scratch HOMEs, + docker ubuntu:22.04) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:68:| REL-10 | S3 | installer, reinstall/repair | install.sh:48-49 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. When the version dir already exists, the verified archive is discarded and the existing tree is reused after checking only 3 executables + VERSION. A corrupted or partially edited install (e.g. deleted dist files) cannot be repaired by re-running the installer. Versions accumulate forever with no prune (two versions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:88:env -i HOME=$S/h1 PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=$S bash -c 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2 sh'\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:123:- **Upgrade and rollback work** by re-running the installer with the tag (RUNTIME). Versioned dirs make rollback instant.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:132:- **Doctor is well built.** It runs with no config, no model and no session. It has a versioned JSON schema and distinct exit codes. Redaction held for env, flag, URL userinfo and query secrets. Repairs are narrow (3 kinds), confirmation-gated (non-TTY refuses without `--yes`), idempotent and backed up. They use verified chmod/mkdir helpers (safe_fs `chmodVerified` with identity expectation).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:279:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:280:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:281:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:320:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17840-b5b4-7d21-b70b-23d081f0129e","create_time":1793018935.9913836}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
