{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:51:29.516Z","ordinal":387335,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17842-5b3f-79c2-b89a-cb68a82856bc","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2671f410-de40-4905-8aba-5e458ed40142","process_id":"57069","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 5 '5\\.3|terminal matrix|xterm|kitty|GNOME Terminal|VS Code|80×24|40×14|200×60'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '120,190p'; git show-ref --verify refs/remotes/origin/main >/dev/null; git show -s --format='%H %s' origin/main"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 5 '5\\.3|terminal matrix|xterm|kitty|GNOME Terminal|VS Code|80×24|40×14|200×60'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '120,190p'; git show-ref --verify refs/remotes/origin/main >/dev/null; git show -s --format='%H %s' origin/main"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n47-| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n55-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n56-### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n--\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n--\n106-These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110-| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n125-### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n126-\n--\n178-These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n179-\n180-| Scenario | Pass condition |\n181-|---|---|\n182-| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n183:| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n184-| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n185-| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n186-| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n193-\n194-For each terminal × size, check:\n195-\n196-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n197-2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n7f52ed1b76e2fa69dee1416d1b13f1e1263ff52d Merge pull request #252 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-discovered-verifier-baseline\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":31600}},"started_at_ms":1793019089516,"completed_at_ms":1793019089516}}
