{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:55:07.087Z","ordinal":387466,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17842-5b3f-79c2-b89a-cb68a82856bc","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf4da8afa081a0b7ccb3749b0e47d5","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**RC8 upgrade status:** The updater fix is present in the published RC8 Linux archive, and I verified the archive against GitHub’s checksum file. On mike-dev, Nexus now reports `1.0.0-rc.8`; its installed provenance digest matches that archive: `bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`.\n\nCorrection: my first check on Ubuntu only looked for `nexus` on `PATH`. The desktop does have a versioned installation, with RC7 active. All five required terminal apps are installed, and a Wayland session is active.\n\nPR #254 remains open at `24774a1136775a9069981a5d8d9b763d8fa09253`. Its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, CodeQL, and independent review checks pass; the Linux packaging job is still running its CLI tests. I’ll wait for that exact-head check before integration.\n\nThe next terminal matrix must use the next exact candidate, not RC7 or RC8. Held-out custody is still unconfirmed, so acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793019304734,"completed_at_ms":1793019307087}}
