{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:12:18.365Z","ordinal":387798,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-21623855-20c2-4434-9663-e8c319880481","process_id":"82884","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:.github/workflows/release.yml | sed -n '1,180p'; git show origin/main:scripts/sync-version.mjs | sed -n '1,100p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | sed -n '1,120p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:.github/workflows/release.yml | sed -n '1,180p'; git show origin/main:scripts/sync-version.mjs | sed -n '1,100p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | sed -n '1,120p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"name: Release\n\non:\n  push:\n    tags: [\"v*.*.*\"]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n  id-token: write\n  attestations: write\n\njobs:\n  package:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-22.04\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      id-token: write\n      attestations: write\n    env:\n      NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE: rust:1.95.0-bookworm@sha256:4c2fd73ef19c5ef9d54bee03b06b2839a392604fbfcd578ed948b71b37c1d7fb\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - run: sudo apt-get update\n      - run: sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n      - name: Mount a dedicated capped tmpfs for evaluator resource fixtures\n        run: |\n          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-release\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$root\"\n          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-release \"$root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n          runtime_root=/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$runtime_root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@b725eda525362e7cf34af9a7243cac1e3f01a7ec # stable\n      - name: Install cargo tools (audit, deny, about, cyclonedx)\n        run: |\n          CARGO_HOME=\"${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}\"\n          export CARGO_HOME\n          mkdir -p \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\"\n          echo \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n          export PATH=\"$CARGO_HOME/bin:$PATH\"\n          cargo install cargo-audit --locked --version 0.22.2\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny/releases/download/0.20.2/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-deny\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about/releases/download/0.9.2/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-about\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-rust-cargo/releases/download/cargo-cyclonedx-0.5.9/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz | tar -xJ -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-cyclonedx\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-cli/releases/download/v0.33.1/cyclonedx-linux-x64 -o \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n          chmod +x \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22.22.1\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: cli/package-lock.json\n      - name: Require the pinned release Node and npm versions\n        run: |\n          test \"$(node --version)\" = \"v22.22.1\"\n          test \"$(npm --version)\" = \"10.9.4\"\n      - name: Install selected Node runtime for isolated evaluation commands\n        run: |\n          node_runtime=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v node)\")\"\n          npm_cli=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v npm)\")\"\n          npm_root=\"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$npm_cli\")\")\"\n          case \"$npm_root\" in */lib/node_modules/npm) ;; *) echo \"Unexpected setup-node npm package path\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac\n          test -f \"$npm_root/package.json\"\n          sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \"$node_runtime\" /usr/bin/node\n          sudo install -d -o root -g root -m 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo cp -a \"$npm_root/.\" /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/\n          sudo chown -hR root:root /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo chmod 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js\n          sudo ln -sfn /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js /usr/bin/npm\n          test \"$(/usr/bin/node --version)\" = \"$(node --version)\"\n          test \"$(env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/npm --version)\" = \"$(npm --version)\"\n      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n        run: |\n          git fetch origin main --no-tags\n          git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$GITHUB_SHA\" origin/main\n          test \"${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}\" = \"$(node -p 'require(\"./package.json\").version')\"\n          node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\"\n          test -f \"docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" || { echo \"Missing docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" >&2; exit 1; }\n      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n        if: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\n        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n        run: |\n          rc=\"$(git tag --points-at \"$GITHUB_SHA^\" | grep -E \"^${GITHUB_REF_NAME//./\\\\.}-rc\\.[0-9]+$\" | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)\"\n          test -n \"$rc\" || { echo \"the parent of $GITHUB_REF_NAME is not a ${GITHUB_REF_NAME}-rc.N tag\" >&2; exit 1; }\n          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n      - run: npm ci --prefix cli\n      - run: npm --prefix cli run build\n      - run: cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\n      - run: cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n      - run: npm --prefix cli test\n      - run: bash scripts/security_gates.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist\"\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/SHA256SUMS\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/SHA256SUMS\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\"\n      - run: cyclonedx validate --input-file \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" --fail-on-errors\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/sbom.cdx.json\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/sbom.cdx.json\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check/install.sh\"\n      - run: bash scripts/smoke-package.sh \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - run: bash scripts/installer-smoke.sh \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/install.sh\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_REF_NAME.tar.gz\"\n      - name: Attest build provenance\n        uses: actions/attest-build-provenance@92c65d2898f1f53cfdc910b962cecff86e7f8fcc # v1\n        with:\n          subject-path: |\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-${{ github.ref_name }}.tar.gz\n            ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/SHA256SUMS\n      # RC tags (vX.Y.Z-rc.N) publish a prerelease: the workflow-produced RC is the qualification candidate\n      # (ACCEPTANCE §1.1 stage 2). Stable tags only build an unpublished draft (stage 5); it is published by hand with\n      # `gh release edit <tag> --draft=false` after the stable artifact checks and the signed acceptance disposition.\n      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@3bb12739c298aeb8a4eeaf626c5b8d85266b0e65 # v2\n        with:\n          files: ${{ runner.temp }}/dist/*\n          body_path: docs/releases/${{ github.ref_name }}.md\n          prerelease: ${{ contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n          draft: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n// The root package.json version is the single source of truth (REQ-REL-103). This writes it into cli/package.json,\n// cli/package-lock.json, core/Cargo.toml and core/Cargo.lock; `--check` only reports drift and exits 1 when any file\n// disagrees (run in CI and the release workflow). `--tag vX.Y.Z` additionally requires the tag to match.\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\n\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst check = args.includes(\"--check\");\nconst tagIndex = args.indexOf(\"--tag\");\nconst tag = tagIndex >= 0 ? args[tagIndex + 1] : undefined;\n\nconst version = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\")).version;\nif (!/^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$/.test(version)) throw new Error(`package.json version '${version}' is not SemVer`);\n\nconst drift = [];\nconst update = (rel, transform) => {\n  const file = path.join(root, rel);\n  const before = fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\");\n  const after = transform(before);\n  if (after === before) return;\n  drift.push(rel);\n  if (!check) fs.writeFileSync(file, after);\n};\n\nconst jsonVersion = (text, paths) => {\n  const data = JSON.parse(text);\n  for (const p of paths) {\n    let node = data;\n    for (const key of p.slice(0, -1)) node = node?.[key];\n    if (node && typeof node === \"object\" && p[p.length - 1] in node) node[p[p.length - 1]] = version;\n  }\n  return JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + \"\\n\";\n};\n\nupdate(\"cli/package.json\", (t) => jsonVersion(t, [[\"version\"]]));\nupdate(\"cli/package-lock.json\", (t) => jsonVersion(t, [[\"version\"], [\"packages\", \"\", \"version\"]]));\nupdate(\"core/Cargo.toml\", (t) => t.replace(/^(\\[package\\][^[]*?\\nversion = )\"[^\"]*\"/s, `$1\"${version}\"`));\nupdate(\"core/Cargo.lock\", (t) => t.replace(/(\\[\\[package\\]\\]\\nname = \"harness-core\"\\nversion = )\"[^\"]*\"/, `$1\"${version}\"`));\n\nif (tag !== undefined && tag !== `v${version}`) {\n  console.error(`tag ${tag} does not match package.json version ${version}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\nif (drift.length) {\n  console.error(`${check ? \"version drift\" : \"updated to \" + version}: ${drift.join(\", \")}`);\n  if (check) process.exit(1);\n} else {\n  console.log(`all components at ${version}`);\n}\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":31090}},"started_at_ms":1793020338365,"completed_at_ms":1793020338365}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:12:19.620Z","ordinal":387799,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17857-25a4-7a51-849b-d68bad954209","call_id":"call_7affd68ede3f4fbcb15fc67ce7b87f17","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4101)\nTotal output lines: 236\n\nname: Release\n\non:\n  push:\n    tags: [\"v*.*.*\"]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n  id-token: write\n  attestations: write\n\njobs:\n  package:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-22.04\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      id-token: write\n      attestations: write\n    env:\n      NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE: rust:1.95.0-bookworm@sha256:4c2fd73ef19c5ef9d54bee03b06b2839a392604fbfcd578ed948b71b37c1d7fb\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n      - run: sudo apt-get update\n      - run: sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n      - name: Mount a dedicated capped tmpfs for evaluator resource fixtures\n        run: |\n          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-release\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$root\"\n          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-release \"$root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n          runtime_root=/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$runtime_root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@b725eda525362e7cf34af9a7243cac1e3f01a7ec # stable\n      - name: Install cargo tools (audit, deny, about, cyclonedx)\n        run: |\n          CARGO_HOME=\"${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}\"\n          export CARGO_HOME\n          mkdir -p \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\"\n          echo \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n          export PATH=\"$CARGO_HOME/bin:$PATH\"\n          cargo install cargo-audit --locked --version 0.22.2\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny/releases/download/0.20.2/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-deny-0.20.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-deny\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about/releases/download/0.9.2/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz | tar -xz -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-about-0.9.2-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-about\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-rust-cargo/releases/download/cargo-cyclonedx-0.5.9/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz | tar -xJ -C \"$RUNNER_TEMP\"\n          mv \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cargo-cyclonedx-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/cargo-cyclonedx\" \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/\"\n          curl -fsSL https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-cli/releases/download/v0.33.1/cyclonedx-linux-x64 -o \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n          chmod +x \"$CARGO_HOME/bin/cyclonedx\"\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@49933ea5288caeca8642d1e84afbd3f7d6820020 # v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22.22.1\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: cli/package-lock.json\n      - name: Require the pinned release Node and npm versions\n        run: |\n          test \"$(node --version)\" = \"v22.22.1\"\n          test \"$(npm --version)\" = \"10.9.4\"\n      - name: Install selected Node runtime for isolated evaluation commands\n        run: |\n          node_runtime=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v node)\")\"\n          npm_cli=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v npm)\")\"\n          npm_root=\"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$npm_cli\")\")\"\n          case \"$npm_root\" in */lib/node_modules/npm) ;; *) echo \"Unexpected setup-node npm package path\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac\n          test -f \"$npm_root/package.json\"\n          sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 \"$node_runtime\" /usr/bin/node\n          sudo install -d -o root -g root -m 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo cp -a \"$npm_root/.\" /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/\n          sudo chown -hR root:root /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm\n          sudo chmod 0755 /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js\n          sudo ln -sfn /usr/lib/nexus-ci/npm/bin/npm-cli.js /usr/bin/npm\n          test \"$(/usr/bin/node --version)\" = \"$(node --version)\"\n          test \"$(env PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /usr/bin/npm --version)\" = \"$(npm --version)\"\n      - name: Require a version-matched tag on main\n        run: |\n          git fetch origin main --no-tags\n          git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$GITHUB_SHA\" origin/main\n          test \"${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}\" = \"$(node -p 'require(\"./package.json\").version')\"\n          node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\"\n          test -f \"docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" || { echo \"Missing docs/releases/${GITHUB_REF_NAME}.md\" >&2; exit 1; }\n      - name: Require a stable tag to be a version-only commit on its RC\n        if: ${{ !contains(github.ref_name, '-') }}\n        # The checkout has full history and tags (fetch-depth: 0). The checker runs from the RC's own copy so a stable\n        # commit cannot replace it; branch and tag protection remain the control over the workflow file itself.\n        run: |\n          rc=\"$(git tag --points-at \"$GITHUB_SHA^\" | grep -E \"^${GITHUB_REF_NAME//./\\\\.}-rc\\.[0-9]+$\" | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)\"\n          test -n \"$rc\" || { echo \"the parent of $GITHUB_REF_NAME is not a ${GITHUB_REF_NAME}-rc.N tag\" >&2; exit 1; }\n          git show \"$rc:scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\"\n          node \"$RUNNER_TEMP/check-version-only-diff.mjs\" \"$rc\" \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n      - run: npm ci --prefix cli\n      - run: npm --prefix cli run build\n      - run: cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\n      - run: cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\n      - run: npm --prefix cli test\n      - run: bash scripts/security_gates.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist\"\n      - run: bash scripts/package-linux.sh \"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\" \"$RUNNER_TEMP/repro-check\"\n      - run: cmp \"$RUNNER_TEMP/dist/nexus-linux-x86_64-$GITHUB_RE…1101 tokens truncated…I 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9","create_time":1793020339.620565}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
