e,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf4fd44fb081a0b1f41f957d15cb30","order":18993,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1784f-d7d2-7342-836c-17fba48217bf","text":"PR #254’s Linux packaging/reproducibility job has now finished successfully on the exact head. I’m doing the final freshness and mergeability check before integrating it; the separate held-out-custody request still has no custodian response.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf4ff38b9081a0a8ebbb78574c75d8","order":18994,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17850-523b-7be0-900e-6a4b93c03af8","text":"PR #254 is merged as `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`. I’m checking requirements enforcement and version consistency in a fresh detached worktree at that merge commit while its exact-main CI and CodeQL runs execute.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf502dd34c81a0a6289e9c68ca15bd","order":18995,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17851-35f3-7262-be6c-ad699210ee94","text":"The provider-stream slice is integrated as `b73b6ec`. Its exact-head full CI, including the Linux reproducible package and installer smoke, passed; the requirements gate and version check also pass on a clean worktree at the merge commit. Post-merge CI and CodeQL have started on that exact main revision.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf51a9d12c81a08bb02dbf39d15414","order":19002,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17857-0196-78d0-8f69-48fdeb1572db","text":"Post-merge CodeQL is green on `b73b6ec`; both exact-main test matrices are now in the CLI test step. I’ve preserved the existing checkout and am not starting overlapping local suites while CI owns that validation.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf531db31c81a0bc8f8aac599e040f","order":19007,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1785c-af54-70a1-b7ca-04305b89900c","text":"The release claim set still has a root-owned `CLOUD` reservation scoped to RC8. RC8 is now superseded, and its live task attempt is not valid acceptance evidence, so I’m releasing that reservation with the outcome recorded; I’ll reclaim it for the exact next RC instead of letting an obsolete lane remain held.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf55f06de481a0ae9fa66618d17eac","order":19016,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17867-b606-75c3-8566-0d62e035d138","text":"I also confirmed the local setup gap you reported: the model picker exposes the appliance endpoint, but the connect flow only configures cloud providers; local endpoints currently require manual config or CLI flags. I’m assigning a separate, claimed implementation slice for local endpoint setup while the post-merge CI continues.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf5649e66c81a08da6c2cba28b57ad","order":19021,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17869-1448-7eb2-85ea-5c2c404a414f","text":"The local setup work hit an ownership boundary: two TUI files are claimed by my checkpoint-protection slice. The implementing agent is respecting that claim and has continued mapping the unclaimed backend path. I’m checking whether my TUI claim can be safely released or whether the setup flow needs a different UI boundary.","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":19022,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-7