{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:33:53.717Z","ordinal":388291,"type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_060b64278a9dfb15016adf56bc39fc81a08b1fb1a3fd31b426","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9"},"summary":[{"text":"**Awaiting host identity**","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:33:55.872Z","ordinal":388292,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf56c1aab481a0a161788a764ecb3c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The failure is in the **installed RC6 updater**: it rejects GitHub’s signed download redirect to `release-assets.githubusercontent.com`. RC7’s updater also lacks that allowance, so retrying the RC6 → RC7 upgrade will hit the same block.\n\nThe merged source at `b73b6ec` accepts that host only for GitHub release-asset paths and includes regression tests for the redirect. That supports the diagnosis; it does **not** prove the failed upgrade completed or that the active installation is unchanged.\n\nI couldn’t verify the machine after the failure because SSH reported that `mike-dev`’s host key has changed. I won’t bypass that check. Once the host identity is verified, I can check the backup and installation state and use the approved installer path to move past RC6. The release remains unaccepted and unpublished as stable v1.0.0; post-merge Linux CI is still running."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793021633720,"completed_at_ms":1793021635872}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:33:55.876Z","ordinal":388293,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf56c1aab481a0a161788a764ecb3c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The failure is in the **installed RC6 updater**: it rejects GitHub’s signed download redirect to `release-assets.githubusercontent.com`. RC7’s updater also lacks that allowance, so retrying the RC6 → RC7 upgrade will hit the same block.\n\nThe merged source at `b73b6ec` accepts that host only for GitHub release-asset paths and includes regression tests for the redirect. That supports the diagnosis; it does **not** prove the failed upgrade completed or that the active installation is unchanged.\n\nI couldn’t verify the machine after the failure because SSH reported that `mike-dev`’s host key has changed. I won’t bypass that check. Once the host identity is verified, I can check the backup and installation state and use the approved installer path to move past RC6. The release remains unaccepted and unpublished as stable v1.0.0; post-merge Linux CI is still running.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9","create_time":1793021633.668695,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf56c1aab481a0a161788a764ecb3c","turn_id":"01a17847-ad27-7861-82f3-55336b77bcc9","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1786a-ed24-7760-bf63-55ea70ce782b","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19026}}
