{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:00:25.455Z","ordinal":389073,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1786b-50a4-7ce3-87df-b08e46a14ac4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-69374bc0-dc0d-435d-af51-6572225645c6","process_id":"72147","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'Nexus|RC|upgrade|checkpoint|release' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -30; git status --short --branch; git rev-parse --show-toplevel; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect log -1 --oneline; find \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort | tail -40"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i 'Nexus|RC|upgrade|checkpoint|release' /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | head -30; git status --short --branch; git rev-parse --show-toplevel; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect log -1 --oneline; find \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort | tail -40"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:# Task Group: Nexus Code client release and Cloudflare contest publication\n2:scope: Package the installed Nexus Code Linux client and prepare the distinct Nexus Workers/Artifacts contest submission in `/home/mike/nexus-code`; retain separate readiness dispositions and do not treat CI or offline fixtures as a clean-account proof.\n3:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code; reuse_rule=recheck the exact release revision, downloadable artifact, endpoint configuration, contest rules, Cloudflare account, broker installation, and credentials; this records a 2026-10-23 partial result, not portable release or contest readiness.\n9:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T16-47-30-01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T04:47:40+00:00, thread_id=01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15, contest CI/video/submission material verified; clean-account reproducibility blocked)\n13:- Cloudflare Workers, Artifacts, docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md, 38471712649, ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9, EXPERIMENT_AUTH, protected broker, /opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker, clean-clone, judge-owned account, e05006b6-5dce-47d1-b2ff-15995e41a886\n15:## Task 2: Package Nexus Code as a complete Linux client with installer and CI, partial\n19:- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/rollout-2026-10-13T16-47-30-01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-23T04:47:40+00:00, thread_id=01a13629-7b99-7b61-a6e3-88bb4ac1dd15, prerelease/installer evidence exists; representative inference remains unverified)\n23:- NEXUS_HOME, install.sh, scripts/package-linux.sh, scripts/smoke-package.sh, cli/src/tools.ts, cli/src/tui.ts, harness-core, nexus-tui, Node.js 20+, Linux x86-64/glibc, v0.1.0-alpha.1, 38459471967, 39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8\n27:- for Cloudflare contest work, the user required using the existing repository, preserving unrelated history/work, and distinguishing the Nexus Code client from the Cloudflare Workers/Artifacts submission -> do not replace repositories or wholesale-integrate unaccepted candidates. [Task 1]\n29:- when preparing a client deliverable, the user required proving the actual architecture rather than assuming one Rust executable -> include the TypeScript sidecar/CLI, production Node dependencies, `harness-core`, `nexus-tui`, and assets in both packaging and clean-environment verification. [Task 2]\n30:- the user required exact downloadable-artifact and clean-environment verification before declaring readiness -> packaging structure, a release workflow, or a fresh-home install alone is insufficient. [Task 2]\n34:- Contest-specific CI passed at `ce7e58b9ce3f6e4a72f84d205c5319b241ca0aa9` in workflow `38471712649`; it covered demo tests and Worker build/typecheck, not a real Cloudflare account run. The service is the submission; Nexus Code is its client/demo harness. [Task 1]\n35:- Cloudflare contest rules require a 5–10 minute video, public source, run instructions, Workers and Artifacts usage, and an MIT/Apache/BSD license; automated application entry is prohibited. [Task 1]\n36:- Installed-runtime resolution needs `NEXUS_HOME`; source-oriented paths under `core/target` and repository-relative CLI paths are not sufficient after installation. [Task 2]\n37:- The stated support envelope is Linux x86-64/glibc with Node.js 20+; do not claim portability beyond it. The rollout records prerelease `v0.1.0-alpha.1`, release workflow `38459471967`, checksum `39548ab8b6ba4043e930f8a30d99ce6f9f787f68c8c46b1b10a9a2f1ea7e5ec8`, and fresh-home installer verification. [Task 2]\n41:- Symptom: parameterized source, synthetic broker tests, Worker build/typecheck, or public video is called contest-ready. Cause: the installed protected broker launcher clears inherited configuration and depends on a prior root-owned `/opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker`, external credential files, and fixed runtime identity. Fix: keep disposition blocked until a fresh account/resource run verifies candidate refs, work-state, Worker response, and integration output; a safe clean-host broker/credential bootstrap is still needed. [Task 1]\n42:- Symptom: a package looks releasable from structure or installer success. Cause: no endpoint was listening at the default local endpoint, so representative inference was not exercised. Fix: require a configured installed-client inference operation before setting `CLIENT_RELEASE_READY`. [Task 2]\n45:# Task Group: Nexus agent effectiveness: unbounded continuation and evidence-bounded diagnosis\n46:scope: Review failed Nexus agent exports and maintain prompt/regression safeguards for progressing continuation loops, direct diagnostic questions, and timeout claims in `/home/mike/nexus-code`.\n47:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code; reuse_rule=recheck the current agent prompt, test suite, and exact export before attributing a specific failure; the no-cumulative-step-ceiling preference is durable, while the observed run metrics are export-specific.\n53:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T22-57-40-v8Tm-nexus_agent_effectiveness_unbounded_loops_evidence_bounded_d.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/14/rollout-2026-10-14T22-57-40-01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-14T23:14:22+00:00, thread_id=01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0, completed diagnosis with failure evidence)\n57:- Nexus, nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json, CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED, 54582+8192+4096>65536, make test, timeout, truncated output, direct status question, evidence-bounded diagnosis\n63:- rollout_summaries/2026-10-14T22-57-40-v8Tm-nexus_agent_effectiveness_unbounded_loops_evidence_bounded_d.md (cwd=/home/mike/nexus-code, rollout_path=/home/mike/.codex/sessions/2026/10/14/rollout-2026-10-14T22-57-40-01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-14T23:14:22+00:00, thread_id=01a13ca2-bc00-7060-ba3c-76dfba4736c0, focused regressions passed; full `make test` not rerun)\n67:- cli/src/agent.ts, cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts, cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts, maxSteps, continuation, Work left unfinished at the step limit, 310 writes, 311, 11 segments, npx tsx --test\n71:- when the user clarified “There should not be any hard limit on step limit for agent loops” -> treat `maxSteps` as a per-segment checkpoint size; preserve automatic continuation for progressing work unless genuinely blocked, cancelled, stagnant, or explicitly budgeted. [Task 1][Task 2]\n76:- The failed export ended `status=failed` with `CONTEXT_CAPACITY_EXCEEDED` at step 36: `54582+8192+4096>65536`; it had 99 requests, 203 archived records, and 16 findings. This is evidence of context admission exhaustion, not of the speculative test/SSE causes asserted during the run. [Task 1]\n78:- `cli/src/agent.ts` now states that `maxSteps` is per-segment, prioritizes direct status questions, and requires evidence-bounded timeout diagnosis. `cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts` covers these rules; the 310-write continuity regression completed step 311 over 11 segments without a runtime exhaustion notice. [Task 2]\n84:- Symptom: a regression rejects explanatory prompt text containing `step limit`. Cause: it searched a generic phrase rather than the true runtime symptom. Fix: assert absence of `Work left unfinished at the step limit`. [Task 2]\n88:applies_to: cwd=/home/mike/Projects/aihost; reuse_rule=revalidate model/release/inventory/live gateway state and preserve the shared worktree before reuse; the selections and validation results are release-specific, and 22 generic validator checks plus listed vLLM/cancellation limits remain unproven.\n108:- Flash-Next Q-TOOLS passed 7/7 synthetic categories and 20/20 Nexus replay points. Q-LONGCTX passed probes from 16K through 59,913 tokens; a 67,335-token input was rejected with HTTP 400 in 0.14s. Both selected models passed production qualification after reboot and rollback restoration. [Task 1]\n## main...origin/main [behind 1124]\n M AGENTS.md\n M cli/dist/agent.js\n M cli/dist/core/state.js\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\n M core/tests/adversarial_path_traversal.rs\nA  docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nA  docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nA  scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n?? cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts\n?? docs/enhancement-opportunities.md\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md\n?? doc