{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:04:17.183Z","ordinal":389165,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17886-b79f-77d2-bff5-90b7ced0d6b9","call_id":"call_8caa94feb1fa4dc79dce5261e8c5257d","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**REQUEST_CHANGES** for `c3d50a1b12de75f619ea4eae403461e5d7db2c64` against `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421` (diff SHA-256 `a0977a671f6c2889ba46b6d31a9079e57c9d9157cfe7a2a08b17c30b5109e415`).\\n\\n- **Redirect can disclose inference content:** the local endpoint’s origin is authorized in [provider_connect.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/provider_connect.ts:68), but [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/client.ts:987) rejects redirects only for connections with a `providerId`. The local appliance connection has none, so a custom endpoint can redirect a completion POST, including its body, to another origin. The entered-origin authorization does not authorize that redirect destination. Add redirect refusal for pinned/local endpoints and a regression with a second-origin canary.\\n\\n- **Cancelling model selection leaves mismatched config:** [provider_connect.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/provider_connect.ts:96) persists the endpoint before model selection. [config.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/config.ts:165) retains `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL` when no model is supplied, and [buildConfig](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/config.ts:288) can then pair the new endpoint with the old model. The model picker can be closed at [live_state.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:578). Defer persistence until selection or clear the prior model; add a connect-and-cancel regression with an existing model configured.\\n\\nThe TUI setup is visible, and the key is masked. Existing tests cover successful setup, but not either finding. No tests were run for this review.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af","create_time":1793023457.1838212}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
