{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:20:24.685Z","ordinal":389676,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17895-7aed-7933-a46f-1e929a4b630f","call_id":"call_c9a475c0472b4875bcc33ebcc5a9b3ef","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #256 at head `1198d773ddb8c27fd27e8b6cdc0a3084edb53016` against base `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421` (diff SHA-256 `0becbc1e84740f33d40f5f4302ace84c44a2929e15f2a177399f9fc0892379d8`).\\n\\n- [credentials.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/credentials.ts:78) checks that the store is a regular file and has an object-valued `providers` field, but does not validate the version or credential records. A parseable unsupported-version store is rewritten as v1; a malformed `null` entry for this endpoint is treated as absent and can be lost on rollback. The malformed-store test covers only invalid JSON at [provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:574).\\n- Canceling while endpoint verification is still pending can restore the canceled setup: `provider.cancel` resets the override at [sidecar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/sidecar.ts:215), but `prepareLocalEndpoint` activates it after the awaited model request at [provider_connect.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/provider_connect.ts:97). The cancellation test covers only cancellation after discovery has completed ([provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:622)).\\n\\nRedirect refusal is applied centrally to requests, and the valid prior-credential rollback test checks byte-for-byte preservation. No tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af","create_time":1793024424.6853461}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
