{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:22:29.917Z","ordinal":389775,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17897-641d-7b63-a052-560102b2feb1","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a` against base `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421` (diff SHA-256 `c87acdb9e218d5a894014350495038e3815fa88843bb5bfdda88baf5fc16d683`).\n\nThe store checks now reject unsupported versions and malformed target credentials before writing. In-flight cancellation also prevents a late discovery result from activating setup.\n\nOne issue remains: [provider_connect.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/provider_connect.ts:61) resets the provisional endpoint unconditionally, even when the supplied request ID is unrelated or unknown. Since [sidecar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/sidecar.ts:215) calls this for every provider cancellation, canceling another request can clear a separate local setup. Make reset conditional on matching the local setup request, while preserving an explicit clear for closing its picker; add coverage for both matching and unrelated cancellation."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af","create_time":1793024549.9177883}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19154}}
