:"github.fetch_issue_comments"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a15643-db25-7cb0-b19b-b1f34bd3c2da","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.update_issue_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15691-fa03-7062-973a-b4e3eaf95fd0","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"send_message_to_thread"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156d7-4dfd-7141-94cc-a0e69c18c919","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.mark_pull_request_ready_for_review"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_repo"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf5d596c3881a092dd0d3dedce497b","order":19088,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a17884-ac97-7a93-b03e-263724550e67","text":"That confirms the cause: **RC6 rejects GitHub’s redirect to `release-assets.githubusercontent.com`**, so its upgrade to RC7 fails after the backup. RC8 allows that download host; upgrading from RC6 to RC7 will keep failing.\n\nI haven’t retried on `mike-dev` because its SSH host key changed and still needs trusted verification. The local-provider PR is also moving: its author is addressing the independent review findings and the Node 22/24 CI failure before I push an updated revision.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; this does not establish an accepted RC or completed release.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:27-30|note=[release verification requires proof from the actual installed deliverable]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a1786b-50a4-7ce3-87df-b08e46a14ac4"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf5d78049481a0b3137d31f6132491","order":19089,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17885-1f79-7221-9674-06e8bc65c8de","text":"I’m refreshing the live PR, branch, and CI state now, then I’ll take the next safe integration step if the follow-up is ready. RC6’s redirect diagnosis is settled; the priority is getting the reviewed local-provider fix through exact-head checks.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf5d990a3081a08de41c0ce7848e32","order":19093,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17885-a2ab-7c11-8329-f7f05e0f4bd4","text":"The implementer reports both review issues fixed: local endpoints now reject redirects, and cancelling model discovery leaves the previous endpoint/model/key untouched. Focused CLI tests pass 41/41 and focused Rust tests pass 8/8; the type/build check is still pending because this isolated worktree lacks its TypeScript compiler dependency. I’ve asked them to complete that check, commit locally, and release the claims; I’ll then inspect and push the exact revision for fresh CI and independent review.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf5e4e262081a0ac34c9afc705d15c","order":19104,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17888-64aa-78b0-83b6-bd188ce06028","text":"The updated candidate is now pushed as `0439289`. Its exact-revision CI is running, and independent review confirms the redirect and cancellation fixes. Review found one remaining edge case: if saving the chosen endpoint settings fails after the key was saved, an orphaned credential could remain. I’m sending that back for a targeted failure-path fix before treating this PR as ready.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf5f24fecc81a0960bdb8f1a6d200f","order":19116,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1788b-ace4-7a61-963a-d36efeb930c6","text":"CodeQL has passed for `0439289`. The Node 22/24 jobs are in their full CLI test stage; their earlier build, requirements, Rust test, and release-build steps passed. The atomicity fix is in a new local follow-up and will need fresh exact-head checks, so I’ll keep the current CI result tied specifically to `0439289` and won’t treat it as evidence for the next commit.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf60fdd8f081a086af8638241280ff","order":19140,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17892-e3c8-7bc2-9f69-77aa90bea83c","text":"The fresh review found two more concrete edge cases on `1198d77`: unsupported credential-store versions or invalid existing entries can still be rewritten, and canceling while model discovery is in flight can let a late response restore the canceled endpoint. I’m sending both for fixes and regressions; the `1198d77` CI results will remain historical if the PR advances again.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf620dad7481a0aae74ba55da83ed4","order":19151,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17897-0969-7e30-8d34-c55aba4c4e4c","text":"The latest candidate `c3bb223` is pushed and the new exact-head CI/CodeQL runs are underway. It now covers the four reviewed failure classes: redirect disclosure, cancellation persistence, credential-store rollback, and canceling an in-flight local model lookup. I’ve asked for a fresh independent disposition on this exact commit; nothing has been merged.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf6235684081a0a353256ba886d6c3","order":19155,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17897-a5d5-7573-bca8-bd06ed0aa7a1","text":"The independent review caught a cancellation-scope issue: canceling an unrelated provider request can still clear the local setup. I’m having the implementer make cleanup conditional on the matching local request while preserving an explicit clear when the local model picker itself is closed, with regressions for both paths.","turn_id":"01a17885-133d-7581-bd2d-36a0306191af"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":19157,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes